  ["magicitem.3-rhythm-maker-s-drum.tce2014"]={title="+3 Rhythm-Maker's Drum",subtitle="Item Magico - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile holding this PHB, you gain a +3 bonus to spell attack rolls and to the saving throw DCs of your bard spells.\n\nAs an action, you can play the PHB to regain one use of your Bardic Inspiration feature. This property of the PHB can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.3-rod-of-the-pact-keeper.dmg2014"]={title="+3 Rod of the Pact Keeper",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile holding this rod, you gain a +3 bonus to spell attack rolls and to the saving throw DCs of your warlock spells.\n\nIn addition, you can regain one warlock spell slot as an action while holding the rod. You can't use this property again until you finish a long rest."},
  ["magicitem.3-rod-of-the-pact-keeper.xdmg2024"]={title="+3 Rod of the Pact Keeper",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 301\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile holding this rod, you gain a +3 bonus to spell attack rolls and to the saving throw DCs of your spells.\n\nIn addition, you can regain one spell slot as a XPHB action while holding the rod. You can't use this property again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.3-wand-of-the-war-mage.dmg2014"]={title="+3 Wand of the War Mage",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile you are holding this wand, you gain a +3 bonus to spell attack rolls. In addition, you ignore Cover when making a spell attack."},
  ["magicitem.3-wand-of-the-war-mage.xdmg2024"]={title="+3 Wand of the War Mage",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 322\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile holding this wand, you gain a +3 bonus to spell attack rolls. In addition, you ignore XPHB when making a spell attack roll."},
  ["magicitem.3-wraps-of-unarmed-power.xdmg2024"]={title="+3 Wraps of Unarmed Power",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 325\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile wearing these wraps, you have a +3 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with your Unarmed Strikes. Those strikes deal your choice of Force damage or their normal damage type."},
  ["magicitem.3-wraps-of-unarmed-prowess.bmt2014"]={title="+3 Wraps of Unarmed Prowess",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 69\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile you're wearing these cloth wraps, your unarmed strikes are considered magical for the purpose of overcoming immunity and resistance to nonmagical attacks and damage, and you gain a +3 bonus to the attack and damage rolls of your unarmed strikes."},
  ["species.aarakocra.dmg2014"]={title="Aarakocra",subtitle="Especie - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nDive Attack\n\nIf you are flying and dive at least 30 ft. straight toward a target and then hit it with a melee weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 1d6 damage to the target.\n\nTalons\n\nYou are proficient with your unarmed strikes, which deal 1d4 slashing damage on a hit.\n\nLanguage\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Auran."},
  ["species.aarakocra.eepc2014"]={title="Aarakocra",subtitle="Especie - EEPC - 2014",body="Pagina: 5\n\nAge\n\nAarakocra reach maturity by age 3. Compared to humans, aarakocra don't usually live longer than 30 years.\n\nAlignment\n\nMost aarakocra are good and rarely choose sides when it comes to law and chaos. Tribal leaders and warriors might be lawful, while explorers and adventurers might tend toward chaotic.\n\nSize\n\nAarakocra are about 5 feet tall. They have thin, lightweight bodies that weigh between 80 and 100 pounds. Your size is Medium.\n\nFlight\n\nYou have a flying speed of 50 feet. To use this speed, you can't be wearing medium or heavy armor.\n\nTalons\n\nYour talons are natural weapons, which you can use to make unarmed strikes. If you hit with them, you deal slashing damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier, instead of the bludgeoning damage normal for an unarmed strike.\n\nLanguage\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common, Aarakocra, and Auran."},
  ["creature.aarakocra.mm2014"]={title="Aarakocra",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 13 (3d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Auran, Aarakocra\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDive Attack\n\nIf the aarakocra is flying and dives at least 30 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a melee weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 3 (1d6) damage to the target.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTalon\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nJavelin\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSummon Air Elemental\n\nFive aarakocra within 30 feet of each other can magically summon an air elemental. Each of the five must use its action and movement on three consecutive turns to perform an aerial dance and must maintain concentration while doing so (as if concentration on a spell). When all five have finished their third turn of the dance, the elemental appears in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of them. It is friendly toward them and obeys their spoken commands. It remains for 1 hour, until it or all its summoners die, or until any of its summoners dismisses it as a bonus action. A summoner can't perform the dance again until it finishes a short rest. When the elemental returns to the Elemental Plane of Air, any aarakocra within 5 feet of it can return with it."},
  ["language.aarakocra.mm2014"]={title="Aarakocra",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 12"},
  ["species.aarakocra.mpmm2014"]={title="Aarakocra",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 5\n\nFlight\n\nBecause of your wings, you have a flying speed equal to your walking speed. You can't use this flying speed if you're wearing medium or heavy armor.\n\nTalons\n\nYou have talons that you can use to make unarmed strikes. When you hit with them, the strike deals 1d6 + your Strength modifier slashing damage, instead of the bludgeoning damage normal for an unarmed strike.\n\nWind Caller\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you can cast the gust of wind spell with this trait, without requiring a material component. Once you cast the spell with this trait, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest. You can also cast the spell using any spell slots you have of 2nd level or higher.\n\nIntelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for when you cast gust of wind with this trait (choose when you select this race)."},
  ["language.aarakocra.xmm2024"]={title="Aarakocra",subtitle="Idioma - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 10"},
  ["creature.aarakocra-aeromancer.xmm2024"]={title="Aarakocra Aeromancer",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 10\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 17 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Aarakocra, Primordial (Auran)\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nFeather Fall (1/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aarakocra makes two Wind Staff attacks, and it can use Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nWind Staff\n\nm,r 5, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage plus 11 (2d10) Lightning damage."},
  ["creature.aarakocra-simulacrum.skt2014"]={title="Aarakocra Simulacrum",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 188\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 6 (3d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Auran, Aarakocra\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDive Attack\n\nIf the aarakocra is flying and dives at least 30 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a melee weapon attack, the attack deals an extra 3 (1d6) damage to the target.\n\nSimulacra\n\nWhen a simulacrum drops to 0 hit points or is subjected to a successful dispel magic spell (17), it reverts to ice and snow and is destroyed.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTalon\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nJavelin\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSummon Air Elemental\n\nFive aarakocra within 30 feet of each other can magically summon an air elemental. Each of the five must use its action and movement on three consecutive turns to perform an aerial dance and must maintain concentration while doing so (as if concentration on a spell). When all five have finished their third turn of the dance, the elemental appears in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of them. It is friendly toward them and obeys their spoken commands. It remains for 1 hour, until it or all its summoners die, or until any of its summoners dismisses it as a bonus action. A summoner can't perform the dance again until it finishes a short rest. When the elemental returns to the Elemental Plane of Air, any aarakocra within 5 feet of it can return with it."},
  ["creature.aarakocra-skirmisher.xmm2024"]={title="Aarakocra Skirmisher",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 10\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Aarakocra, Primordial (Auran)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTalons\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage, or 9 (3d4 + 2) Slashing damage if the aarakocra moved 30+ feet straight toward the target immediately before the hit.\n\nWind Javelin\n\nm,r 4, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) Thunder damage. homThe javelin magically returns to the aarakocra's hand immediately after a ranged attack."},
  ["creature.aarakocra-spelljammer.lox2014"]={title="Aarakocra Spelljammer",subtitle="Criatura - LoX - 2014",body="Pagina: 43\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.aartuk-elder.bam2014"]={title="Aartuk Elder",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 75 (10d10 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aartuk\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe aartuk can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aartuk makes two Branch attacks, two Radiant Pellet attacks, or one of each.\n\nBranch\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRadiant Pellet\n\nrs 4 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h10 (4d4) radiant damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTongue {@recharge}\n\nThe aartuk tries to use its gooey tongue to snare one Large or smaller creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target is grappled by the tongue (escape 14) and pulled up to 25 feet toward the aartuk. The tongue can grapple one creature at a time."},
  ["creature.aartuk-starhorror.bam2014"]={title="Aartuk Starhorror",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 16 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aartuk\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe aartuk can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aartuk makes two Branch attacks, two Radiant Pellet attacks, or one of each.\n\nBranch\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (2d6 + 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRadiant Pellet\n\nrs 2 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h7 (3d4) radiant damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nRally the Troops (1/Day)\n\nThe aartuk magically ends the charmed and frightened conditions on itself and each creature of its choice that it can see within 30 feet of itself.\n\nTongue {@recharge}\n\nThe aartuk tries to use its gooey tongue to snare one Medium or smaller creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target is grappled by the tongue (escape 11) and pulled up to 25 feet toward the aartuk. The tongue can grapple one creature at a time."},
  ["creature.aartuk-weedling.bam2014"]={title="Aartuk Weedling",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: plant / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 38 (7d8 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, climb: 20\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Aartuk\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe aartuk can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aartuk makes two Branch attacks, two Radiant Pellet attacks, or one of each.\n\nBranch\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h8 (2d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRadiant Pellet\n\nrs 3 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h7 (3d4 + 1) radiant damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTongue {@recharge}\n\nThe aartuk tries to use its gooey tongue to snare one Medium or smaller creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must make a 11 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the target is grappled by the tongue (escape 12) and pulled up to 25 feet toward the aartuk. The tongue can grapple one creature at a time."},
  ["species.aasimar.dmg2014"]={title="Aasimar",subtitle="Especie - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 286\n\nAge\n\nAasimar mature at the same rate as humans but live a few years longer.\n\nSize\n\nAasimar are built like well-proportioned humans. Your size is Medium.\n\nDarkvision\n\nThanks to your celestial heritage, you have superior vision in dark and dim conditions. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of grey.\n\nCelestial Resistance\n\nYou have resistance to necrotic and radiant damage.\n\nCelestial Legacy\n\nYou know the light cantrip. Once you reach 3rd level, you can cast the lesser restoration spell once with this trait, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a long rest. Once you reach 5th level, you can cast the daylight spell once with this trait, and you regain the ability to do so when you finish a long rest. Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells.\n\nLanguage\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Celestial."},
  ["species.aasimar.mpmm2014"]={title="Aasimar",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\nSize\n\nYou are Medium or Small. You choose the size when you select this race.\n\nCelestial Resistance\n\nYou have resistance to necrotic damage and radiant damage.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light and in darkness as if it were dim light. You discern colors in that darkness only as shades of gray.\n\nHealing Hands\n\nAs an action, you can touch a creature and roll a number of d4s equal to your proficiency bonus. The creature regains a number of hit points equal to the total rolled. Once you use this trait, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nLight Bearer\n\nYou know the light cantrip. Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it.\n\nCelestial Revelation\n\nWhen you reach 3rd level, choose one of the revelation options below. Thereafter, you can use a bonus action to unleash the celestial energy within yourself, gaining the benefits of that revelation. Your transformation lasts for 1 minute or until you end it as a bonus action. Once you transform using your revelation below, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.\n\n• Necrotic Shroud\n\n• Radiant Consumption\n\n• Radiant Soul"},
  ["species.aasimar.vgm2014"]={title="Aasimar",subtitle="Especie - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 104\n\nAge\n\nAasimar mature at the same rate as humans, but they can live up to 160 years.\n\nSize\n\nAasimar have the same range of height and weight as humans.\n\nDarkvision\n\nBlessed with a radiant soul, your vision can easily cut through darkness. You can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nCelestial Resistance\n\nYou have resistance to necrotic damage and radiant damage.\n\nHealing Hands\n\nAs an action, you can touch a creature and cause it to regain a number of hit points equal to your level. Once you use this trait, you can't use it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nLight Bearer\n\nYou know the light cantrip. Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Celestial."},
  ["species.aasimar.xphb2024"]={title="Aasimar",subtitle="Especie - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 186\n\nCelestial Resistance\n\nYou have XPHB to Necrotic damage and Radiant damage.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 60 feet.\n\nHealing Hands\n\nAs a XPHB action, you touch a creature and roll a number of d4s equal to your XPHB. The creature regains a number of XPHB equal to the total rolled. Once you use this trait, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nLight Bearer\n\nYou know the XPHB cantrip. Charisma is your spellcasting ability for it.\n\nCelestial Revelation\n\nWhen you reach character level 3, you can transform as a XPHB using one of the options below (choose the option each time you transform). The transformation lasts for 1 minute or until you end it (no action required). Once you transform, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nOnce on each of your turns before the transformation ends, you can deal extra damage to one target when you deal damage to it with an attack or a spell. The extra damage equals your XPHB, and the extra damage's type is either Necrotic for Necrotic Shroud or Radiant for Heavenly Wings and Inner Radiance.\n\nHere are the transformation options:\n\n• Heavenly Wings Two spectral wings sprout from your back temporarily. Until the transformation ends, you have a XPHB equal to your XPHB.\n\n• Inner Radiance Searing light temporarily radiates from your eyes and mouth. For the duration, you shed XPHB in a 10-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 10 feet, and at the end of each of your turns, each creature within 10 feet of you takes Radiant damage equal to your XPHB.\n\n• Necrotic Shroud Your eyes briefly become pools of darkness, and flightless wings sprout from your back temporarily. Creatures other than your allies within 10 feet of you must succeed on a Charisma saving throw (8 plus your Charisma modifier and XPHB) or have the XPHB condition until the end of your next turn."},
  ["item.abacus.phb2014"]={title="Abacus",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["language.abanasinian.dsotdq2014"]={title="Abanasinian",subtitle="Idioma - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["deity.abbathor.mtf2014"]={title="Abbathor",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 73\n\nThe Great Master of Greed exerts an influence, no matter how subtle, over every dwarven heart. Abbathor teaches that greed isn't only desirable, but necessary to keep the dwarves in a strong and safe position.\n\nAbbathor has no skill in crafting. Instead, he relies on his ability as a thief to take ownership of what he wants. Why work so hard to manufacture something when a much easier path to riches lies open?\n\nAbbathor is the only advocate for change within the dwarven pantheon. He can inspire dwarves to seek shortcuts, normally frowned upon, but sometimes those methods turn out to be efficient techniques that improve a clan's capabilities."},
  ["deity.abbathor.scag2014"]={title="Abbathor",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 22"},
  ["feat.aberrant-anatomy.rhw2014"]={title="Aberrant Anatomy",subtitle="Feat - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\nExposure to alien horrors like those of the Far Realm has warped your physical form in supernatural ways. You gain the following features.\n\nBreathless\n\nYou can hold your breath for 1 hour.\n\nExtrasensory Perception\n\nYou have proficiency in the XPHB skill, if you lack it. You also gain XPHB in that skill.\n\nIn addition, you have XPHB with a range of 15 feet.\n\nWarping Flesh\n\nImmediately after you make a XPHB and roll a 1 on the d20, the aberrant influence infecting your form flares, wrenching control of your flesh. Make a Constitution saving throw (DC 13 plus your XPHB). On a failed save, you have the XPHB condition until the end of your next turn."},
  ["creature.aberrant-cultist.xmm2024"]={title="Aberrant Cultist",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 86\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 137 (25d8 + 25)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 19 | CON 12 | INT 16 | WIS 18 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 90 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Deep Speech; telepathy 30 ft.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nCounterspell (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe cultist makes two Tentacle Lash attacks. It can replace any attack with a use of Mind Rot.\n\nTentacle Lash\n\nm 7, reach 10 ft. h7 (1d6 + 4) Slashing damage plus 14 (4d6) Psychic damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 14) from one of two tentacles, and it has the XPHB condition until the grapple ends.\n\nMind Rot\n\nwis 15, one creature the cultist can see within 90 feet. actSaveFail 27 (6d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the cultist's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["creature.aberrant-death-s-head.rhw2014"]={title="Aberrant Death's Head",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / T\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 24 (7d4 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 13 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 3\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: necrotic, psychic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe death's head doesn't provoke an XPHB when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBrain-Rending Bite\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h3 (1d4 + 1) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the death's head's next turn."},
  ["feat.aberrant-dragonmark.efa2014"]={title="Aberrant Dragonmark",subtitle="Feat - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAberrant Fortitude\n\nWhen you fail a Constitution saving throw, you can take a XPHB to roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the save, potentially turning the failure into a success. Once you've used this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nAberrant Magic\n\nYou know one spells. Also, choose a level 1 spell from that spell list. You always have that spell prepared. You can cast it once without a spell slot, and you regain the ability to cast it in that way when you finish a XPHB or XPHB. You can also cast this spell using any spell slots you have. Constitution is your spellcasting ability for this spell.\n\nAberrant Surge\n\nWhen you cast the level 1 spell from this feat, you can expend one of your XPHB and roll it. If you roll an even number, you gain a number of XPHB equal to the number rolled. If you roll an odd number, one creature within 30 feet of you (not including you) takes Force damage equal to the number rolled. If no other creatures are in range, you take the damage."},
  ["feat.aberrant-dragonmark.erlw2014"]={title="Aberrant Dragonmark",subtitle="Feat - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 52\n\nYou have manifested an aberrant dragonmark. Determine its appearance and the flaw associated with it. You gain the following benefits:\n\n• You learn a spells. In addition, choose a spells. You learn that spell and can cast it through your mark. Once you cast it, you must finish a short or long rest before you can cast it again through the mark. Constitution is your spellcasting ability for these spells.\n\n• When you cast the 1st-level spell through your mark, you can expend one of your Hit Dice and roll it. If you roll an even number, you gain a number of temporary hit points equal to the number rolled. If you roll an odd number, one random creature within 30 feet of you (not including you) takes force damage equal to the number rolled. If no other creatures are in range, you take the damage.\n\nYou also develop a random flaw from the Aberrant Dragonmark Flaws table.\n\nd8 | Flaw\n\n1 | Your mark is a source of constant physical pain.\n\n2 | Your mark whispers to you. Its meaning can be unclear.\n\n3 | When you're stressed, the mark hisses audibly.\n\n4 | The skin around the mark is burned, scaly, or withered.\n\n5 | Animals are uneasy around you.\n\n6 | You have a mood swing any time you use your mark.\n\n7 | Your looks change slightly whenever you use the mark.\n\n8 | You have horrific nightmares after you use your mark.\n\nOption: Greater Aberrant Powers\n\nAt the DM's option, a character who has the Aberrant Dragonmark feat has a chance of manifesting greater power. Upon reaching 10th level, such a character has a 10 chance of gaining an rewards from among the options in chapter 7 of the DMG. If the character fails to gain a boon, they have a 10 chance the next time they gain a level.\n\nIf the character gains a boon, the DM chooses it or determines it randomly. The character also permanently loses one of their Hit Dice, and their hit point maximum is reduced by an amount equal to a roll of that die plus their Constitution modifier (minimum reduction of 1). This reduction can't be reversed by any means."},
  ["background.aberrant-heir.efa2014"]={title="Aberrant Heir",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 25\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["subclass.aberrant-mind.tce2014.sorcerer.aberrant-mind.0"]={title="Aberrant Mind",subtitle="Subclasse - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.aberrant-mind.tce2014.sorcerer.aberrant-mind.1"]={title="Aberrant Mind",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 66\n\nAn alien influence has wrapped its tendrils around your mind, giving you psionic power. You can now touch other minds with that power and alter the world around you by using it to control the magical energy of the multiverse. Will this power shine from you as a hopeful beacon to others? Or will you be a source of terror to those who feel the stab of your mind and witness the strange manifestations of your might?\n\nAs an Aberrant Mind sorcerer, you decide how you acquired your powers. Were you born with them? Or did an event later in life leave you shining with psionic awareness? Consult the Aberrant Origins table for a possible origin of your power.\n\nd6 | Origin\n\n1 | You were exposed to the Far Realm's warping influence. You are convinced that a tentacle is now growing on you, but no one else can see it.\n\n2 | A psychic wind from the Astral Plane carried psionic energy to you. When you use your powers, faint motes of light sparkle around you.\n\n3 | You once suffered the dominating powers of an aboleth, leaving a psychic splinter in your mind.\n\n4 | You were implanted with a mind flayer tadpole, but the ceremorphosis never completed. And now its psionic power is yours. When you use it, your flesh shines with a strange mucus.\n\n5 | As a child, you had an imaginary friend that looked like a flumph or a strange platypus-like creature. One day, it gifted you with psionic powers, which have ended up being not so imaginary.\n\n6 | Your nightmares whisper the truth to you: your psionic powers are not your own. You draw them from your parasitic twin!"},
  ["feature.aberrant-mind.tce2014.sorcerer.aberrant-mind.3"]={title="Aberrant Mind",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.aberrant-sorcery.xphb2024.sorcerer.aberrant.0"]={title="Aberrant Sorcery",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 145"},
  ["feature.aberrant-sorcery.xphb2024.sorcerer.aberrant.3"]={title="Aberrant Sorcery",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 145\n\nWield Unnatural Psionic Power\n\nAn alien influence has wrapped its tendrils around your mind, giving you psionic power. You can now touch other minds with that power and alter the world around you. Will this power shine from you as a hopeful beacon to others? Or will you be a terror to those who feel the stab of your mind?\n\nPerhaps a psychic wind from the Astral Plane carried psionic energy to you, or you were exposed to the Far Realm's warping influence. Alternatively, you were implanted with a mind flayer tadpole, but your transformation into a mind flayer never occurred; now the tadpole's psionic power is yours. However you acquired this power, your mind is aflame with it."},
  ["creature.aberrant-spirit.tce2014"]={title="Aberrant Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 109\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 16 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, understands the languages you speak\n\nImunidades: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRegeneration (Slaad Only)\n\nThe aberration regains 5 hit points at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 hit point.\n\nWhispering Aura (Star Spawn Only)\n\nAt the start of each of the aberration's turns, each creature within 5 feet of the aberration must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or take 2d6 psychic damage, provided that the aberration isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aberration makes a number of attacks equal to half this spell's level (rounded down).\n\nEye Ray (Beholderkin Only)\n\nrs hitYourSpellAttack to hit, range 150 ft., one creature. h1d8 + 3 + summonSpellLevel psychic damage.\n\nClaws (Slaad Only)\n\nmw hitYourSpellAttack to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h1d10 + 3 + summonSpellLevel slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it can't regain hit points until the start of the aberration's next turn.\n\nPsychic Slam (Star Spawn Only)\n\nms hitYourSpellAttack to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h1d8 + 3 + summonSpellLevel psychic damage."},
  ["creature.aberrant-spirit.xphb2024"]={title="Aberrant Spirit",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 322\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 16 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Deep Speech, understands the languages you know\n\nImunidades: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRegeneration (Slaad Only)\n\nThe spirit regains 5 XPHB at the start of its turn if it has at least 1 XPHB.\n\nWhispering Aura (Mind Flayer Only)\n\nAt the start of each of the spirit's turns, the spirit emits psionic energy if it doesn't have the XPHB condition. wis DC equals your spell save DC, each creature (other than you) within 5 feet of the spirit. actSaveFail 2d6 Psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe spirit makes a number of attacks equal to half this spell's level (round down).\n\nClaw (Slaad Only)\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. h1d10 + 3 + summonSpellLevel Slashing damage, and the target can't regain XPHB until the start of the spirit's next turn.\n\nEye Ray (Beholderkin Only)\n\nr Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, range 150 ft. h1d8 + 3 + summonSpellLevel Psychic damage.\n\nPsychic Slam (Mind Flayer Only)\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. h1d8 + 3 + summonSpellLevel Psychic damage."},
  ["creature.aberrant-zealot.pabtso2014"]={title="Aberrant Zealot",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 203\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 93 (17d8 + 17)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 8 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., truesight 10 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Deep Speech\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, frightened, grappled, restrained\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAberrant Form\n\nThe zealot exudes the chaos of the Far Realm. Any non-Aberration creature that starts its turn within 5 feet of the zealot must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or take 7 (2d6) psychic damage.\n\nWeirdly Pliable\n\nThe zealot, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, is unnaturally flexible. The zealot can move through any space as narrow as 1 inch without squeezing.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe zealot makes one Psychic Rend attack and two Shortsword attacks.\n\nPsychic Rend\n\nms,rs 7 to hit, reach 15 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h14 (3d6 + 4) psychic damage, and the target must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or have the stunned condition until the start of the zealot's next turn.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nVoid Warp {@recharge 5}\n\nThe zealot teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, to an unoccupied space it can see within 120 feet of itself, leaving a churning void in the space it left. Immediately after it teleports, each creature within 30 feet of the void other than the zealot must make a 15 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 18 (4d8) force damage and is pulled to the unoccupied space closest to the void. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only. The void then disappears."},
  ["creature.aberrant-zealot-tentacled.pabtso2014"]={title="Aberrant Zealot (Tentacled)",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 181\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.abhorrent-overlord.mot2014"]={title="Abhorrent Overlord",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 136 (16d10 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 15 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nInsatiable Greed\n\nThe abhorrent overlord can sense the presence of gold within 1,000 feet of itself. It can determine which location has the greatest amount of gold and can sense the direction to that site. If the gold is being moved, it knows the direction of the movement. It can't locate gold if any thickness of clay or lead, even a thin sheet, blocks a direct path between it and the gold.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe abhorrent overlord has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe abhorrent overlord makes two attacks with its claws.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) slashing damage plus 14 (4d6) necrotic damage. The abhorrent overlord regains hit points equal to half the amount of necrotic damage dealt if the target is a creature.\n\nStorm of Crows {@recharge}\n\nThe abhorrent overlord conjures a swarm of spectral crows and harpies in a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on a point the overlord can see within 120 feet of it. The sphere remains for 1 minute or until the overlord loses concentration (as if concentration on a spell), and its area is lightly obscured and difficult terrain.\n\nAny creature that moves into the area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must make a 15 Constitution saving throw. A creature takes 16 (3d10) slashing damage plus 16 (3d10) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["spell.abi-dalzim-s-horrid-wilting.xge2024"]={title="Abi-Dalzim's Horrid Wilting",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 150\n\nYou draw the moisture from every creature in a 30-foot cube centered on a point you choose within range. Each creature in that area must make a Constitution saving throw. Constructs and undead aren't affected, and plants and water elementals make this saving throw with disadvantage. A creature takes 12d8 necrotic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nNonmagical plants in the area that aren't creatures, such as trees and shrubs, wither and die instantly."},
  ["creature.abigor.coa2014"]={title="Abigor",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 193\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 337 (27d10 + 189)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 20 | WIS 16 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Infernal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede Abigor's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nAbigor has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAbigor makes four attacks using its Warhammer, Throwing Hammer, or a combination of the two.\n\nWarhammer\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) thunder damage.\n\nThrowing Hammer\n\nrw 15 to hit, range 30/60 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage plus 3 (1d6) thunder damage. Hammers thrown this way fall and stick into the ground after hitting their target and a new hammer appears in Abigor's hand.\n\nThunderous Slam {@recharge 5}\n\nAbigor causes all its hammers left on the battlefield to bristle with thunderous energy, exploding outwards with a roar. All creatures within a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on each hammer must make a 22 Constitution saving throw. Targets take 26 (4d12) thunder damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If a creature is within multiple spheres, it must make the save multiple times, taking damage from each source.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nThrow Hammer\n\nAbigor makes a Throwing Hammer attack.\n\nCall Thunder (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nAbigor targets a hammer that it can see within 60 feet to let out a thunderous roar. Creatures within a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on the hammer must make a 22 Constitution saving throw, taking 26 (4d12) thunder damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["feature.ability-score-improvement.efa2014.artificer.base.4"]={title="Ability Score Improvement",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feat of your choice for which you qualify. You gain this feature again at Artificer levels 8, 12, and 16."},
  ["feature.ability-score-improvement.efa2014.artificer.base.8"]={title="Ability Score Improvement",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feat of your choice for which you qualify."},
  ["feature.ability-score-improvement.efa2014.artificer.base.12"]={title="Ability Score Improvement",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feat of your choice for which you qualify."},
  ["feature.ability-score-improvement.efa2014.artificer.base.16"]={title="Ability Score Improvement",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feat of your choice for which you qualify."},
  ["feature.ability-score-improvement.phb2014.barbarian.base.4"]={title="Ability Score Improvement",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 46\n\nWhen you reach 4th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html."},
