geoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-red-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Red Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 256\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 507 (26d20 + 234)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 10 | CON 29 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 27\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 17, reach 15 ft. h19 (2d8 + 10) Slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) Fire damage.\n\nFire Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 24, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 91 (26d6) Fire damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nCommanding Presence\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version). The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nFiery Rays\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 3 version). The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.ancient-sapphire-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Sapphire Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 370 (20d20 + 160)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 27 | INT 21 | WIS 19 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe dragon can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 20-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) thunder damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nDebilitating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a pulse of high-pitched, nearly inaudible sound in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 23 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 55 (10d10) thunder damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nTelekinetic Fling (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon chooses one Medium or smaller object that isn't being worn or carried that it can see within 60 feet of it, and it magically hurls the object at a creature it can see within 60 feet of the object. The target must succeed on a 20 Dexterity saving throw or take 42 (12d6) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.ancient-sea-serpent.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Sea Serpent",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 170 (11d20 + 55)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 60\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 15 | CON 20 | INT 13 | WIS 16 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe sea serpent can breathe air and water.\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf the sea serpent fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe sea serpent deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sea serpent makes one Bite attack and one Constrict or Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d12 + 7) piercing damage plus 6 (1d12) cold damage.\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 20 ft., one creature. h29 (4d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 20). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the sea serpent can't constrict another target.\n\nTail\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h13 (1d12 + 7) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 20 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 30 feet away from the sea serpent and knocked prone.\n\nRime Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe sea serpent exhales a 60-foot cone of cold. Each creature in that area must make a 18 Constitution saving throw, taking 49 (9d10) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail\n\nThe sea serpent makes one Tail attack.\n\nBite (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe sea serpent makes one Bite attack"},
  ["reward.ancient-seal.vrgr2014"]={title="Ancient Seal",subtitle="Recompensa - VRGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 193\n\nThis curse protects the resting place of a long-dead ruler and punishes any who disturb the ruler's remains or plunder the treasures.\n\nPronouncement\n\nCarved into the stone of the crypt door are the words \"Relentless death follows those who disturb the sovereign's rest.\"\n\nBurden\n\nEach character that gains the curse is hunted by a wraith that appears at sunset and vanishes at dawn, pursuing the single-minded goal of slaying the cursed individual. The wraith manifests in an unoccupied space within 30 feet of its victim. Destroying the wraith grants a temporary reprieve; it doesn't reform for 10 days. You can scale this curse for lower- and higher-level characters by choosing another kind of creature.\n\nResolution\n\nThe cursed character sets right what they disturbed; stolen treasure must be returned, and if the ruler's body was disturbed, it must be reinterred with proper observances."},
  ["creature.ancient-silver-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient Silver Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 487 (25d20 + 225)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 10 | CON 29 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h21 (2d10 + 10) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h17 (2d6 + 10) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h19 (2d8 + 10) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 21 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nBreath Weapons {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon uses one of the following breath weapons.\n\n• Cold Breath\n\n• Paralyzing Breath\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically polymorphs into a humanoid or beast that has a challenge rating no higher than its own, or back into its true form. It reverts to its true form if it dies. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is absorbed or borne by the new form (the dragon's choice).\n\nIn a new form, the dragon retains its alignment, hit points, Hit Dice, ability to speak, proficiencies, Legendary Resistance, lair actions, and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores, as well as this action. Its statistics and capabilities are otherwise replaced by those of the new form, except any class features or legendary actions of that form.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 25 Dexterity saving throw or take 17 (2d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-silver-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient Silver Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 280\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 468 (24d20 + 216)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 10 | CON 29 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Paralyzing Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 17, reach 15 ft. h19 (2d8 + 10) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Cold damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 24, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 67 (15d8) Cold damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nParalyzing Breath\n\ncon 24, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. 1 The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, when it repeats the save. 2 The target has the XPHB condition, and it repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nChill\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB. The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nCold Gale\n\ndex 23, each creature in a 60-foot-long, 10-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Cold damage, and the target is pushed up to 30 feet straight away from the dragon. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.ancient-solar-dragon.bam2014"]={title="Ancient Solar Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 425 (23d20 + 184)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 120\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 15 | CON 26 | INT 17 | WIS 18 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 240 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe dragon doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nNebulous Thoughts\n\nMagical attempts to read the dragon's mind or glean its thoughts fail automatically.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe dragon deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and one Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h19 (3d6 + 9) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) radiant damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h13 (1d8 + 9) bludgeoning damage.\n\nPhotonic Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a flashing mote of radiant energy that travels to a point the dragon can see within 240 feet of itself, then blossoms into a 40-foot-radius sphere centered on that point. Each creature in the sphere must make a 23 Constitution saving throw, taking 66 (12d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes one Tail attack.\n\nBlinding Brilliance (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon emits magical light in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on itself. Each creature in this area must succeed on a 23 Wisdom saving throw or be blinded until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.ancient-spirit-dragon.fraif2014"]={title="Ancient Spirit Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 279\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 420 (24d20 + 168)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 24 | WIS 18 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of (A) Time-Warping Breath or (B) Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 15, reach 15 ft. h19 (2d10 + 8) Slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) Necrotic damage.\n\nRuinous Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 22, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 72 (16d8) Necrotic damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\nTime-Warping Breath\n\nwis 22, each creature that isn't currently affected by this breath in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail The target's XPHB is halved, it can't take Reactions, and it can take either an action or a XPHB on its turn, not both. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. After 1 minute, it succeeds automatically.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nShattering Wave\n\nThe dragon uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 2 version).\n\nUnearth Ruins\n\nThe dragon magically raises broken, ancient ruins in a 20-foot-radius, 60-foot-high XPHB centered on a point it can see within 120 feet. Ground in the XPHB becomes XPHB. Each creature in the XPHB when it appears is subjected to the following effect. str 22. actSaveFail 13 (3d8) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.ancient-time-dragon.mpp2014"]={title="Ancient Time Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 22\n\nPV: 536 (29d20 + 232)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40, fly: 80\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 26 | INT 27 | WIS 18 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCycle of Rebirth\n\nIf the dragon dies, its soul coalesces into a steely egg and teleports to a random plane of existence. The egg is immune to all damage and hatches into a time dragon wyrmling after 1d100 years. The dragon retains all memories and knowledge it gained in its previous life.\n\nLegendary Resistance (5/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h22 (3d8 + 9) slashing damage plus 10 (3d6) force damage.\n\nTime Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a wave of shimmering light in a 90-foot cone. Nonmagical objects and vegetation in that area that aren't being worn or carried crumble to dust. Each creature in that area must make a 24 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 52 (8d12) force damage and is magically weakened as it is desynchronized from the time stream. While the creature is in this state, attack rolls against it have advantage, it has the poisoned condition, and other creatures have resistance to all damage it deals. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage only. A weakened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself after it succeeds on three of these saves.\n\nTime Gate (1/Day)\n\nThe dragon conjures a 20-foot-diameter, circular portal in the space between its horns or in an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of itself. The portal links to a precise location on any plane of existence at a point in time up to 8,000 years from the present, whether past or future. The portal lasts for 24 hours or until the dragon's concentration ends (as if concentration on a spell). The portal has a front and a back on each plane where it appears. Travel through the portal is possible only by moving through its front. Anything that does so is transported to the destination, appearing in the unoccupied space nearest to the portal. Deities and other planar rulers can prevent portals created by the dragon from opening in the rulers' presence or anywhere within their domains.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nReactive Rend\n\nAfter using Legendary Resistance or in response to being hit by an attack roll, the dragon makes one Rend attack.\n\nSlow Time\n\nImmediately after a creature the dragon can see ends its turn, the dragon targets a creature it can see within 90 feet of itself that is weakened by its Time Breath. Until the weakened effect ends on the target, its speed becomes 0, and its speed can't increase.\n\nTime Slip\n\nThe dragon halves the damage it takes from an attack made against it, provided it can see the attacker. The dragon can then immediately teleport, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.ancient-topaz-dragon.ftd2014"]={title="Ancient Topaz Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 280 (17d20 + 102)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 12 | CON 23 | INT 20 | WIS 19 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe dragon can breathe both air and water.\n\nFabricate (1/Day)\n\nThe dragon can cast fabricate, requiring no spell components and using Intelligence as the spellcasting ability.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) necrotic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nDesiccating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales yellowish necrotic energy in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 20 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 49 (14d6) necrotic damage and is weakened until the end of its next turn. A weakened creature has disadvantage on Strength-based ability checks and Strength saving throws, and the creature's weapon attacks that rely on Strength deal half damage. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't weakened.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe dragon magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the dragon is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe dragon magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe dragon makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nEssential Reduction (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe dragon targets a creature or an object not being worn or carried that it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 19 Constitution saving throw or take 40 (9d8) necrotic damage. If this damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, it crumbles to dust."},
  ["creature.ancient-white-dragon.mm2014"]={title="Ancient White Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 100\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 333 (18d20 + 144)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 10 | CON 26 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIce Walk\n\nThe dragon can move across and climb icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, difficult terrain composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon can use its Frightful Presence. It then makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) piercing damage plus 9 (2d8) cold damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h15 (2d6 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h17 (2d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nFrightful Presence\n\nEach creature of the dragon's choice that is within 120 feet of the dragon and aware of it must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or become frightened for 1 minute. A creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the dragon's Frightful Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales an icy blast in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Constitution saving throw, taking 72 (16d8) cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDetect\n\nThe dragon makes a Wisdom (Perception) check.\n\nTail Attack\n\nThe dragon makes a tail attack.\n\nWing Attack (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe dragon beats its wings. Each creature within 15 feet of the dragon must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or take 15 (2d6 + 8) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. The dragon can then fly up to half its flying speed."},
  ["creature.ancient-white-dragon.xmm2024"]={title="Ancient White Dragon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 330\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 333 (18d20 + 144)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 40, fly: 80, swim: 40\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 10 | CON 26 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIce Walk\n\nThe dragon can move across and climb icy surfaces without needing to make an ability check. Additionally, XPHB composed of ice or snow doesn't cost it extra movement.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the dragon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nFrightful Presence\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes three Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 14, reach 15 ft. h17 (2d8 + 8) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Cold damage.\n\nCold Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 22, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 63 (14d8) Cold damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFreezing Burst\n\ncon 20, each creature in a 30-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the dragon can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Cold damage, and the target's XPHB is 0 until the end of the target's next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail The dragon can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nPounce\n\nThe dragon moves up to half its XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack."},
  ["creature.andir-valmakos.dsotdq2014"]={title="Andir Valmakos",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBonus Proficiencies\n\nAndir is proficient with simple weapons and light armor.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) force damage.\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage, or 4 (1d8) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands."},
  ["creature.andras.imr2014"]={title="Andras",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant Owl"},
  ["creature.android.qftis2014"]={title="Android",subtitle="Criatura - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 194\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 91 (14d8 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (sentry only), darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus the languages spoken by its creator\n\nResistencias: acid, fire\n\nImunidades: cold, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDesign Specialization\n\nWhen the android is created, it gains one of six possible designs suited for its role (choose or roll a d6): 1, aerialist; 2, diplomat; 3, diver; 4, duelist; 5, medic; 6, sentry. This design determines certain traits in this stat block.\n\nLightning Overload\n\nWhen the android takes lightning damage, it must succeed on a 10 Constitution saving throw or have the stunned condition until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Diplomat and Medic Only)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe android makes two Force Strike attacks.\n\nForce Strike\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 40/120 ft., one target. h15 (2d10 + 4) force damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry (Duelist Only)\n\nThe android adds 3 to its AC against one melee attack roll that would hit it. To do so, the android must see the attacker."},
  ["creature.androsphinx.mm2014"]={title="Androsphinx",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 281\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 199 (19d10 + 95)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, fly: 60\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 16 | WIS 18 | CHA 23\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Sphinx\n\nImunidades: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nInscrutable\n\nThe sphinx is immune to any effect that would sense its emotions or read its thoughts, as well as any divination spell that it refuses. Wisdom (Insight) checks made to ascertain the sphinx's intentions or sincerity have disadvantage.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe sphinx's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sphinx makes two claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nRoar (3/Day)\n\nThe sphinx emits a magical roar. Each time it roars before finishing a long rest, the roar is louder and the effect is different, as detailed below. Each creature within 500 feet of the sphinx and able to hear the roar must make a saving throw.\n\n• First Roar\n\n• Second Roar\n\n• Third Roar\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw Attack\n\nThe sphinx makes one claw attack.\n\nTeleport (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe sphinx magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe sphinx casts a spell from its list of prepared spells, using a spell slot as normal."},
  ["creature.angel.psk2014"]={title="Angel",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.angel.psz2014"]={title="Angel",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.angel-of-amonkhet.psa2014"]={title="Angel of Amonkhet",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["deity.angharradh.mtf2014"]={title="Angharradh",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["deity.angharradh.scag2014"]={title="Angharradh",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 23"},
  ["creature.angry-sorrowsworn.mpmm2014"]={title="Angry Sorrowsworn",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 222\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 255 (30d8 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 8 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTwo Heads\n\nThe sorrowsworn has advantage on saving throws against being blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, or knocked unconscious.\n\nRising Anger\n\nIf another creature deals damage to the sorrowsworn, the sorrowsworn's attack rolls have advantage until the end of its next turn, and the first time it hits with a Hook attack on its next turn, the attack's target takes an extra 19 (3d12) psychic damage.\n\nOn its turn, the sorrowsworn has disadvantage on attack rolls if no other creature has dealt damage to it since the end of its last turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sorrowsworn makes two Hook attacks.\n\nHook\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d12 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.anhkolox.dsotdq2014"]={title="Anhkolox",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 157 (15d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 4 | WIS 14 | CHA 2\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe anhkolox doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe anhkolox makes two Claw attacks and one Entrapping Rend attack.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (2d10 + 6) piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 20 feet in a horizontal direction of the anhkolox's choice.\n\nEntrapping Rend\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h23 (5d6 + 6) piercing damage, and if the target is a Large or smaller creature, the target must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or be trapped in the anhkolox's rib cage and grappled (escape 18). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the anhkolox can't use Entrapping Rend on another target."},
  ["spell.animal-friendship.phb2014"]={title="Animal Friendship",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\nThis spell lets you convince a beast that you mean it no harm. Choose a beast that you can see within range. It must see and hear you. If the beast's Intelligence is 4 or higher, the spell fails. Otherwise, the beast must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be charmed by you for the spell's duration. If you or one of your companions harms the target, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.animal-friendship.xphb2024"]={title="Animal Friendship",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 239\n\nTarget a Beast that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition for the duration. If you or one of your allies deals damage to the target, the spell ends."},
  ["creature.animal-lord.xmm2024"]={title="Animal Lord",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 15\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / M\n\nCR: 20\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 323 (34d8 + 170)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 60, swim: 60\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 25 | CON 20 | INT 19 | WIS 23 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, necrotic, psychic, radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimal Lordship\n\nAn animal lord represents a Forager, Hunter, or Sage (DM's choice), which determines certain traits in this stat block.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the animal lord fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nLordly Presence\n\nwis 20, any enemy that starts its turn in a 30-foot XPHB originating from the animal lord. actSaveFail The target suffers one of the following effects:\n\n• Captivated (Forager Only) The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition.\n\n• Fearful (Hunter Only) The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn.\n\n• Mired (Sage Only) The target takes 10 (3d6) Psychic damage, and the target is magically bewildered until the end of its next turn. While bewildered, the target subtracts 1d4 from its saving throws.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe animal lord has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe animal lord makes two attacks, using Rend or Radiant Ray in any combination, and uses Animal Spirit.\n\nRend\n\nm 13, reach 5 ft. h14 (2d6 + 7) Slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) Force damage.\n\nRadiant Ray\n\nr 12, range 120 ft. h20 (4d6 + 6) Radiant damage.\n\nAnimal Spirit\n\nThe animal lord conjures an animal spirit that strikes at a creature and then disappears. dex 20, one creature the animal lord can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 28 (4d10 + 6) Radiant damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage. actSaveSuccessOrFail One of the following effects occurs:\n\n• Fortify (Forager Only) The animal lord gains 20 XPHB.\n\n• Marked as Prey (Hunter Only) The animal lord has XPHB on attack rolls against the target until the start of the animal lord's next turn.\n\n• Pesky Swarm (Sage Only) The target has XPHB on attack rolls and ability checks until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe animal lord shape-shifts into a Huge or smaller version of the animal it represents or a Medium or Small Humanoid, or it returns to its true form. Its game statistics, other than its size, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFeral Strike\n\nThe animal lord moves up to its XPHB without provoking XPHB, and it makes one Rend attack.\n\nRadiant Strike\n\nThe animal lord makes one Radiant Ray attack."},
  ["spell.animal-messenger.phb2014"]={title="Animal Messenger",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\nBy means of this spell, you use an animal to deliver a message. Choose a Tiny beast you can see within range, such as a squirrel, a blue jay, or a bat. You specify a location, which you must have visited, and a recipient who matches a general description, such as \"a man or woman dressed in the uniform of the town guard\" or \"a red-haired dwarf wearing a pointed hat.\" You also speak a message of up to twenty-five words. The target beast travels for the duration of the spell toward the specified location, covering about 50 miles per 24 hours for a flying messenger, or 25 miles for other animals.\n\nWhen the messenger arrives, it delivers your message to the creature that you described, replicating the sound of your voice. The messenger speaks only to a creature matching the description you gave. If the messenger doesn't reach its destination before the spell ends, the message is lost, and the beast makes its way back to where you cast this spell."},
  ["spell.animal-messenger.xphb2024"]={title="Animal Messenger",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nA bestiary of your choice that you can see within range must succeed on a Charisma saving throw, or it attempts to deliver a message for you (if the target's XPHB isn't 0, it automatically succeeds). You specify a location you have visited and a recipient who matches a general description, such as \"a person dressed in the uniform of the town guard\" or \"a red-haired dwarf wearing a pointed hat.\" You also communicate a message of up to twenty-five words. The Beast travels for the duration toward the specified location, covering about 25 miles per 24 hours or 50 miles if the Beast can fly.\n\nWhen the Beast arrives, it delivers your message to the creature that you described, mimicking your communication. If the Beast doesn't reach its destination before the spell ends, the message is lost, and the Beast returns to where you cast the spell."},
  ["spell.animal-shapes.phb2014"]={title="Animal Shapes",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\nYour magic turns others into beasts. Choose any number of willing creatures that you can see within range. You transform each target into the form of a bestiary. On subsequent turns, you can use your action to transform affected creatures into new forms.\n\nThe transformation lasts for the duration for each target, or until the target drops to 0 hit points or dies. You can choose a different form for each target. A target's game statistics are replaced by the statistics of the chosen beast, though the target retains its alignment and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. The target assumes the hit points of its new form, and when it reverts to its normal form, it returns to the number of hit points it had before it transformed. If it reverts as a result of dropping to 0 hit points, any excess damage carries over to its normal form. As long as the excess damage doesn't reduce the creature's normal form to 0 hit points, it isn't knocked unconscious. The creature is limited in the actions it can perform by the nature of its new form, and it can't speak or cast spells.\n\nThe target's gear melds into the new form. The target can't activate, wield, or otherwise benefit from any of its equipment."},
  ["spell.animal-shapes.xphb2024"]={title="Animal Shapes",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nChoose any number of willing creatures that you can see within range. Each target shape-shifts into a Large or smaller Beast of your choice that has a XPHB of 4 or lower. You can choose a different form for each target. On later turns, you can take a XPHB action to transform the targets again.\n\nA target's game statistics are replaced by the chosen Beast's statistics, but the target retains its creature type; XPHB; XPHB; alignment; ability to communicate; and Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma scores. The target's actions are limited by the Beast form's anatomy, and it can't cast spells. The target's equipment melds into the new form, and the target can't use any of that equipment while in that form.\n\nThe target gains a number of XPHB equal to the XPHB of the first form into which it shape-shifts. These XPHB vanish if any remain when the spell ends. The transformation lasts for the duration or until the target ends it as a XPHB."},
  ["feature.animal-speaker.xphb2024.barbarian.wild-heart.3"]={title="Animal Speaker",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 55\n\nYou can cast the XPHB and XPHB spells but only as Rituals. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for them."},
  ["spell.animate-dead.phb2014"]={title="Animate Dead",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\nThis spell creates an undead servant. Choose a pile of bones or a corpse of a Medium or Small humanoid within range. Your spell imbues the target with a foul mimicry of life, raising it as an undead creature. The target becomes a skeleton if you chose bones or a zombie if you chose a corpse (the DM has the creature's game statistics).\n\nOn each of your turns, you can use a bonus action to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 60 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any or all of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). You decide what action the creature will take and where it will move during its next turn, or you can issue a general command, such as to guard a particular chamber or corridor. If you issue no commands, the creature only defends itself against hostile creatures. Once given an order, the creature continues to follow it until its task is complete.\n\nThe creature is under your control for 24 hours, after which it stops obeying any command you've given it. To maintain control of the creature for another 24 hours, you must cast this spell on the creature again before the current 24-hour period ends. This use of the spell reasserts your control over up to four creatures you have animated with this spell, rather than animating a new one."},
  ["spell.animate-dead.xphb2024"]={title="Animate Dead",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nChoose a pile of bones or a corpse of a Medium or Small Humanoid within range. The target becomes an Undead creature: a XMM if you chose bones or a XMM if you chose a corpse.\n\nOn each of your turns, you can take a XPHB to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 60 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). You decide what action the creature will take and where it will move on its next turn, or you can issue a general command, such as to guard a chamber or corridor. If you issue no commands, the creature takes the XPHB action and moves only to avoid harm. Once given an order, the creature continues to follow it until its task is complete.\n\nThe creature is under your control for 24 hours, after which it stops obeying any command you've given it. To maintain control of the creature for another 24 hours, you must cast this spell on the creature again before the current 24-hour period ends. This use of the spell reasserts your control over up to four creatures you have animated with this spell rather than animating a new creature."},
  ["spell.animate-objects.phb2014"]={title="Animate Objects",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nObjects come to life at your command. Choose up to ten nonmagical objects within range that are not being worn or carried. Medium targets count as two objects, Large targets count as four objects, Huge targets count as eight objects. You can't animate any object larger than Huge. Each target animates and becomes a creature under your control until the spell ends or until reduced to 0 hit points.\n\nAs a bonus action, you can mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 500 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any or all of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). You decide what action the creature will take and where it will move during its next turn, or you can issue a general command, such as to guard a particular chamber or corridor. If you issue no commands, the creature only defends itself against hostile creatures. Once given an order, the creature continues to follow it until its task is complete.\n\nSize | HP | AC | Attack | Str | Dex\n\nphb | 20 | 18 | +8 to hit, 1d4 + 4 damage | 4 | 18\n\nphb | 25 | 16 | +6 to hit, 1d8 + 2 damage | 6 | 14\n\nphb | 40 | 13 | +5 to hit, 2d6 + 1 damage | 10 | 12\n\nphb | 50 | 10 | +6 to hit, 2d10 + 2 damage | 14 | 10\n\nphb | 80 | 10 | +8 to hit, 2d12 + 4 damage | 18 | 6\n\nAn animated object is a construct with AC, hit points, attacks, Strength, and Dexterity determined by its size. Its Constitution is 10 and its Intelligence and Wisdom are 3, and its Charisma is 1. Its speed is 30 feet; if the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or a larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0. It has blindsight with a radius of 30 feet and is blind beyond that distance. When the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nIf you command an object to attack, it can make a single melee attack against a creature within 5 feet of it. It makes a slam attack with an attack bonus and bludgeoning damage determined by its size. The DM might rule that a specific object inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form."},
  ["spell.animate-objects.xphb2024"]={title="Animate Objects",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\nObjects animate at your command. Choose a number of nonmagical objects within range that aren't being worn or carried, aren't fixed to a surface, and aren't Gargantuan. The maximum number of objects is equal to your spellcasting ability modifier; for this number, a Medium or smaller target counts as one object, a Large target counts as two, and a Huge target counts as three.\n\nEach target animates, sprouts legs, and becomes a Construct that uses the XPHB stat block; this creature is under your control until the spell ends or until it is reduced to 0 XPHB. Each creature you make with this spell is an ally to you and your allies. In combat, it shares your XPHB count and takes its turn immediately after yours.\n\nUntil the spell ends, you can take a XPHB to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 500 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one). If you issue no commands, the creature takes the XPHB action and moves only to avoid harm. When the creature drops to 0 XPHB, it reverts to its object form, and any remaining damage carries over to that form."},
  ["creature.animated-armor.mm2014"]={title="Animated Armor",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 11 | CON 13 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAntimagic Susceptibility\n\nThe armor is incapacitated while in the area of an antimagic field. If targeted by dispel magic, the armor must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against the caster's spell save DC or fall unconscious for 1 minute.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the armor remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal suit of armor.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe armor makes two melee attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-armor.xmm2024"]={title="Animated Armor",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 16\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 11 | CON 13 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe armor makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-armor-detention-drone.bmt2014"]={title="Animated Armor Detention Drone",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30"},
  ["creature.animated-ballista.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Ballista",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 39\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 50 (50d1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMagic Bolt\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h16 (3d10) fire damage."},
  ["creature.animated-breath.ftd2014"]={title="Animated Breath",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15/17\n\nPV: 95 (10d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Draconic but can't speak\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nChromatic Form\n\nWhen created, the animated breath takes one of five forms, matching its creator's breath weapon: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison. This form determines the creature's AC, damage resistance, traits, and attacks.\n\nFire Aura (Fire Form Only)\n\nAt the start of each of the animated breath's turns, each creature within 5 feet of it takes 3 (1d6) fire damage, and flammable objects in the aura that aren't being worn or carried ignite. A creature that touches the animated breath or hits it with a melee attack takes 3 (1d6) fire damage.\n\nPutrid Aura (Acid and Poison Forms Only)\n\nA creature that starts its turn within 5 feet of the animated breath must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the start of its next turn. A creature that touches the animated breath or hits it with a melee attack takes 3 (1d6) acid damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe animated breath makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 11 (2d10) damage of a type determined by the animated breath's form: acid, cold, fire, lightning, or poison.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nLightning Burst (Lightning Form Only)\n\nThe animated breath magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 30 feet of it. Each creature within 5 feet of the animated breath after it teleports takes 3 (1d6) lightning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-broom.cm2014"]={title="Animated Broom",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 17 (5d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 17 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 5 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Object\n\nIf the broom is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the broom move or act, that creature must succeed on a 15 Wisdom (Perception) check to discern that the broom is animate.\n\nFlyby\n\nThe broom doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe broom makes two melee attacks.\n\nBroomstick\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-broom.xmm2024"]={title="Animated Broom",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 16\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 14 (4d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 17 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 5 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe broom doesn't provoke an XPHB when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-chained-library.cm2014"]={title="Animated Chained Library",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 8 | CON 14 | INT 1 | WIS 5 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Object\n\nIf the library is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the library move or act, that creature must succeed on a 15 Wisdom (Perception) check to discern that the library is animate.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe library makes two attacks.\n\nChained Book\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a creature, it is grappled (escape 12)."},
  ["creature.animated-coffin.aatm2014"]={title="Animated Coffin",subtitle="Criatura - AATM - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 60 (8d10 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (can't see beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the animated coffin is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the coffin move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the coffin is animate.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe animated coffin can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe animated coffin makes two Slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nEntrap\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Large or smaller creature. hThe target has the grappled condition (escape 13). Until this grapple ends, if the target is not an Undead, the target has the restrained condition and takes 14 (4d6) piercing damage at the start of each of its turns. The animated coffin can grapple only one creature at a time."},
  ["creature.animated-drow-statue.oota2014"]={title="Animated Drow Statue",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 96\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental"},
  ["creature.animated-flying-sword.xmm2024"]={title="Animated Flying Sword",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 17\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 14 (4d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 50\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 15 | CON 11 | INT 1 | WIS 5 | CHA 1\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlash\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Slashing damage."},
  ["creature.animated-furniture.coa2014"]={title="Animated Furniture",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 170\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nImunidades: cold, fire, poison, psychic"},
  ["object.animated-ghaunadaur-statue.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Ghaunadaur Statue",subtitle="Objeto - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 250"},
  ["creature.animated-glass-statue.crcotn2014"]={title="Animated Glass Statue",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 109\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 22 (3d10 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 10 | CON 15 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak it\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Sight and Smell\n\nThe statue has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight or smell.\n\nPack Tactics\n\nThe statue has advantage on an attack roll against a creature if at least one of the statue's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe statue makes two attacks: one with its beak and one with its talons.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nTalons\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.animated-halberd.cos2014"]={title="Animated Halberd",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 59\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCA: 15\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHalberd\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d10 + 1) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.animated-jade-serpent.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Jade Serpent",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 92\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned"},
  ["creature.animated-knife.egw2014"]={title="Animated Knife",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 248\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: T\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nPV: 12 (5d4)"},
  ["creature.animated-object.xphb2024"]={title="Animated Object",subtitle="Criatura - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 240\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / T/S/M/L/H\n\nCA: 15\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages you know\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nm Bonus equals your spell attack modifier, reach 5 ft. hForce damage equal to 1d4 + 3, 2d6 + 3 + your spellcasting ability modifier (Large), or 2d12 + 3 + your spellcasting ability modifier (Huge)."},
  ["creature.animated-object-huge.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Huge)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCA: 10\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 6 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (2d12 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-object-large.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Large)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCA: 10\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d10 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-object-medium.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Medium)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCA: 13\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d6 + 1) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-object-small.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Small)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / S\n\nCA: 16\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-object-tiny.phb2014"]={title="Animated Object (Tiny)",subtitle="Criatura - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / T\n\nCA: 18\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 4 | DEX 18 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAnimated\n\nIf the object lacks legs or other appendages it can use for locomotion, it instead has a flying speed of 30 feet and can hover. If the object is securely attached to a surface or larger object, such as a chain bolted to a wall, its speed is 0.\n\nWhen the animated object drops to 0 hit points, it reverts to its original object form, and any remaining damage carries over to its original object form.\n\nThe DM might rule that a specific objects slam attack inflicts slashing or piercing damage based on its form.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-rug-of-smothering.xmm2024"]={title="Animated Rug of Smothering",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 17\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 27 (5d10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSmother\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, the rug can give it the XPHB condition (escape 13) instead of dealing damage. Until the grapple ends, the target has the XPHB and XPHB conditions, is suffocating, and takes 10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of its turns. The rug can smother only one creature at a time.\n\nWhile grappling the target, the rug can't take this action, the rug halves the damage it takes (round down), and the target takes the same amount of damage."},
  ["magicitem.animated-shield.dmg2014"]={title="Animated Shield",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile holding this shield, you can speak its command word as a bonus action to cause it to animate. The shield leaps into the air and hovers in your space to protect you as if you were wielding it, leaving your hands free. The shield remains animated for 1 minute, until you use a bonus action to end this effect, or until you are incapacitated or die, at which point the shield falls to the ground or into your hand if you have one free."},
  ["magicitem.animated-shield.xdmg2024"]={title="Animated Shield",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile holding this Shield, you can take a XPHB to cause it to animate. The Shield leaps into the air and hovers in your space to protect you as if you were wielding it, leaving your hands free. The Shield remains animate for 1 minute, until you take a XPHB to end this effect, or until you die or have the XPHB condition, at which point the Shield falls to the ground or into your hand if you have one free."},
  ["creature.animated-staff.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Staff",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 262\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCA: 17\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 12 | CON 10 | INT 18 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: cold\n\nImunidades: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharm\n\nA creature can grab the staff out of the air with a successful grapple check against the staff, and grappling the staff does not reduce the creature's speed. Any creature that successfully grapples the staff must succeed on a 12 Charisma saving throw or be charmed by the staff until the staff is no longer in its grasp. While the creature is charmed, the staff can issue commands to it, which the creature does its best to obey. The creature can repeat the saving throw each time it takes damage, ending the effect on itself on a success. A creature that successfully resists the staff's control can't be charmed by it for 24 hours.\n\nA creature holding the staff that isn't charmed by it can use an action to attempt to break the staff over a knee or against a solid surface, doing so with a successful 17 Strength (Athletics) check. Breaking the staff in this manner destroys it.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nStaff of Frost\n\nThe staff has 10 charges. It can expend 1 or more of its charges to cast one of the following spells (save 12): cone of cold (5 charges), fog cloud (1 charge), ice storm (4 charges), or wall of ice (4 charges). It regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If the staff expends its last charge, roll a d20. On a 1, the staff turns to water and is destroyed.\n\nMelee Attack\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (2d6) bludgeoning damage plus 1 cold damage."},
  ["creature.animated-statue.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Statue",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 125\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct"},
  ["creature.animated-statue-of-lolth.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Statue of Lolth",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 142\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: H\n\nCR: 11\n\nPV: 230 (20d12 + 100)\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak"},
  ["creature.animated-stove.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Stove",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 186\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 50 (50d1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nBelch Fire {@recharge 4}\n\nThe stove belches fire in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in the area must make a 10 Dexterity saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.animated-table.tftyp2014"]={title="Animated Table",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 230\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 39 (6d10 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 8 | CON 13 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAntimagic Susceptibility\n\nThe table is incapacitated while in the area of an antimagic field. If targeted by dispel magic, the table must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against the caster's spell save DC or fall unconscious for 1 minute.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the table remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal table.\n\nCharge\n\nIf the table moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a ram attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 9 (2d8) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRam\n\nmw 6, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.animated-tile-chimera.rot2014"]={title="Animated Tile Chimera",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nResistencias: piercing\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned"},
  ["creature.animated-tree.egw2014"]={title="Animated Tree",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 130\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nIdiomas: understands Common, Druidic, Elvish, and Sylvan but cannot speak"},
  ["creature.animated-wand.wdmm2014"]={title="Animated Wand",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 299\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.animating-performance.tce2014.bard.creation.6"]={title="Animating Performance",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.animatronic-allosaurus.kftgv2014"]={title="Animatronic Allosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.ankheg.mm2014"]={title="Ankheg",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14/11\n\nPV: 39 (6d10 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 11 | CON 13 | INT 1 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft., tremorsense 60 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) acid damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 13). Until this grapple ends, the ankheg can bite only the grappled creature and has advantage on attack rolls to do so.\n\nAcid Spray {@recharge}\n\nThe ankheg spits acid in a line that is 30 feet long and 5 feet wide, provided that it has no creature grappled. Each creature in that line must make a 13 Dexterity saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.ankheg.wtthc2014"]={title="Ankheg",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.ankheg.xmm2024"]={title="Ankheg",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 18\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 45 (6d10 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 1 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft., Tremorsense 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTunneler\n\nThe ankheg can burrow through solid rock at half its XPHB and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 5 (with XPHB if the target is XPHB by the ankheg), reach 5 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) Acid damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition (escape 13).\n\nAcid Spray {@recharge}\n\ndex 12, each creature in a 30-foot-long, 5-foot-wide XPHB. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Acid damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.ankhtepot.rhw2014"]={title="Ankhtepot",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 88\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 202 (27d8 + 81)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 15 | WIS 20 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDarklord Restoration\n\nIf Ankhtepot dies, he revives with all his XPHB in 1d10 weeks somewhere in Har'Akir.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Domain)\n\nIf Ankhtepot fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nAnkhtepot has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAnkhtepot makes four Negative Energy Burst attacks. He can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB.\n\nNegative Energy Burst\n\nm,r 11, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. h26 (6d6 + 5) Necrotic damage.\n\nTouch of Death {@recharge}\n\nAnkhtepot touches one creature within 5 feet. If the creature has 80 XPHB or fewer, it dies. Otherwise, it takes 52 (8d12) Necrotic damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDeath Strike\n\nAnkhtepot makes one Negative Energy Burst attack.\n\nHand of Fate\n\nstr 19, one Large or smaller creature Ankhtepot can see within 60 feet. actSaveFail 14 (2d8 + 5) Force damage, and the target is pushed or pulled up to 20 feet straight away or toward Ankhtepot. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail Ankhtepot can't take this action again until the start of his next turn.\n\nSands of Time\n\nAnkhtepot teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space he can see. cha 19, each creature in a 10-foot XPHB originating from Ankhtepot at his destination space. actSaveFail 11 (2d10) Necrotic damage, and the target magically ages 10 years. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail Ankhtepot can't take this action again until the start of his next turn."},
  ["creature.ankylosaurus.mm2014"]={title="Ankylosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 79\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 68 (8d12 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.ankylosaurus.xmm2024"]={title="Ankylosaurus",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 348\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 68 (8d12 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 12 | CHA 5\n\nSalvamentos: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ankylosaurus makes two Tail attacks.\n\nTail\n\nm 6, reach 10 ft. h9 (1d10 + 4) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.ankylosaurus-zombie.toa2014"]={title="Ankylosaurus Zombie",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 240\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 68 (8d12 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 9 | CON 15 | INT 2 | WIS 6 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUndead Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the zombie to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5+the damage taken, unless the damage is radiant or from a critical hit. On a success, the zombie drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nTail\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target h18 (4d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone."},
  ["creature.annis-hag.mpmm2014"]={title="Annis Hag",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 47\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: cold\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe annis makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nCrushing Hug\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h36 (9d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 15) if it is a Large or smaller creature. Until the grapple ends, the target takes 36 (9d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage at the start of each of the hag's turns. The hag can't make attacks while grappling a creature in this way."},
  ["creature.annis-hag.vgm2014"]={title="Annis Hag",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 159\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 75 (10d10 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: cold\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe annis makes three attacks: one with her bite and two with her claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nCrushing Hug\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h36 (9d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 15) if it is a Large or smaller creature. Until the grapple ends, the target takes 36 (9d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage at the start of each of the hag's turns. The hag can't make attacks while grappling a creature in this way."},
  ["creature.anointed.psa2014"]={title="Anointed",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["spell.antagonize.bmt2014"]={title="Antagonize",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\nYou whisper magical words that antagonize one creature of your choice within range. The target must make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the target takes 4d4 psychic damage and must immediately use its reaction to make a melee attack against another creature of your choice that you can see. If the target can't make this attack (for example, because there is no one within its reach or because its reaction is unavailable), the target instead has disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the start of your next turn. On a successful save, the target takes half as much damage only."},
  ["background.anthropologist.toa2014"]={title="Anthropologist",subtitle="Background - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 191\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nCultural Chameleon\n\nBefore becoming an adventurer, you spent much of your adult life away from your homeland, living among people different from your kin. You came to understand these foreign cultures and the ways of their people, who eventually treated you as one of their own. One culture had more of an influence on you than any other, shaping your beliefs and customs. Choose a race whose culture you've adopted, or roll on the Adopted Culture table.\n\nd8 | Culture\n\n1 | Aarakocra\n\n2 | Dwarf\n\n3 | Elf\n\n4 | Goblin\n\n5 | Halfling\n\n6 | Human\n\n7 | Lizardfolk\n\n8 | Orc\n\nFeature: Adept Linguist\n\nYou can communicate with humanoids who don't speak any language you know. You must observe the humanoids interacting with one another for at least 1 day, after which you learn a handful of important words, expressions, and gestures - enough to communicate on a rudimentary level.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nAnthropologists leave behind the societies into which they were born to discover what life is like in other parts of the world. They seek to see how other races and civilizations survive - or why they did not. Some anthropologists are driven by intellectual curiosity, while others want the fame and recognition that comes with being the first to discover a new people, a lost tribe, or the truth about an ancient empire's downfall.\n\nd6 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I prefer the company of those who aren't like me, including people of other races\n\n2 | I'm a stickler when it comes to observing proper etiquette and local customs\n\n3 | I would rather observe than meddle\n\n4 | By living among violent people, I have become desensitized to violence.\n\n5 | I would risk life and limb to discover a new culture or unravel the secrets of a dead one.\n\n6 | When I arrive at a new settlement for the first time, I must learn all its customs.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Discovery. I want to be the first person to discover a lost culture. (Any)\n\n2 | Distance. One must not interfere with the affairs of another culture - even one in need of aid. (Lawful)\n\n3 | Knowledge. By understanding other races and cultures, we learn to understand ourselves. (Any)\n\n4 | Power. Common people crave strong leadership, and I do my utmost to provide it. (Lawful)\n\n5 | Protection. I must do everything possible to save a society facing extinction. (Good)\n\n6 | Indifferent. Life is cruel. What's the point in saving people if they're going to die anyway? (Chaotic)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | My mentor gave me a journal filled with lore and wisdom. Losing it would devastate me.\n\n2 | Having lived among the people of a primeval tribe or clan, I long to return and see how they are faring.\n\n3 | Years ago, tragedy struck the members of an isolated society I befriended, and I will honor them.\n\n4 | I want to learn more about a particular humanoid culture that fascinates me.\n\n5 | I seek to avenge a clan, tribe, kingdom, or empire that was wiped out.\n\n6 | I have a trinket that I believe is the key to finding a long-lost society.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | Boats make me seasick.\n\n2 | I talk to myself, and I don't make friends easily.\n\n3 | I believe that I'm intellectually superior to people from other cultures and have much to teach them.\n\n4 | I've picked up some unpleasant habits living among goblins, lizardfolk, or orcs.\n\n5 | I complain about everything.\n\n6 | I wear a tribal mask and never take it off."},
  ["item.antigravity-belt.qftis2014"]={title="Antigravity Belt",subtitle="Item - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\nRaridade: none\n\nMetal tubes ring the lower edge of this wide belt. It is powered by an energy cell stored in a metal case near the buckle. Placing a full energy cell in the belt gives the belt 10 charges.\n\nActivating the Belt\n\nAs a bonus action, you can expend any number of the belt's charges to activate it; the belt remains active for 1 minute per charge expended. You can use a bonus action to deactivate the belt early, but doing so doesn't recover any expended charges.\n\nWhen you activate the belt, and as a bonus action while it remains active, you can rise or descend vertically up to 20 feet. You remain floating in place while the property is active, and you can move yourself horizontally by being pushed or towed or by scooting yourself along a surface, such as a wall or ceiling, at half your walking speed. If you are still levitating when the belt deactivates, you fall.\n\nReplacing the Energy Cell\n\nWhile the belt has charges remaining, its energy cell can't be removed. Once the belt has 0 charges, you can replace the energy cell with a new cell by using an action or a bonus action."},
  ["spell.antilife-shell.phb2014"]={title="Antilife Shell",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nA shimmering barrier extends out from you in a 10-foot radius and moves with you, remaining centered on you and hedging out creatures other than undead and constructs. The barrier lasts for the duration.\n\nThe barrier prevents an affected creature from passing or reaching through. An affected creature can cast spells or make attacks with ranged or reach weapons through the barrier.\n\nIf you move so that an affected creature is forced to pass through the barrier, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.antilife-shell.xphb2024"]={title="Antilife Shell",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 241\n\nAn aura extends from you in a 10-foot XPHB for the duration. The aura prevents creatures other than Constructs and Undead from passing or reaching through it. An affected creature can cast spells or make attacks with Ranged or Reach weapons through the barrier.\n\nIf you move so that an affected creature is forced to pass through the barrier, the spell ends."},
  ["spell.antimagic-field.phb2014"]={title="Antimagic Field",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nA 10-foot-radius invisible sphere of antimagic surrounds you. This area is divorced from the magical energy that suffuses the multiverse. Within the sphere, spells can't be cast, summoned creatures disappear, and even magic items become mundane. Until the spell ends, the sphere moves with you, centered on you.\n\nSpells and other magical effects, except those created by an artifact or a deity, are suppressed in the sphere and can't protrude into it. A slot expended to cast a suppressed spell is consumed. While an effect is suppressed, it doesn't function, but the time it spends suppressed counts against its duration.\n\nTargeted Effects\n\nSpells and other magical effects, such as magic missile and charm person, that target a creature or an object in the sphere have no effect on that target.\n\nAreas of Magic\n\nThe area of another spell or magical effect, such as fireball, can't extend into the sphere. If the sphere overlaps an area of magic, the part of the area that is covered by the sphere is suppressed. For example, the flames created by a wall of fire are suppressed within the sphere, creating a gap in the wall if the overlap is large enough.\n\nSpells\n\nAny active spell or other magical effect on a creature or an object in the sphere is suppressed while the creature or object is in it.\n\nMagic Items\n\nThe properties and powers of magic items are suppressed in the sphere. For example, a +1 longsword in the sphere functions as a nonmagical longsword.\n\nA magic weapon's properties and powers are suppressed if it is used against a target in the sphere or wielded by an attacker in the sphere. If a magic weapon or a piece of magic ammunition fully leaves the sphere (for example, if you fire a magic arrow or throw a magic spear at a target outside the sphere), the magic of the item ceases to be suppressed as soon as it exits.\n\nMagical Travel\n\nTeleportation and planar travel fail to work in the sphere, whether the sphere is the destination or the departure point for such magical travel. A portal to another location, world, or plane of existence, as well as an opening to an extradimensional space such as that created by the rope trick spell, temporarily closes while in the sphere.\n\nCreatures and Objects\n\nA creature or object summoned or created by magic temporarily winks out of existence in the sphere. Such a creature instantly reappears once the space the creature occupied is no longer within the sphere.\n\nDispel Magic\n\nSpells and magical effects such as dispel magic have no effect on the sphere. Likewise, the spheres created by different antimagic field spells don't nullify each other."},
  ["spell.antimagic-field.xphb2024"]={title="Antimagic Field",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 241\n\nAn aura of antimagic surrounds you in a 10-foot XPHB. No one can cast spells, take XPHB actions, or create other magical effects inside the aura, and those things can't target or otherwise affect anything inside it. Magical properties of magic items don't work inside the aura or on anything inside it.\n\nAreas of effect created by spells or other magic can't extend into the aura, and no one can teleport into or out of it or use planar travel there. Portals close temporarily while in the aura.\n\nOngoing spells, except those cast by an Artifact or a deity, are suppressed in the area. While an effect is suppressed, it doesn't function, but the time it spends suppressed counts against its duration.\n\nXPHB has no effect on the aura, and the auras created by different XPHB spells don't nullify each other."},
  ["item.antimatter-rifle.dmg2014"]={title="Antimatter Rifle",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.antimatter-rifle.xdmg2024"]={title="Antimatter Rifle",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 73\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["spell.antipathy-sympathy.phb2014"]={title="Antipathy/Sympathy",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nThis spell attracts or repels creatures of your choice. You target something within range, either a Huge or smaller object or creature or an area that is no larger than a 200-foot cube. Then specify a kind of intelligent creature, such as red dragons, goblins, or vampires. You invest the target with an aura that either attracts or repels the specified creatures for the duration. Choose antipathy or sympathy as the aura's effect.\n\nAntipathy\n\nThe enchantment causes creatures of the kind you designated to feel an intense urge to leave the area and avoid the target. When such a creature can see the target or comes within 60 feet of it, the creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become frightened. The creature remains frightened while it can see the target or is within 60 feet of it. While frightened by the target, the creature must use its movement to move to the nearest safe spot from which it can't see the target. If the creature moves more than 60 feet from the target and can't see it, the creature is no longer frightened, but the creature becomes frightened again if it regains sight of the target or moves within 60 feet of it.\n\nSympathy\n\nThe enchantment causes the specified creatures to feel an intense urge to approach the target while within 60 feet of it or able to see it. When such a creature can see the target or comes within 60 feet of it, the creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or use its movement on each of its turns to enter the area or move within reach of the target. When the creature has done so, it can't willingly move away from the target.\n\nIf the target damages or otherwise harms an affected creature, the affected creature can make a Wisdom saving throw to end the effect, as described below.\n\nEnding the Effect\n\nIf an affected creature ends its turn while not within 60 feet of the target or able to see it, the creature makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the creature is no longer affected by the target and recognizes the feeling of repugnance or attraction as magical. In addition, a creature affected by the spell is allowed another Wisdom saving throw every 24 hours while the spell persists.\n\nA creature that successfully saves against this effect is immune to it for 1 minute, after which time it can be affected again."},
  ["spell.antipathy-sympathy.xphb2024"]={title="Antipathy/Sympathy",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 8 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nAs you cast the spell, choose whether it creates antipathy or sympathy, and target one creature or object that is Huge or smaller. Then specify a kind of creature, such as red dragons, goblins, or vampires. A creature of the chosen kind makes a Wisdom saving throw when it comes within 120 feet of the target. Your choice of antipathy or sympathy determines what happens to a creature when it fails that save:\n\n• Antipathy The creature has the XPHB condition. The XPHB creature must use its movement on its turns to get as far away as possible from the target, moving by the safest route.\n\n• Sympathy The creature has the XPHB condition. The XPHB creature must use its movement on its turns to get as close as possible to the target, moving by the safest route. If the creature is within 5 feet of the target, the creature can't willingly move away. If the target damages the XPHB creature, that creature can make a Wisdom saving throw to end the effect, as described below.\n\nEnding the Effect\n\nIf the XPHB or XPHB creature ends its turn more than 120 feet away from the target, the creature makes a Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the creature is no longer affected by the target. A creature that successfully saves against this effect is immune to it for 1 minute, after which it can be affected again."},
  ["item.antitoxin.xphb2024"]={title="Antitoxin",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs a XPHB, you can drink a vial of Antitoxin to gain XPHB on saving throws to avoid or end the XPHB condition for 1 hour."},
  ["item.antitoxin-vial.phb2014"]={title="Antitoxin (vial)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA creature that drinks this vial of liquid gains advantage on saving throws against poison for 1 hour. It confers no benefit to undead or constructs."},
  ["deity.anubis.phb2014"]={title="Anubis",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["charoption.anvilwrought.mot2014"]={title="Anvilwrought",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\nYou were forged in the fires of Purphoros's forge. Your appearance bears a metallic sheen and visible joints. The Anvilwrought Characteristics table suggests details of your life or origins. Additionally, you gain the following traits.\n\nConstructed Resilience\n\nYou were created to have remarkable fortitude, represented by the following benefits:\n\n• You have advantage on saving throws against being poisoned, and you have resistance to poison damage.\n\n• You don't need to eat, drink, or breathe.\n\n• You are immune to disease.\n\n• You don't need to sleep, and magic can't put you to sleep.\n\nSentry's Rest\n\nWhen you take a long rest, you must spend at least six hours in an inactive, motionless state, rather than sleeping. In this state, you appear inert, but it doesn't render you unconscious, and you can see and hear as normal.\n\nd6 | Characteristic\n\n1 | An oread who works in Purphoros's forge is the closest thing I have to a parent.\n\n2 | Purphoros made me to serve him.\n\n3 | I was created decades ago and, fearing that I'm growing obsolete, recently fled Mount Velus.\n\n4 | Purphoros regrets my creation and wants to reforge me into something better.\n\n5 | Purphoros intended me to carry on his work by making even greater creations of my own.\n\n6 | Someone in Mount Velus implanted a terrible secret within me in order to smuggle it out into the world."},
  ["creature.anvilwrought-raptor.mot2014"]={title="Anvilwrought Raptor",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / T\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 18 (4d4 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 14 | INT 3 | WIS 14 | CHA 1\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands one language of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Sight\n\nThe raptor has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nRecorded Mimicry\n\nThe raptor can mimic any sound, including voices, it has heard in the last 24 hours. A creature that hears the sounds can tell they are imitations with a successful 12 Wisdom (Insight) check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe raptor makes two attacks with its beak.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.ape.mm2014"]={title="Ape",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 317\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ape makes two fist attacks.\n\nFist\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 25/50 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.ape.xmm2024"]={title="Ape",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 348\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 14 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ape makes two Fist attacks.\n\nFist\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock {@recharge}\n\nr 5, range 25/50 ft. h10 (2d6 + 3) Bludgeoning damage."},
  ["deity.apep.phb2014"]={title="Apep",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["creature.aphemia.mot2014"]={title="Aphemia",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 226\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 52 (8d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 50\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nIf Aphemia fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nAphemia has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAphemia makes two attacks: one with her bite and one with her claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (2d4 + 3) piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) necrotic damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nDiscordant Song\n\nAphemia shrieks a cacophony of magical sounds. Each humanoid within 120 feet of her must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened of her until the song ends. A frightened creature takes 7 (2d6) psychic damage at the start of its turn while Aphemia is singing. A frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to Aphemia's Discordant Song for the next 24 hours. Aphemia must take a bonus action on her subsequent turns to continue singing. She can stop singing at any time. The song ends if Aphemia is incapacitated or dies.\n\nGrave Calling Song\n\nAphemia intones a low, growling magical melody. Every undead within 300 feet of her must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or fall under her control until the song ends. Aphemia must take a bonus action on her subsequent turns to continue singing, and she can mentally command the undead under her control as part of the same bonus action. She can stop singing at any time. The song ends if Aphemia is incapacitated or dies."},
  ["deity.aphrodite.phb2014"]={title="Aphrodite",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["deity.apollo.phb2014"]={title="Apollo",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["magicitem.apparatus-of-kwalish.dmg2014"]={title="Apparatus of Kwalish",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis item first appears to be a Large sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. The barrel has a hidden catch, which can be found with a successful 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check. Releasing the catch unlocks a hatch at one end of the barrel, allowing two Medium or smaller creatures to crawl inside. Ten levers are set in a row at the far end, each in a neutral position, able to move either up or down. When certain levers are used, the apparatus transforms to resemble a giant lobster.\n\nThe apparatus of Kwalish is a Large object with the following statistics:\n\n• Armor Class:\n\n• Hit Points:\n\n• Speed:\n\n• Damage Immunities:\n\nTo be used as a vehicle, the apparatus requires one pilot. While the apparatus's hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight. The compartment holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.\n\nThe apparatus floats on water. It can also go underwater to a depth of 900 feet. Below that, the vehicle takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage per minute from pressure.\n\nA creature in the compartment can use an action to move as many as two of the apparatus's levers up or down. After each use, a lever goes back to its neutral position. Each lever, from left to right, functions as shown in the Apparatus of Kwalish Levers table.\n\nLever | Up | Down\n\n1 | Legs and tail extend, allowing the apparatus to walk and swim. | Legs and tail retract, reducing the apparatus's speed to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bonuses to speed.\n\n2 | Forward window shutter opens. | Forward window shutter closes.\n\n3 | Side window shutters open (two per side). | Side window shutters close (two per side).\n\n4 | Two claws extend from the front sides of the apparatus. | The claws retract.\n\n5 | Each extended claw makes the following melee weapon attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h 7 (2d6) bludgeoning damage. | Each extended claw makes the following melee weapon attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h The target is grappled (escape 15).\n\n6 | The apparatus walks or swims forward. | The apparatus walks or swims backward.\n\n7 | The apparatus turns 90 degrees left. | The apparatus turns 90 degrees right.\n\n8 | Eyelike fixtures emit bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. | The light turns off.\n\n9 | The apparatus sinks as much as 20 feet in liquid. | The apparatus rises up to 20 feet in liquid.\n\n10 | The rear hatch unseals and opens. | The rear hatch closes and seals."},
  ["vehicle.apparatus-of-kwalish.dmg2014"]={title="Apparatus of Kwalish",subtitle="Veiculo - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nThis item first appears to be a Large sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. The barrel has a hidden catch, which can be found with a successful 20 Intelligence (Investigation) check. Releasing the catch unlocks a hatch at one end of the barrel, allowing two Medium or smaller creatures to crawl inside. Ten levers are set in a row at the far end, each in a neutral position, able to move either up or down. When certain levers are used, the apparatus transforms to resemble a giant lobster.\n\nTo be used as a vehicle, the apparatus requires one pilot. While the apparatus's hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight. The compartment holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.\n\nThe apparatus floats on water. It can also go underwater to a depth of 900 feet. Below that, the vehicle takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage per minute from pressure.\n\nA creature in the compartment can use an action to move as many as two of the apparatus's levers up or down. After each use, a lever goes back to its neutral position. Each lever, from left to right, functions as shown in the Apparatus of Kwalish Levers table.\n\nLever | Up | Down\n\n1 | Legs and tail extend, allowing the apparatus to walk and swim. | Legs and tail retract, reducing the apparatus's speed to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bonuses to speed.\n\n2 | Forward window shutter opens. | Forward window shutter closes.\n\n3 | Side window shutters open (two per side). | Side window shutters close (two per side).\n\n4 | Two claws extend from the front sides of the apparatus. | The claws retract.\n\n5 | Each extended claw makes the following melee weapon attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h 7 (2d6) bludgeoning damage. | Each extended claw makes the following melee weapon attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h The target is grappled (escape 15).\n\n6 | The apparatus walks or swims forward. | The apparatus walks or swims backward.\n\n7 | The apparatus turns 90 degrees left. | The apparatus turns 90 degrees right.\n\n8 | Eyelike fixtures emit bright light in a 30-foot radius and dim light for an additional 30 feet. | The light turns off.\n\n9 | The apparatus sinks as much as 20 feet in liquid. | The apparatus rises up to 20 feet in liquid.\n\n10 | The rear hatch unseals and opens. | The rear hatch closes and seals."},
  ["magicitem.apparatus-of-kwalish.xdmg2024"]={title="Apparatus of Kwalish",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis item first appears to be a sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. The barrel has a hidden catch, which can be found with a successful 20 Intelligence (XPHB) check. Releasing the catch unlocks a hatch at one end of the barrel, allowing two Medium or smaller creatures to crawl inside. Ten levers are set in a row at the far end, each in a neutral position, able to move up or down. When certain levers are used, the apparatus transforms to resemble a giant lobster.\n\nThe Apparatus of Kwalish is a Large object with the following statistics: AC 20; HP 200; Speed 30 ft., Swim 30 ft. (or 0 ft. for both if the legs aren't extended); Immunity to Poison and Psychic damage.\n\nTo be used as a vehicle, the apparatus requires one pilot. While the apparatus's hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight. The compartment holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.\n\nThe apparatus floats on water. It can also go underwater to a depth of 900 feet. Below that, the vehicle takes 2d6 Bludgeoning damage each minute from pressure.\n\nA creature in the compartment can take a XPHB action to move as many as two of the apparatus's levers up or down. After each use, a lever goes back to its neutral position. Each lever, from left to right, functions as shown in the Apparatus of Kwalish Levers table.\n\nLever | Up | Down\n\n1 | Legs extend, allowing the apparatus to walk and swim. | Legs retract, reducing the apparatus's XPHB and XPHB to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bonuses to speed.\n\n2 | Forward window shutter opens. | Forward window shutter closes.\n\n3 | Side window shutters open (two per side). | Side window shutters close (two per side).\n\n4 | Two claws extend from the front side of the apparatus. | The claws retract.\n\n5 | Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. Hit: 7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage. | Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. Hit: The target has the XPHB condition (escape 15).\n\n6 | The apparatus walks or swims forward provided its legs are extended. | The apparatus walks or swims backward provided its legs are extended.\n\n7 | The apparatus turns 90 degrees counterclockwise provided its legs are extended. | The apparatus turns 90 degrees clockwise provided its legs are extended.\n\n8 | Eyelike fixtures emit XPHB in a 30-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 30 feet. | The light turns off.\n\n9 | The apparatus sinks up to 20 feet if it's in liquid. | The apparatus rises up to 20 feet if it's in liquid.\n\n10 | The rear hatch unseals and opens. | The rear hatch closes and seals."},
  ["vehicle.apparatus-of-kwalish.xdmg2024"]={title="Apparatus of Kwalish",subtitle="Veiculo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 229\n\nThis item first appears to be a sealed iron barrel weighing 500 pounds. The barrel has a hidden catch, which can be found with a successful 20 Intelligence (XPHB) check. Releasing the catch unlocks a hatch at one end of the barrel, allowing two Medium or smaller creatures to crawl inside. Ten levers are set in a row at the far end, each in a neutral position, able to move up or down. When certain levers are used, the apparatus transforms to resemble a giant lobster.\n\nTo be used as a vehicle, the apparatus requires one pilot. While the apparatus's hatch is closed, the compartment is airtight and watertight. The compartment holds enough air for 10 hours of breathing, divided by the number of breathing creatures inside.\n\nThe apparatus floats on water. It can also go underwater to a depth of 900 feet. Below that, the vehicle takes 2d6 Bludgeoning damage each minute from pressure.\n\nA creature in the compartment can take a XPHB action to move as many as two of the apparatus's levers up or down. After each use, a lever goes back to its neutral position. Each lever, from left to right, functions as shown in the Apparatus of Kwalish Levers table.\n\nLever | Up | Down\n\n1 | Legs extend, allowing the apparatus to walk and swim. | Legs retract, reducing the apparatus's XPHB and XPHB to 0 and making it unable to benefit from bonuses to speed.\n\n2 | Forward window shutter opens. | Forward window shutter closes.\n\n3 | Side window shutters open (two per side). | Side window shutters close (two per side).\n\n4 | Two claws extend from the front side of the apparatus. | The claws retract.\n\n5 | Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. h7 (2d6) Bludgeoning damage. | Each extended claw makes the following melee attack: 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. hThe target has the XPHB condition (escape 15).\n\n6 | The apparatus walks or swims forward provided its legs are extended. | The apparatus walks or swims backward provided its legs are extended.\n\n7 | The apparatus turns 90 degrees counterclockwise provided its legs are extended. | The apparatus turns 90 degrees clockwise provided its legs are extended.\n\n8 | Eyelike fixtures emit XPHB in a 30-foot radius and XPHB for an additional 30 feet. | The light turns off.\n\n9 | The apparatus sinks up to 20 feet if it's in liquid. | The apparatus rises up to 20 feet if it's in liquid.\n\n10 | The rear hatch unseals and opens. | The rear hatch closes and seals."},
  ["creature.apprentice.hol2014"]={title="Apprentice",subtitle="Criatura - HoL - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 7 (2d8 - 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 10 | CON 9 | INT 13 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nQuarterstaff\n\nmw 1 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h2 (1d6 - 1) bludgeoning damage, or 3 (1d8 - 1) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands.\n\nBurning Hands (1st-Level Spell; 2/Day)\n\nYou shoot forth a 15-foot cone of fire. Each creature in that area must make a 11 Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 10 (3d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one The fire ignites any flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried.\n\nFire Bolt (Cantrip)\n\nrs Ranged Spell Attack: 3 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h5 (1d10) fire damage. A flammable object hit by this spell ignites if it isn't being worn or carried."},
  ["creature.apprentice-wizard.mpmm2014"]={title="Apprentice Wizard",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 259\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10/13\n\nPV: 13 (3d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nArcane Burst\n\nms,rs 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) force damage."},
  ["creature.apprentice-wizard.vgm2014"]={title="Apprentice Wizard",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h2 (1d4) piercing damage."},
  ["item.aquamarine.dmg2014"]={title="Aquamarine",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent pale blue-green gemstone."},
  ["item.aquamarine.xdmg2024"]={title="Aquamarine",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA pale blue green gemstone."},
  ["feature.aquatic-affinity.xphb2024.druid.sea.6"]={title="Aquatic Affinity",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 87\n\nThe size of the XPHB created by your Wrath of the Sea increases to 10 feet.\n\nIn addition, you gain a XPHB equal to your XPHB."},
  ["creature.aquatic-ghoul.pota2014"]={title="Aquatic Ghoul",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 87\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30"},
  ["creature.aquatic-troll.rot2014"]={title="Aquatic Troll",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nResistencias: cold"},
  ["creature.arabelle.cos2014"]={title="Arabelle",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nPV: 2 (1d8)"},
  ["creature.aradrine-the-owl.crcotn2014"]={title="Aradrine the Owl",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["deity.araleth-letheranil.mtf2014"]={title="Araleth Letheranil",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["creature.aranea.fraif2014"]={title="Aranea",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 250\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 17 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb (Hybrid or Spider Form Only)\n\nThe aranea can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe aranea ignores movement restrictions caused by webs, and it knows the location of any other creature in contact with the same web.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe aranea makes two attacks, using Bite, Slam, or Sling in any combination.\n\nBite (Hybrid or Spider Form Only)\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage plus 2 (1d4) Poison damage.\n\nSlam\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nSling (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nr 5, range 30/120 ft. h8 (2d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nThe aranea shape-shifts into a humanoid form, into a humanoid-spider hybrid form, or back into its true spider form. Its game statistics are the same in each form, except where noted. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed."},
  ["creature.arasta.mot2014"]={title="Arasta",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 248\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 300 (24d12 + 144)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 16 | CON 23 | INT 15 | WIS 22 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nArmor of Spiders (Mythic Trait; Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf Arasta is reduced to 0 hit points, she doesn't die or fall unconscious. Instead, she regains 200 hit points. In addition, Arasta's children immediately swarm over her body to protect her, granting her 100 temporary hit points.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Arasta fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nArasta has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nArasta can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nArasta ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nArasta makes three attacks: one with her bite and two with her claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h20 (3d8 + 7) piercing damage, and the target must make a 21 Constitution saving throw, taking 32 (5d12) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If the damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target is stable but poisoned for 1 hour, even after regaining hit points, and is paralyzed while poisoned in this way.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h17 (3d6 + 7) slashing damage.\n\nWeb of Hair {@recharge 4}\n\nArasta unleashes her hair in the form of webbing that fills a 30-foot cube next to her. The web is difficult terrain, its area is lightly obscured, and it lasts for 1 minute. Any creature that moves into the web or that starts its turn there must make a 21 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature is restrained while in the web. A creature can use an action to make a 21 Strength check. On a success, it can free itself or a creature within 5 feet of it that is restrained by the web. This webbing is immune to all damage except magical fire. A 5-foot cube of the web is destroyed if it takes at least 20 fire damage from a spell or other magical source on a single turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaws\n\nArasta makes one attack with her claws.\n\nSwarm (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nArasta causes two swarm of spiders to appear in unoccupied spaces within 5 feet of her.\n\nToxic Web (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nEach creature restrained by Arasta's Web of Hair takes 18 (4d8) poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES MITICAS ===\n\nSwipe\n\nArasta makes two attacks with her claws.\n\nWeb of Hair (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nArasta recharges Web of Hair and uses it.\n\nNyx Weave (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nEach creature restrained by Arasta's Web of Hair must succeed on a 21 Constitution saving throw, or the creature takes 26 (4d12) force damage and any spell of 6th level or lower on it ends."},
  ["deity.arawai.erlw2014"]={title="Arawai",subtitle="Divindade - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 141\n\nArawai is the Sovereign of Life and Love. She is the patron of fertility and of the benevolent aspects of nature, bringing good harvest and gentle rain."},
  ["deity.arawai.phb2014"]={title="Arawai",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["deity.arawn.phb2014"]={title="Arawn",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["subclass.arcana-domain.au2014.cleric.arcana.0"]={title="Arcana Domain",subtitle="Subclasse - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 8"},
  ["feature.arcana-domain.au2014.cleric.arcana.3"]={title="Arcana Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nAmplify Your Magical Power\n\nMagic suffuses the multiverse and fuels both destruction and creation. Clerics with the Arcana Domain view magical knowledge not as power to be used in pursuit of personal ends, but as a gift they have the responsibility to share.\n\nGods associated with the Arcana Domain know the secrets and potential of magic intimately. These gods are often connected to knowledge, secrecy, or power."},
  ["subclass.arcana-domain.scag2014.cleric.arcana.0"]={title="Arcana Domain",subtitle="Subclasse - SCAG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.arcana-domain.scag2014.cleric.arcana.1"]={title="Arcana Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 125\n\nMagic is an energy that suffuses the multiverse and that fuels both destruction and creation. Gods of the Arcana domain know the secrets and potential of magic intimately. For some of these gods, magical knowledge is a great responsibility that comes with a special understanding of the nature of reality. Other gods of Arcana see magic as pure power, to be used as its wielder sees fit.\n\nThe gods of this domain are often associated with knowledge, as learning and arcane power tend to go hand-in-hand. In the Realms, deities of this domain include Faerûnian and Faerûnian, as well as Elven of the elven pantheon. In other worlds, this domain includes Greek, Celtic, and Egyptian; the triple moon gods of Dragonlance, Dragonlance, and Dragonlance of Krynn; and Greyhawk, Greyhawk, and Greyhawk of Greyhawk.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared. They do not count towards your limit.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | detect magic, magic missile\n\n3rd | magic weapon, Nystul's magic aura\n\n5th | dispel magic, magic circle\n\n7th | arcane eye, Leomund's secret chest\n\n9th | planar binding, teleportation circle"},
  ["feature.arcana-domain.scag2014.cleric.arcana.3"]={title="Arcana Domain",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.arcana-domain-spells.au2014.cleric.arcana.3"]={title="Arcana Domain Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nYour connection to this divine domain means you always have certain spells ready. When you reach a Cleric level specified in the Arcana Domain Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Prepared Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["creature.arcanaloth.mm2014"]={title="Arcanaloth",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 313\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 104 (16d8 + 32)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 20 | WIS 16 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe arcanaloth has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe arcanaloth's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (2d4 + 3) slashing damage. The target must make a 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nTeleport\n\nThe arcanaloth magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["creature.arcanaloth.xmm2024"]={title="Arcanaloth",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 19\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 175 (27d8 + 54)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 20 | WIS 16 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFiendish Restoration\n\nIf the arcanaloth dies outside Gehenna, its body dissolves into ichor, and it gains a new body instantly and revives with all its XPHB in Gehenna.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe arcanaloth has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSoul Tome\n\nThe arcanaloth has a magic tome. While holding or carrying the tome, the arcanaloth can use its Banishing Claw action.\n\nThe tome has AC 17; HP 35; and XPHB to Necrotic, Poison, and Psychic damage. The tome regains all its XPHB at the end of every turn, but it turns to dust if reduced to 0 XPHB or when the arcanaloth dies. If the tome is destroyed, the arcanaloth can create a new one when it finishes a XPHB or XPHB.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nCounterspell\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe arcanaloth makes three Fiendish Burst attacks. It can replace one attack with a Banishing Claw attack.\n\nFiendish Burst\n\nm,r 9, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h31 (4d12 + 5) Necrotic damage.\n\nBanishing Claw (Requires Soul Tome)\n\nm 9, reach 5 ft. h10 (2d4 + 5) Slashing damage plus 19 (3d12) Psychic damage. If the target is a creature, it is subjected to the following effect. cha 17. actSaveFail The target is trapped in a demiplane inside the Soul Tome. While trapped there, the target has the XPHB condition. At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the save, escaping the tome on a success. When the target escapes, it appears in the space it left or, if that space is occupied, the nearest unoccupied space.\n\nIf the target fails three of these saves while in the demiplane, it becomes bound to the tome and can escape only if the tome is reduced to 0 XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTeleport\n\nThe arcanaloth teleports up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space it can see."},
  ["magicitem.arcanaloth-s-music-box.toa2014"]={title="Arcanaloth's Music Box",subtitle="Item Magico - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 188\n\nRaridade: unknown (magic)\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nThis music box is made of dark wood with gold filigree. Each of its five sides is sculpted with the image of a horned woman playing a different PHB: a PHB, a PHB, a harp, a PHB, and a PHB. While touching the box, you can use an action to make it play music featuring one of the instruments shown, which can be heard up to 60 feet away. You can also use an action to stop the music."},
  ["feature.arcane-abeyance.egw2014.wizard.chronurgy.10"]={title="Arcane Abeyance",subtitle="Caracteristica - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 184\n\n10th-level Chronurgy Magic feature\n\nWhen you cast a spell using a spell slot of 4th level or lower, you can condense the spell's magic into a mote. The spell is frozen in time at the moment of casting and held within a gray bead for 1 hour. This bead is a Tiny object with AC 15 and 1 hit point, and it is immune to poison and psychic damage. When the duration ends, or if the bead is destroyed, it vanishes in a flash of light, and the spell is lost.\n\nA creature holding the bead can use its action to release the spell within, whereupon the bead disappears. The spell uses your spell attack bonus and save DC, and the spell treats the creature who released it as the caster for all other purposes.\n\nOnce you create a bead with this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a short or long rest."},
  ["feature.arcane-apotheosis.xphb2024.sorcerer.base.20"]={title="Arcane Apotheosis",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 141\n\nWhile your Innate Sorcery feature is active, you can use one Metamagic option on each of your turns without spending Sorcery Points on it."},
  ["subclass.arcane-archer.au2014.fighter.arcane-archer.0"]={title="Arcane Archer",subtitle="Subclasse - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-archer.au2014.fighter.arcane-archer.3"]={title="Arcane Archer",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nDeploy Magical Effects Through Enchanted Ammunition\n\nAn Arcane Archer studies a unique elven method of archery that weaves magic into attacks to produce supernatural effects. Over the centuries, other folk have learned this technique and broadened it so it applies to ranged weapons of many kinds and to aspects of adventuring life outside of combat."},
  ["subclass.arcane-archer.xge2024.fighter.arcane-archer.0"]={title="Arcane Archer",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-archer.xge2024.fighter.arcane-archer.3"]={title="Arcane Archer",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 28\n\nAn Arcane Archer studies a unique elven method of archery that weaves magic into attacks to produce supernatural effects. Arcane Archers are some of the most elite warriors among the elves. They stand watch over the fringes of elven domains, keeping a keen eye out for trespassers and using magic-infused arrows to defeat monsters and invaders before they can reach elven settlements. Over the centuries, the methods of these elf archers have been learned by members of other races who can also balance arcane aptitude with archery."},
  ["feature.arcane-archer-lore.au2014.fighter.arcane-archer.3"]={title="Arcane Archer Lore",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nYou learn magical theory and secrets of nature, granting you the following benefits.\n\nCantrip\n\nYou know either the XPHB or the XPHB cantrip. Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for it.\n\nSkills\n\nYou gain proficiency in the XPHB and XPHB skills. If you already have one of these proficiencies, you instead gain proficiency in a different skill of your choice from the skills available to Fighters at level 1 (or in two skills available to Fighters at level 1 if you have both)."},
  ["feature.arcane-archer-lore.xge2024.fighter.arcane-archer.3"]={title="Arcane Archer Lore",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-armor.efa2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Arcane Armor",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nAs a XPHB action while you have XPHB in hand, you can turn a suit of armor you are wearing into Arcane Armor. The armor continues to be Arcane Armor until you don another suit of armor or you die.\n\nYou gain the following benefits while wearing your Arcane Armor.\n\nNo Strength Requirement\n\nIf the armor normally has a Strength requirement, the Arcane Armor lacks this requirement for you.\n\nQuick Don and Doff\n\nYou can don or doff the armor as a XPHB action. The armor can't be removed against your will.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use the Arcane Armor as a XPHB for your Artificer spells."},
  ["feature.arcane-armor.tce2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Arcane Armor",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n3rd-level Armorer feature\n\nYour metallurgical pursuits have led to you making armor a conduit for your magic. As an action, you can turn a suit of armor you are wearing into Arcane Armor, provided you have PHB in hand.\n\nYou gain the following benefits while wearing this armor:\n\n• If the armor normally has a Strength requirement, the arcane armor lacks this requirement for you.\n\n• You can use the arcane armor as a spellcasting focus for your artificer spells.\n\n• The armor attaches to you and can't be removed against your will. It also expands to cover your entire body, although you can retract or deploy the helmet as a bonus action. The armor replaces any missing limbs, functioning identically to a limb it replaces.\n\n• You can doff or don the armor as an action. The armor continues to be Arcane Armor until you don another suit of armor or you die."},
  ["feat.arcane-artist.au2014"]={title="Arcane Artist",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCantrip\n\nYou learn the XPHB cantrip. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nInspiring Magic\n\nWhen you cast a spell from the Illusion school, you can choose one ally within 30 feet of yourself who can see you. That ally gains XPHB. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.arcane-battery.nf2014"]={title="Arcane Battery",subtitle="Item Magico - NF - 2014",body="Raridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis smooth, oval stone is etched with faintly glowing, magical symbols. While holding the battery, you can take a XPHB action to touch the battery to one magic item. If that magic item normally regains expended charges daily, it immediately regains 1d4 + 1 expended charges, and the battery loses its magic."},
  ["magicitem.arcane-cannon.egw2014"]={title="Arcane Cannon",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 265\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis Large cannon is imbued with magic. It requires no ammunition and doesn't need to be loaded. It takes one action to aim the cannon and one action to fire it. After the cannon has fired, it must recharge for 5 minutes before it can be fired again.\n\nThe creature firing the cannon chooses the effect from the following options:\n\nAcid Jet\n\nThe cannon discharges acid in a line 300 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. In addition, a creature that fails its saving throw takes 11 (2d10) acid damage at the start of each of its turns; a creature can end this damage by using its action to wash off the acid with a pint or more of water.\n\nFire Jet\n\nThe cannon discharges fire in a line 300 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in the area must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 33 (6d10) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The fire ignites any flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried.\n\nFrost Shot\n\nThe cannon shoots a ball of frost to a point you can see within 1,200 feet of the cannon. The ball then expands to form a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on that point. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 22 (4d10) cold damage, and its speed is reduced by 10 feet for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage, and its speed isn't reduced. A creature whose speed is reduced by this effect can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nLightning Shot\n\nThe cannon shoots a ball of lightning to a point you can see within 1,200 feet of the cannon. The lightning then expands to form a 20-foot-radius sphere centered on that point. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 33 (6d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Creatures wearing metal armor have disadvantage on the save.\n\nPoison Spray\n\nThe cannon expels poison gas in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 22 (4d10) poison damage and is poisoned for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't poisoned. A creature poisoned in this way can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["feature.arcane-charge.phb2014.fighter.eldritch-knight.15"]={title="Arcane Charge",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-charge.xphb2024.fighter.eldritch-knight.15"]={title="Arcane Charge",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 98\n\nWhen you use your Action Surge, you can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. You can teleport before or after the additional action."},
  ["magicitem.arcane-chatelaine.au2014"]={title="Arcane Chatelaine",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis ornate clasp has six spectral keys attached to it. As a XPHB action, you can touch one of the keys to a closed door, window, gate, container, or hatch to cast the XPHB spell on it. Once a key is used, it disappears. When all six keys have disappeared, the chatelaine disappears."},
  ["feature.arcane-dabbler.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.wu-jen.6"]={title="Arcane Dabbler",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nAt 6th level, you learn three wizard spells of your choice and always have them prepared. The spells must be of spells.\n\nAs a bonus action, you can spend psi points to create spell slots that you can use to cast these spells, as well as other spells you are capable of casting. The psi-point cost of each spell slot is detailed on the table below.\n\nSpell Slot Level | Psi Cost\n\n1st | 2\n\n2nd | 3\n\n3rd | 5\n\n4th | 6\n\n5th | 7\n\nThe spell slot remains until you use it or finish a long rest. You must observe your psi limit when spending psi points to create a spell slot.\n\nWhenever you gain a level in this class, you can replace one of the chosen wizard spells with a different spells."},
  ["feature.arcane-deflection.xge2024.wizard.war.2"]={title="Arcane Deflection",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 59\n\nAt 2nd level, you have learned to weave your magic to fortify yourself against harm. When you are hit by an attack or you fail a saving throw, you can use your reaction to gain a +2 bonus to your AC against that attack or a +4 bonus to that saving throw.\n\nWhen you use this feature, you can't cast spells other than cantrips until the end of your next turn."},
  ["traphazard.arcane-effluence.nf2014"]={title="Arcane Effluence",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - NF - 2014",body="Spoiled potions, broken magic items, or runoff from magical workshops can pollute waterways, creating a sludge called arcane effluence. While many Low Netherese individuals recognize the effluence's peculiar violet sheen, careless High Netherese mages usually don't even know such pollution exists.\n\nOne patch of arcane effluence covers a 5-foot square, and creatures within 30 feet of it can smell its acrid, unnatural scent. A creature that comes into contact with arcane effluence takes 3 (1d6) Acid damage. The creature takes the damage again at the start of each of its turns until the effluence is scraped off (requiring an action) or destroyed.\n\nThe XPHB spell or a similar effect destroys arcane effluence."},
  ["feat.arcane-eloquence.au2014"]={title="Arcane Eloquence",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCantrip\n\nYou learn the XPHB cantrip. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nSmooth Talker\n\nWhen you make a Charisma (XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB) check, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check."},
  ["spell.arcane-eye.phb2014"]={title="Arcane Eye",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nYou create an invisible, magical eye within range that hovers in the air for the duration.\n\nYou mentally receive visual information from the eye, which has normal vision and darkvision out to 30 feet. The eye can look in every direction.\n\nAs an action, you can move the eye up to 30 feet in any direction. There is no limit to how far away from you the eye can move, but it can't enter another plane of existence. A solid barrier blocks the eye's movement, but the eye can pass through an opening as small as 1 inch in diameter."},
  ["spell.arcane-eye.xphb2024"]={title="Arcane Eye",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 4 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nYou create an XPHB, invulnerable eye within range that hovers for the duration. You mentally receive visual information from the eye, which can see in every direction. It also has XPHB with a range of 30 feet.\n\nAs a XPHB, you can move the eye up to 30 feet in any direction. A solid barrier blocks the eye's movement, but the eye can pass through an opening as small as 1 inch in diameter."},
  ["feature.arcane-firearm.efa2014.artificer.artillerist.5"]={title="Arcane Firearm",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB, you can use XPHB to carve special sigils into a XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or items and thereby turn it into your Arcane Firearm. The sigils disappear from the object if you later carve them on a different item. The sigils otherwise last indefinitely.\n\nYou can use your Arcane Firearm as a XPHB for your Artificer spells. When you cast an Artificer spell through the firearm, roll 1d8, and you gain a bonus to one of the spell's damage rolls equal to the number rolled."},
  ["feature.arcane-firearm.tce2014.artificer.artillerist.5"]={title="Arcane Firearm",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["spell.arcane-gate.phb2014"]={title="Arcane Gate",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 214\n\nYou create linked teleportation portals that remain open for the duration. Choose two points on the ground that you can see, one point within 10 feet of you and one point within 500 feet of you. A circular portal, 10 feet in diameter, opens over each point. If the portal would open in the space occupied by a creature, the spell fails, and the casting is lost.\n\nThe portals are two-dimensional glowing rings filled with mist, hovering inches from the ground and perpendicular to it at the points you choose. A ring is visible only from one side (your choice), which is the side that functions as a portal.\n\nAny creature or object entering the portal exits from the other portal as if the two were adjacent to each other; passing through a portal from the nonportal side has no effect. The mist that fills each portal is opaque and blocks vision through it. On your turn, you can rotate the rings as a bonus action so that the active side faces in a different direction."},
  ["spell.arcane-gate.xphb2024"]={title="Arcane Gate",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nYou create linked teleportation portals. Choose two Large, unoccupied spaces on the ground that you can see, one space within range and the other one within 10 feet of you. A circular portal opens in each of those spaces and remains for the duration.\n\nThe portals are two-dimensional glowing rings filled with mist that blocks sight. They hover inches from the ground and are perpendicular to it.\n\nA portal is open on only one side (you choose which). Anything entering the open side of a portal exits from the open side of the other portal as if the two were adjacent to each other. As a XPHB, you can change the facing of the open sides."},
  ["feat.arcane-infiltrator.au2014"]={title="Arcane Infiltrator",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCantrip\n\nYou learn the XPHB cantrip. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nCunning Diversion\n\nYou can take the XPHB action as a XPHB. You can use this benefit a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feature.arcane-initiate.scag2014.cleric.arcana.1"]={title="Arcane Initiate",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-jolt.efa2014.artificer.battle-smith.9"]={title="Arcane Jolt",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nWhen either you hit a target with an attack roll using a magic weapon or your EFA hits a target, you can channel magical energy through the strike to create one of the following effects:\n\n• Destructive Energy The target takes an extra 2d6 Force damage.\n\n• Restorative Energy Choose one creature or object you can see within 30 feet of the target. Healing energy flows into the chosen recipient, restoring 2d6 XPHB to it.\n\nYou can use this energy a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), but you can do so no more than once per turn. You regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feature.arcane-jolt.tce2014.artificer.battle-smith.9"]={title="Arcane Jolt",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 18\n\nAt 9th level, you learn new ways to channel arcane energy to harm or heal. When either you hit a target with a magic weapon attack or your steel defender hits a target, you can channel magical energy through the strike to create one of the following effects:\n\n• The target takes an extra 2d6 force damage.\n\n• Choose one creature or object you can see within 30 feet of the target. Healing energy flows into the chosen recipient, restoring 2d6 hit points to it.\n\nYou can use this energy a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), but you can do so no more than once on a turn. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["spell.arcane-lock.phb2014"]={title="Arcane Lock",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\nYou touch a closed door, window, gate, chest, or other entryway, and it becomes locked for the duration. You and the creatures you designate when you cast this spell can open the object normally. You can also set a password that, when spoken within 5 feet of the object, suppresses this spell for 1 minute. Otherwise, it is impassable until it is broken or the spell is dispelled or suppressed. Casting knock on the object suppresses arcane lock for 10 minutes.\n\nWhile affected by this spell, the object is more difficult to break or force open; the DC to break it or pick any locks on it increases by 10."},
  ["spell.arcane-lock.xphb2024"]={title="Arcane Lock",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nYou touch a closed door, window, gate, container, or hatch and magically lock it for the duration. This lock can't be unlocked by any nonmagical means. You and any creatures you designate when you cast the spell can open and close the object despite the lock. You can also set a password that, when spoken within 5 feet of the object, unlocks it for 1 minute."},
  ["feature.arcane-mastery.scag2014.cleric.arcana.17"]={title="Arcane Mastery",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 125\n\nAt 17th level, you choose four spells from the Wizard spell list, one from each of the following levels: 6th, 7th, 8th, and 9th. You add them to your list of domain spells. Like your other domain spells, they are always prepared and count as cleric spells for you."},
  ["feat.arcane-omens.au2014"]={title="Arcane Omens",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCantrip\n\nYou learn the XPHB cantrip. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nHelpful Premonition\n\nWhen you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of yourself fails a saving throw, you can take a XPHB to roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the save's total, potentially turning the failure into a success. You can use this benefit a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feat.arcane-overload.au2014"]={title="Arcane Overload",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCantrip\n\nYou learn the XPHB cantrip. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nPower Surge\n\nWhen you cast an Evocation spell and deal damage with it, you can add your XPHB to one damage roll of that spell. Once you use this benefit, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["magicitem.arcane-propulsion-arm.erlw2014"]={title="Arcane Propulsion Arm",subtitle="Item Magico - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis prosthetic appendage was developed by artificers of House Cannith. To attune to this item, you must attach it to your arm at the wrist, elbow, or shoulder, at which point the prosthetic magically forms a copy of the appendage it's replacing.\n\nWhile attached, the prosthetic provides these benefits:\n\n• The prosthetic is a fully capable part of your body.\n\n• You can take an action to remove the prosthetic, and it removes itself if your attunement to it ends. It can't be removed against your will.\n\n• The prosthetic is a magic melee weapon with which you're proficient. It deals 1d8 force damage on a hit and has the thrown property, with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. When thrown, the prosthetic detaches and flies at the target of the attack, then immediately returns to you and reattaches."},
  ["optionalfeature.arcane-propulsion-armor.tce2014"]={title="Arcane Propulsion Armor",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nThe wearer of this armor gains these benefits:\n\n• The wearer's walking speed increases by 5 feet.\n\n• The armor includes gauntlets, each of which is a magic melee weapon that can be wielded only when the hand is holding nothing. The wearer is proficient with the gauntlets, and each one deals 1d8 force damage on a hit and has the thrown property, with a normal range of 20 feet and a long range of 60 feet. When thrown, the gauntlet detaches and flies at the attack's target, then immediately returns to the wearer and reattaches.\n\n• The armor can't be removed against the wearer's will.\n\n• If the wearer is missing any limbs, the armor replaces those limbs—hands, arms, feet, legs, or similar appendages. The replacements function identically to the body parts they replace."},
  ["feature.arcane-recovery.phb2014.wizard.base.1"]={title="Arcane Recovery",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nYou have learned to regain some of your magical energy by studying your spellbook. Once per day when you finish a short rest, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level that is equal to or less than half your wizard level (rounded up), and none of the slots can be 6th level or higher.\n\nFor example, if you're a 4th-level wizard, you can recover up to two levels worth of spell slots. You can recover either a 2nd-level spell slot or two 1st-level spell slots."},
  ["feature.arcane-recovery.xphb2024.wizard.base.1"]={title="Arcane Recovery",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nYou can regain some of your magical energy by studying your spellbook. When you finish a XPHB, you can choose expended spell slots to recover. The spell slots can have a combined level equal to no more than half your Wizard level (round up), and none of the slots can be level 6 or higher. For example, if you're a level 4 Wizard, you can recover up to two levels' worth of spell slots, regaining either one level 2 spell slot or two level 1 spell slots.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["feat.arcane-safeguard.au2014"]={title="Arcane Safeguard",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCantrip\n\nYou learn the XPHB cantrip. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat). You can cast the XPHB cantrip as a XPHB. You can do so a number of times equal to your XPHB, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nSheltering Aid\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action to assist with an ally's ability check, that ally gains a number of XPHB equal to your XPHB."},
  ["feature.arcane-shot.au2014.fighter.arcane-archer.3"]={title="Arcane Shot",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-shot.xge2024.fighter.arcane-archer.3"]={title="Arcane Shot",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-shot-options.au2014.fighter.arcane-archer.3"]={title="Arcane Shot Options",subtitle="Caracteristica - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\nThe Arcane Shot feature lets you choose options for it at certain levels. The options are presented here in alphabetical order."},
  ["feature.arcane-shot-options.xge2024.fighter.arcane-archer.3"]={title="Arcane Shot Options",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Arcane shots are all magical effects, and each one is associated with one of the schools of magic.\n\nIf an option requires a saving throw, your Arcane Shot save DC is calculated as follows:\n\nArcane Shot"},
  ["reward.arcane-study-charm.xdmg2024"]={title="Arcane Study Charm",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 336\n\nAfter spending a XPHB in your XDMG, you gain a magical Charm (see \"XDMG\" in XDMG) that lasts for 7 days or until you use it. The Charm allows you to cast XPHB without expending a spell slot or using Material components. You can't gain this Charm again while you still have it."},
  ["feature.arcane-tradition.phb2014.wizard.base.2"]={title="Arcane Tradition",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nWhen you reach 2nd level, you choose an arcane tradition from the list of available traditions, shaping your practice of magic. Your choice grants you features at 2nd level and again at 6th, 10th, and 14th level."},
  ["feature.arcane-tradition-feature.phb2014.wizard.base.6"]={title="Arcane Tradition feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nAt 6th level, you gain a feature granted by your Arcane Tradition."},
  ["feature.arcane-tradition-feature.phb2014.wizard.base.10"]={title="Arcane Tradition feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nAt 10th level, you gain a feature granted by your Arcane Tradition."},
  ["feature.arcane-tradition-feature.phb2014.wizard.base.14"]={title="Arcane Tradition feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nAt 14th level, you gain a feature granted by your Arcane Tradition."},
  ["subclass.arcane-trickster.phb2014.rogue.arcane-trickster.0"]={title="Arcane Trickster",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-trickster.phb2014.rogue.arcane-trickster.3"]={title="Arcane Trickster",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 97\n\nSome rogues enhance their fine-honed skills of stealth and agility with magic, learning tricks of enchantment and illusion. These rogues include pickpockets and burglars, but also pranksters, mischief-makers, and a significant number of adventurers."},
  ["subclass.arcane-trickster.xphb2024.rogue.arcane-trickster.0"]={title="Arcane Trickster",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-trickster.xphb2024.rogue.arcane-trickster.3"]={title="Arcane Trickster",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 132\n\nEnhance Stealth with Arcane Spells\n\nSome Rogues enhance their fine-honed skills of stealth and agility with spells, learning magical tricks to aid them in their trade. Some Arcane Tricksters use their talents as pickpockets and burglars, while others are pranksters."},
  ["feat.arcane-undertaker.au2014"]={title="Arcane Undertaker",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nCantrip\n\nYou learn one Cleric or Wizard cantrip of your choice. The cantrip must be from the Necromancy school. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for this spell (choose when you select this feat).\n\nKnowledge from the Dead\n\nWhen you make an Intelligence (XPHB) or Wisdom (XPHB) check, you can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to the ability check.\n\nUnderstanding of Death\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action to stabilize a creature with 0 XPHB, you gain XPHB. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB."},
  ["spell.arcane-vigor.xphb2024"]={title="Arcane Vigor",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 242\n\nYou tap into your life force to heal yourself. Roll one or two of your unexpended XPHB, and regain a number of XPHB equal to the roll's total plus your spellcasting ability modifier. Those dice are then expended."},
  ["feature.arcane-ward.phb2014.wizard.abjuration.2"]={title="Arcane Ward",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.arcane-ward.xphb2024.wizard.abjurer.3"]={title="Arcane Ward",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["feat.arcane-warrior.au2014"]={title="Arcane Warrior",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\nYou learn two Wizard cantrips of your choice. XPHB and XPHB are recommended. Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma is your spellcasting ability for these spells (choose when you select this feat).\n\nWhenever you gain a level, you can replace one of these cantrips with another Wizard cantrip."},
  ["magicitem.arcanist-s-bestiary.au2014"]={title="Arcanist's Bestiary",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nHundreds of pages of illustrations, tables, and diagrams about a wide variety of monsters fill this magical tome.\n\nCharm Monster\n\nWhile holding the book, you can cast the XPHB spell (spell save 15) from it. The target has XPHB on the saving throw against this spell if it isn't a Humanoid. You can't cast this spell again in this way until the next dawn.\n\nExtensive Knowledge\n\nWhen you become attuned to the book, you gain proficiency in one of the following skills of your choice: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB. Whenever you finish a XPHB, you can change your choice. If your XPHB to the book ends, you lose this proficiency.\n\nMonster Primer\n\nWhile carrying the book, whenever you take a XPHB action to make an Intelligence (XPHB) check to recall information about an Aberration, Construct, Elemental, Fey, or Monstrosity you can see, on a successful check, you learn whether that creature has any Immunities, Resistances, or Vulnerabilities. If the creature has any, you know what they are."},
  ["creature.arch-hag.xmm2024"]={title="Arch-hag",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / L\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 333 (29d10 + 174)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 15 | CON 23 | INT 19 | WIS 19 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day, or 5/Day in Lair)\n\nIf the hag fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe hag has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSpiteful Escape\n\nWhen the hag drops to 0 XPHB, it dies only if it is within 30 feet of its anathema (a thing the DM chooses as the hag's most hated thing). Otherwise, the hag drops to 1 XPHB and teleports to a harmless demiplane, and it can't return to the plane it left for 2d6 days. When the hag teleports away, each creature within 60 feet of the space it left is cursed. Until the curse ends, a creature has XPHB on ability checks and saving throws, and the hag knows its location anywhere in the multiverse.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nCoven Magic\n\nSpellcasting\n\nTongue Twister\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe hag makes two Spectral Claw attacks and uses Crackling Wave.\n\nSpectral Claw\n\nm,r 14, reach 10 ft. or range 60 ft. h17 (3d6 + 7) Force damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it has the XPHB condition.\n\nCrackling Wave\n\ndex 22, each creature in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 32 (5d12) Lightning damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage. actSaveSuccessOrFail The target is cursed until the end of the hag's next turn. The target can't take Reactions until the curse ends.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nWitch Strike\n\nEach creature cursed by the hag and within 60 feet of it takes 14 (4d6) Lightning damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nHag's Swipe\n\nThe hag makes one Spectral Claw attack.\n\nMalicious Magic\n\nThe hag uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB or XPHB. The hag can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["background.archaeologist.efa2014"]={title="Archaeologist",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["background.archaeologist.toa2014"]={title="Archaeologist",subtitle="Background - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nDust Digger\n\nPrior to becoming an adventurer, you spent most of your young life crawling around in the dust, pilfering relics of questionable value from crypts and ruins. Though you managed to sell a few of your discoveries and earn enough coin to buy proper adventuring gear, you have held onto an item that has great emotional value to you. Roll on the Signature Item table to see what you have, or choose an item from the table.\n\nd8 | Item\n\n1 | phb\n\n2 | phb\n\n3 | Hat\n\n4 | phb\n\n5 | Medallion\n\n6 | phb\n\n7 | phb\n\n8 | phb\n\nFeature: Historical Knowledge\n\nWhen you enter a ruin or dungeon, you can correctly ascertain its original purpose and determine its builders, whether those were dwarves, elves, humans, yuan-ti, or some other known race. In addition, you can determine the monetary value of art objects more than a century old.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nFew archaeologists can resist the lure of an unexplored ruin or dungeon, particularly if such a site is the source of legends or is rumored to contain the treasures and relics of wizards, warlords, or royalty. Some archaeologists plunder for wealth or fame, while others consider it their calling to illuminate the past or keep the world's greatest treasures from falling into the wrong hands. Whatever their motivations, archaeologists combine the qualities of a scrappy historian with the self-made heroism of a treasure-hunting scoundrel.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I love a good puzzle or mystery\n\n2 | I'm a pack rat who never throws anything away.\n\n3 | Fame is more important to me than money.\n\n4 | I have no qualms about stealing from the dead.\n\n5 | I'm happier in a dusty old tomb than I am in the centers of civilization.\n\n6 | Traps don't make me nervous. Idiots who trigger traps make me nervous.\n\n7 | I might fail, but I will never give up.\n\n8 | You might think I'm a scholar, but I love a good brawl. These fists were made for punching.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Preservation. That artifact belongs in a museum. (Good)\n\n2 | Greed. I won't risk my life for nothing. I expect some kind of payment. (Any)\n\n3 | Death Wish. Nothing is more exhilarating than a narrow escape from the jaws of death. (Chaotic)\n\n4 | Dignity. The dead and their belongings deserve to be treated with respect. (Lawful)\n\n5 | Immortality. All of my exploring is part of a plan to find the secret of everlasting life. (Any)\n\n6 | Danger. With every great discovery comes grave danger. The two walk hand in hand. (Any)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | Ever since I was a child, I've heard stories about a lost city. I aim to find it, learn its secrets, and earn my place in the history books.\n\n2 | I want to find my mentor, who disappeared on an expedition some time ago.\n\n3 | I have a friendly rival. Only one of us can be the best, and I aim to prove it's me.\n\n4 | I won't sell an art object or other treasure that has historical significance or is one of a kind.\n\n5 | I'm secretly in love with the wealthy patron who sponsors my archaeological exploits.\n\n6 | I hope to bring prestige to a library, a museum, or a university.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | I have a secret fear of some common wild animal - and in my work, I see them everywhere.\n\n2 | I can't leave a room without searching it for secret doors.\n\n3 | When I'm not exploring dungeons or ruins, I get jittery and impatient.\n\n4 | I have no time for friends or family. I spend every waking moment thinking about and preparing for my next expedition.\n\n5 | When given the choice of going left or right, I always go left.\n\n6 | I can't sleep except in total darkness."},
  ["creature.archaic.scc2014"]={title="Archaic",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 184\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / G\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 245 (14d20 + 98)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 24 | INT 27 | WIS 24 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nResistencias: force\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEnigmatic Mind\n\nThe archaic's mind can't be read, creatures can communicate telepathically with the archaic only if it allows, and magic can't determine whether the archaic is lying.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the archaic fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe archaic doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archaic makes two Force Strike attacks. It can also use Gravity Shift, if available.\n\nForce Strike\n\nms,rs 14 to hit, reach 15 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h19 (2d10 + 8) force damage, and the target is pulled up to 10 feet toward the archaic or pushed 10 feet away from it, as the archaic chooses.\n\nGravity Shift {@recharge 5}\n\nThe archaic reverses gravity for one creature it can see within 100 feet of itself. The creature must succeed on a 22 Wisdom saving throw or fall 100 feet upward. If the falling creature encounters a solid object (such as a ceiling) in this fall, it strikes the object just as it would during a downward fall. If the creature reaches the top of the area without striking anything, it hovers there until the start of the archaic's next turn, at which time gravity returns to normal and the creature falls.\n\nTeleport\n\nThe archaic teleports to an unoccupied space that it can see within 120 feet of itself.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSpell Mimicry (1/Day)\n\nImmediately after a creature the archaic can see casts a spell of 5th level or lower, that creature must succeed on a 22 Charisma saving throw, or the archaic immediately casts the same spell at the same level (14 to hit with spell attacks, spell save 22), requiring no material components and choosing the spell's targets.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nStrike\n\nThe archaic makes one Force Strike attack.\n\nTeleport\n\nThe archaic uses Teleport.\n\nUnravel Magic (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe archaic targets one creature it can see within 120 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 22 Constitution saving throw or take 35 (10d6) force damage, and each spell of 5th level or lower on the target ends."},
  ["creature.archdruid.mpmm2014"]={title="Archdruid",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 154 (28d8 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 20 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Druidic plus any two languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archdruid makes three Staff or Wildfire attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nStaff\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage plus 21 (6d6) poison damage.\n\nWildfire\n\nrs 9 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h26 (6d6 + 5) fire damage, and the target is blinded until the start of the druid's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape (2/Day)\n\nThe archdruid magically transforms into a Beast or an Elemental with a challenge rating of 6 or less and can remain in that form for up to 9 hours. The archdruid can choose whether its equipment falls to the ground, melds with its new form, or is worn by the new form. The archdruid reverts to its true form if it dies or falls unconscious. The archdruid can revert to its true form using a bonus action.\n\nWhile in a new form, the archdruid's stat block is replaced by the stat block of that form, except the archdruid keeps its current hit points, its hit point maximum, this bonus action, its languages and ability to speak, and its Spellcasting action.\n\nThe new form's attacks count as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistances and immunity to nonmagical attacks."},
  ["feature.archdruid.phb2014.druid.base.20"]={title="Archdruid",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 64\n\nAt 20th level, you can use your Wild Shape an unlimited number of times.\n\nAdditionally, you can ignore the verbal and somatic components of your druid spells, as well as any material components that lack a cost and aren't consumed by a spell. You gain this benefit in both your normal shape and your beast shape from Wild Shape."},
  ["creature.archdruid.vgm2014"]={title="Archdruid",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 132 (24d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 20 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Druidic plus any two languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nChange Shape (2/Day)\n\nThe archdruid magically polymorphs into a beast or elemental with a challenge rating of 6 or less, and can remain in this form for up to 9 hours. The archdruid can choose whether its equipment falls to the ground, melds with its new form, or is worn by the new form. The archdruid reverts to its true form if it dies or falls unconscious. The archdruid can revert to its true form using a bonus action on its turn.\n\nWhile in a new form, the archdruid retains its game statistics and ability to speak, but its AC, movement modes, Strength, and Dexterity are replaced by those of the new form, and it gains any special senses, proficiencies, traits, actions, and reactions (except class features, legendary actions, and lair actions) that the new form has but that it lacks. It can cast its spells with verbal or somatic components in its new form.\n\nThe new form's attacks count as magical for the purpose of overcoming resistances and immunity to nonmagical attacks."},
  ["feature.archdruid.xphb2024.druid.base.20"]={title="Archdruid",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.archduke-zariel-of-avernus.bgdia2014"]={title="Archduke Zariel of Avernus",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nResistencias: fire, radiant\n\nImunidades: cold, necrotic, poison"},
  ["creature.archelon.xmm2024"]={title="Archelon",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 349\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 90 (12d12 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 80\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 4 | WIS 14 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe archelon can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archelon makes two Bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h14 (3d6 + 4) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.archer.mpmm2014"]={title="Archer",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 49\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archer makes two Shortsword or Longbow attacks.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nArcher's Eye (3/Day)\n\nImmediately after making an attack roll or a damage roll with a ranged weapon, the archer can roll a d10 and add the number rolled to the total."},
  ["feature.archer.tce2014.druid.stars.2"]={title="Archer",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nA constellation of an archer appears on you. When you activate this form, and as a bonus action on your subsequent turns while it lasts, you can make a ranged spell attack, hurling a luminous arrow that targets one creature within 60 feet of you. On a hit, the attack deals radiant damage equal to 1d8 + your Wisdom modifier."},
  ["creature.archer.vgm2014"]={title="Archer",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nArcher's Eye (3/Day)\n\nAs a bonus action, the archer can add 1d10 to its next attack or damage roll with a longbow or shortbow.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archer makes two attacks with its longbow.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage."},
  ["feature.archer.xphb2024.druid.stars.3"]={title="Archer",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.archery.phb2014"]={title="Archery",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls you make with ranged weapons."},
  ["feat.archery.xphb2024"]={title="Archery",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 209\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls you make with Ranged weapons."},
  ["subclass.archfey-patron.xphb2024.warlock.archfey.0"]={title="Archfey Patron",subtitle="Subclasse - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 159"},
  ["feature.archfey-patron.xphb2024.warlock.archfey.3"]={title="Archfey Patron",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 159\n\nBargain with Whimsical Fey\n\nYour pact draws on the power of the Feywild. When you choose this subclass, you might make a deal with an archfey, such as the Prince of Frost; the Queen of Air and Darkness, ruler of the Gloaming Court; Titania of the Summer Court; or an ancient hag. Or you might call on a spectrum of Fey, weaving a web of favors and debts. Whoever they are, your patron is often inscrutable and whimsical."},
  ["feature.archfey-spells.xphb2024.warlock.archfey.3"]={title="Archfey Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 159\n\nThe magic of your patron ensures you always have certain spells ready; when you reach a Warlock level specified in the Archfey Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nWarlock Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n7 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["creature.archfiend-of-ifnir.psa2014"]={title="Archfiend of Ifnir",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.archmage.mm2014"]={title="Archmage",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 342\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 99 (18d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 20 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any six languages\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe archmage has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.archmage.xmm2024"]={title="Archmage",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 199\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 170 (31d8 + 31)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 20 | WIS 15 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus five other languages\n\nImunidades: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe archmage has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nMisty Step (3/Day)\n\nProtective Magic (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archmage makes four Arcane Burst attacks.\n\nArcane Burst\n\nm,r 9, reach 5 ft. or range 150 ft. h27 (4d10 + 5) Force damage."},
  ["creature.archon-of-boundaries.mcv4ec2014"]={title="Archon of Boundaries",subtitle="Criatura - MCV4EC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 195 (17d12 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 90\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 17 | CON 20 | INT 14 | WIS 18 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common and Celestial but can't speak\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the archon fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe archon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archon makes one Hooves attack and one Radiant Lance attack.\n\nHooves\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h20 (4d6 + 6) bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) radiant damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 19 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nRadiant Lance\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (1d12 + 6) piercing damage plus 28 (8d6) radiant damage, and the target is marked until the start of the archon's next turn. While it is marked, the target has disadvantage on attack rolls against creatures other than the archon.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nArchon's Pursuit\n\nWhen a creature marked by the archon's Radiant Lance ends its turn within 120 feet of the archon, the archon teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 5 feet of the creature.\n\nHaunting Radiance\n\nImmediately after a creature within 120 feet of the archon forces it to make a saving throw, the archon responds with a burst of light. The creature must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or have the blinded condition until the end of the creature's next turn.\n\nParry\n\nThe archon adds 5 to its AC against one melee attack that would hit it, provided it can see the attacker."},
  ["creature.archon-of-falling-stars.mot2014"]={title="Archon of Falling Stars",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 144 (17d8 + 68)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 19 | INT 15 | WIS 21 | CHA 19\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nImunidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe archon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMount\n\nIf the archon isn't mounted, it can use a bonus action to magically teleport onto the creature serving as its mount, provided the archon and its mount are on the same plane of existence. When it teleports, the archon appears astride the mount, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying. While mounted and not incapacitated, the archon can't be surprised, and both it and its mount have advantage on Dexterity saving throws. If the archon is reduced to 0 hit points while riding its mount, the mount is reduced to 0 hit points as well.\n\nRadiant Rebirth (Recharges after a Long Rest)\n\nIf the archon is reduced to 0 hit points, it regains 30 hit points and springs back to its feet with a burst of radiance. Each creature of the archon's choice within 30 feet of it must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw, or the creature takes 13 (3d8) radiant damage and is blinded until the start of the archon's turn.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archon makes two attacks with its radiant spear.\n\nRadiant Spear\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) radiant damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe archon makes a radiant spear attack or casts guiding bolt.\n\nCoordinated Assault (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe archon makes a radiant spear attack, and then its mount can use its reaction to make a melee weapon attack.\n\nReturn to Nyx (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe archon causes a corpse it can see within 30 feet of it to burst into a shower of radiant stars leaving no trace of it behind. Everything it is wearing or carrying remains. Each creature within 10 feet of the corpse when it bursts must succeed on a 16 Dexterity saving throw or take 22 (4d10) radiant damage."},
  ["creature.archon-of-redemption.psz2014"]={title="Archon of Redemption",subtitle="Criatura - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 22\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 136 (16d8 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 90\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 18 | CON 18 | INT 17 | WIS 20 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAngelic Weapons\n\nThe archon's weapon attacks are magical. When the archon hits with any weapon, the weapon deals an extra 3d8 radiant damage (included in the attack).\n\nAxiomatic Mind\n\nThe archon can't be compelled to act in a manner contrary to its nature or its understanding of justice.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe archon has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nOne Being\n\nThough it appears as a humanoid creature riding a mount, an archon is a single being. The \"rider\" can't be dismounted, and no other means can separate the two portions of the archon's being short of its death.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archon makes two attacks: one with its sword and one with its claws.\n\nSword\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) radiant damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) radiant damage."},
  ["creature.archon-of-the-triumvirate.ggr2014"]={title="Archon of the Triumvirate",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / M\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 144 (17d8 + 68)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 19 | INT 15 | WIS 21 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEye of the Law\n\nAs a bonus action, the archon can target a creature it can see within 120 feet of it and determine which laws that creature has broken in the last 24 hours.\n\nMount\n\nIf the archon isn't mounted, it can use a bonus action to magically teleport onto the creature serving as its mount, provided the archon and its mount are on the same plane of existence. When it teleports, the archon appears astride the mount along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying. While mounted and not incapacitated, the archon can't be surprised, and both it and its mount gain advantage on Dexterity saving throws. If the archon is reduced to 0 hit points while riding its mount, the mount is reduced to 0 hit points as well.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archon makes two Hammer of Justice attacks.\n\nHammer of Justice\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) force damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 18 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nPacifying Presence\n\nEach creature of the archon's choice that the archon can see within 120 feet of it must succeed on a 18 Wisdom saving throw, or else the target drops any weapons it is holding, ends its concentration on any spells or other effects, and becomes charmed by the archon for 1 minute. The charmed creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. If a creature's saving throw is successful or the effect ends for it, the creature is immune to the archon's Pacifying Presence for the next 24 hours.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nRejoin Mount\n\nIf the archon isn't mounted, it magically teleports to its steed and mounts it as long as the archon and its steed are on the same plane of existence.\n\nSmite (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe archon makes a Hammer of Justice attack, and then its mount can use its reaction to make a melee weapon attack.\n\nDetention (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe archon targets a creature it can see within 60 feet of it. The target must succeed on a 18 Charisma saving throw or be magically teleported to a harmless demiplane until the end of the archon's next turn, whereupon the target reappears in the space it left or the nearest unoccupied space if that space is occupied."},
  ["creature.archpriest.xmm2024"]={title="Archpriest",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 248\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 240 (32d8 + 96)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 14 | WIS 21 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus two other languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nDivine Aid (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe archpriest makes three Radiant Burst attacks.\n\nRadiant Burst\n\nm,r 9, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. h27 (4d10 + 5) Radiant damage.\n\nHoly Word {@recharge 4}\n\nwis 17, each enemy in a 20-foot XPHB originating from the archpriest. actSaveFail 21 (6d6) Radiant damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the archpriest's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only."},
  ["creature.arclight-phoenix.ggr2014"]={title="Arclight Phoenix",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 193\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 142 (19d8 + 57)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 120\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 22 | CON 17 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 7\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: thunder\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe arclight phoenix doesn't provoke an opportunity attack when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nGrounded Lightning\n\nThe first time on a turn that the arclight phoenix touches the ground, it takes 11 (2d10) force damage.\n\nIllumination\n\nThe arclight phoenix sheds bright light in a 15-foot radius and dim light for an additional 15 feet.\n\nLightning Form\n\nThe arclight phoenix can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing. A creature that touches the phoenix or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 9 (2d8) lightning damage. In addition, the arclight phoenix can enter a hostile creature's space and stop there. The first time it enters a creature's space on a turn, that creature takes 9 (2d8) lightning damage.\n\nCrackling Death\n\nWhen the arclight phoenix dies, it explodes. Each creature within 30 feet of it must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The explosion destroys the phoenix but leaves behind a Tiny, warm egg with a mizzium shell. The egg contains the embryo of a new arclight phoenix. It hatches when it is in the area of a spell that deals lightning damage, or if a creature touches the egg and expends spell slots whose combined levels equal 13 or more. When it hatches, the egg releases a new arclight phoenix that appears in the egg's space.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nArclight Touch\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h27 (6d8) lightning damage, and lightning jumps from the target to one creature of the phoenix's choice that it can see within 30 feet of the target. That second creature must succeed on a 18 Dexterity saving throw or take 27 (6d8) lightning damage."},
  ["creature.arcturia.wdmm2014"]={title="Arcturia",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 296\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting"},
  ["deity.ares.phb2014"]={title="Ares",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["creature.argentia-skywright.veor2014"]={title="Argentia Skywright",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.argonnessen-trinket.erlw2014"]={title="Argonnessen Trinket",subtitle="Item - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nd10 | Trinket\n\n1 | A pierced dragon scale on a cord\n\n2 | A statuette of a dragon carved from black bone\n\n3 | A dragon's tooth, engraved with an unknown sigil\n\n4 | A child's doll of a dragon, woven from leather cords\n\n5 | A dagger carved from a dragon's talon\n\n6 | A brass disk bearing the silhouette of a black dragon\n\n7 | A small egg-shaped piece of polished bone\n\n8 | A bone fragment with brass inlaid runes\n\n9 | A leather pouch filled with tiny draconic teeth\n\n10 | A single large seed that's warm to the touch"},
  ["creature.aribeth-de-tylmarande.mabjov2014"]={title="Aribeth de Tylmarande",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 108\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 120 (16d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Infernal\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nInfernal Tracker\n\nAribeth knows the distance to and direction of any creature that has broken a pact with Mephistopheles, even if the creature and Aribeth are on different planes of existence.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nAribeth has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nNightmare\n\nAribeth is accompanied by a nightmare. The nightmare allows Aribeth to use it as a mount.\n\nRegeneration\n\nAribeth regains 20 hit points at the start of her turn. If Aribeth takes radiant damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of Aribeth's next turn. Aribeth's body is destroyed only if she starts her turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nShadows\n\nThree shadow hide within the saddle of Aribeth's nightmare. These shadows only come out if there is a creature within 30 feet that is at 0 hit points. When that happens, a shadow emerges and attacks the creature in order to make it fail a death saving throw. It continues to do so until the creature is dead.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, Aribeth has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAribeth makes three Void or Unholy Strike attacks.\n\nVoid\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage or 8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage if used with two hands, plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage. A creature reduced to 0 hit points from damage dealt by the sword Void dies and can't be revived by any means short of a wish spell.\n\nUnholy Strike\n\nrs 7 to hit, range 120 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) necrotic damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nAribeth adds 4 to her AC against one melee attack that would hit her. To do so, Aribeth must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.arisen-sarrukh.aud2014"]={title="Arisen Sarrukh",subtitle="Criatura - AUD - 2014",body="Pagina: 125\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 18\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 273 (26d8 + 156)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 17 | CON 22 | INT 18 | WIS 17 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: fire, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the sarrukh fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe sarrukh has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sarrukh makes three attacks, using Trident or Necrotic Spit in any combination.\n\nTrident\n\nm 12, reach 10 ft. h33 (6d8 + 6) Piercing damage.\n\nNecrotic Spit\n\nr 12, range 90 ft. h11 (2d10) Poison damage plus 22 (4d10) Necrotic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nVenomous Teleport {@recharge 5}\n\nThe sarrukh teleports up to 120 feet to an occupied space it can see, and each creature within 10 feet of the space the sarrukh leaves or arrives in (sarrukh's choice) is subjected to the following effect. con 20. actSaveFail 22 (4d10) Poison damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nShape Control\n\nactTrigger A creature the sarrukh can see shape-shifts. actResponse The sarrukh chooses the resulting form from among the options available to the shape-shifting creature or prevents the creature from shape-shifting."},
  ["creature.arkhan-the-cruel.bgdia2014"]={title="Arkhan the Cruel",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 111\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 16\n\nCA: 23\n\nPV: 221 (26d8 + 104)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 12 | CON 18 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft. (can see invisible creatures out to the same range)\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nResistencias: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Hate\n\nWhile Arkhan isn't incapacitated, he and all fiends and undead within 30 feet of him deal 4 extra damage whenever they hit with a melee weapon attack (already factored into Arkhan's attacks). This extra damage is of the same type as the weapon's damage type.\n\nHand of Vecna\n\nThe Hand of Vecna has 8 charges and regains 1d4 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. Arkhan can cast the following spells from the hand by expending the specified number of charges (spell save 18): finger of death (5 charges), sleep (1 charge), slow (2 charges), and teleport (3 charges).\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nArkhan wields BGDIA and wears a suit of BGDIA. The armor gives Arkhan advantage on ability checks and saving throws made to avoid or end the grappled condition on him.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nArkhan makes three weapon attacks.\n\nFane-Eater (Battleaxe)\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h16 (1d8 + 12) slashing damage, or 17 (1d10 + 12) slashing damage when used with two hands, plus 9 (2d8) cold damage. If the target is a creature and Arkhan rolls a 20 on the attack roll, the creature takes an extra 9 (2d8) necrotic damage, and Arkhan regains an amount of hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt.\n\nJavelin\n\nmw,rw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h8 (1d6 + 5) piercing damage, plus 4 piercing damage and 9 (2d8) cold damage if the javelin was used to make a melee attack."},
  ["creature.arlo-kettletoe-levels-1-4.kftgv2014"]={title="Arlo Kettletoe (Levels 1-4)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.arlo-kettletoe-levels-5-8.kftgv2014"]={title="Arlo Kettletoe (Levels 5-8)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.arlo-kettletoe-levels-9-11.kftgv2014"]={title="Arlo Kettletoe (Levels 9-11)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.armanite.mpmm2014"]={title="Armanite",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 94 (9d10 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 18 | CON 21 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 13\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe armanite has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe armanite makes one Claw attack, one Hooves attack, and one Serrated Tail attack.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d4 + 5) slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) lightning damage.\n\nHooves\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 16 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\nSerrated Tail\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nLightning Lance {@recharge 5}\n\nThe armanite looses a bolt of lightning in a line that is 60 feet long and 10 feet wide. Each creature in the line must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.armanite.mtf2014"]={title="Armanite",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 131\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 84 (8d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 18 | CON 21 | INT 8 | WIS 12 | CHA 13\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe armanite has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe armanite's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe armanite makes three attacks: one with its hooves, one with its claws, and one with its serrated tail.\n\nHooves\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d4 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nSerrated Tail\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h16 (2d10 + 5) slashing damage.\n\nLightning Lance {@recharge 5}\n\nThe armanite looses a bolt of lightning in a line 60 feet long and 10 feet wide. Each creature in the line must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 27 (6d8) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.armasaur.psx2014"]={title="Armasaur",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["feature.armor-model.efa2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Armor Model",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nYou can customize your Arcane Armor. When you do so, choose one of the following armor models: Artificer, Artificer, or Artificer. The model you choose gives you special benefits while you wear it.\n\nEach model includes a special weapon. When you attack with that weapon, you can add your Intelligence modifier, instead of your Strength or Dexterity modifier, to the attack and damage rolls.\n\nYou can change the armor's model whenever you finish a XPHB or XPHB if you have XPHB in hand."},
  ["feature.armor-model.tce2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Armor Model",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.armor-modifications.tce2014.artificer.armorer.9"]={title="Armor Modifications",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n9th-level Armorer feature\n\nYou learn how to use your artificer infusions to specially modify your Arcane Armor. That armor now counts as separate items for the purposes of your Infuse Items feature: armor (the chest piece), boots, helmet, and the armor's special weapon. Each of those items can bear one of your infusions, and the infusions transfer over if you change your armor's model with the Armor Model feature. In addition, the maximum number of items you can infuse at once increases by 2, but those extra items must be part of your Arcane Armor."},
  ["spell.armor-of-agathys.phb2014"]={title="Armor of Agathys",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\nA protective magical force surrounds you, manifesting as a spectral frost that covers you and your gear. You gain 5 temporary hit points for the duration. If a creature hits you with a melee attack while you have these hit points, the creature takes 5 cold damage."},
  ["spell.armor-of-agathys.xphb2024"]={title="Armor of Agathys",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 243\n\nProtective magical frost surrounds you. You gain 5 XPHB. If a creature hits you with a melee attack roll before the spell ends, the creature takes 5 Cold damage. The spell ends early if you have no XPHB."},
  ["feature.armor-of-hexes.xge2024.warlock.hexblade.10"]={title="Armor of Hexes",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 55\n\nAt 10th level, your hex grows more powerful. If the target cursed by your Hexblade's Curse hits you with an attack roll, you can use your reaction to roll a d6. On a 4 or higher, the attack instead misses you, regardless of its roll."},
  ["magicitem.armor-of-invulnerability.dmg2014"]={title="Armor of Invulnerability",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nYou have resistance to nonmagical damage while you wear this armor. Additionally, you can use an action to make yourself immune to nonmagical damage for 10 minutes or until you are no longer wearing the armor. Once this special action is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.armor-of-invulnerability.xdmg2024"]={title="Armor of Invulnerability",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 230\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nYou have XPHB to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage while you wear this armor.\n\nMetal Shell\n\nYou can take a XPHB action to give yourself XPHB to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage for 10 minutes or until you are no longer wearing the armor. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["optionalfeature.armor-of-magical-strength.tce2014"]={title="Armor of Magical Strength",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nThis armor has 6 charges. The wearer can expend the armor's charges in the following ways:\n\n• When the wearer makes a Strength check or a Strength saving throw, it can expend 1 charge to add a bonus to the roll equal to its Intelligence modifier.\n\n• If the creature would be knocked prone, it can use its reaction to expend 1 charge to avoid being knocked prone.\n\nThe armor regains 1d6 expended charges daily at dawn."},
  ["optionalfeature.armor-of-shadows.phb2014"]={title="Armor of Shadows",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nYou can cast mage armor on yourself at will, without expending a spell slot or material components."},
  ["optionalfeature.armor-of-shadows.xphb2024"]={title="Armor of Shadows",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 155\n\nYou can cast XPHB on yourself without expending a spell slot."},
  ["magicitem.armor-of-vulnerability-bludgeoning.dmg2014"]={title="Armor of Vulnerability (Bludgeoning)",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing this armor, you have resistance to bludgeoning damage.\n\nCurse\n\nThis armor is cursed, a fact that is revealed only when an identify spell is cast on the armor or you attune to it. Attuning to the armor curses you until you are targeted by the remove curse spell or similar magic; removing the armor fails to end the curse. While cursed you have vulnerability to piercing and slashing damage."},
  ["magicitem.armor-of-vulnerability-piercing.dmg2014"]={title="Armor of Vulnerability (Piercing)",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing this armor, you have resistance to piercing damage.\n\nCurse\n\nThis armor is cursed, a fact that is revealed only when an identify spell is cast on the armor or you attune to it. Attuning to the armor curses you until you are targeted by the remove curse spell or similar magic; removing the armor fails to end the curse. While cursed you have vulnerability to bludgeoning and slashing damage."},
  ["magicitem.armor-of-vulnerability-slashing.dmg2014"]={title="Armor of Vulnerability (Slashing)",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nWhile wearing this armor, you have resistance to slashing damage.\n\nCurse\n\nThis armor is cursed, a fact that is revealed only when an identify spell is cast on the armor or you attune to it. Attuning to the armor curses you until you are targeted by the remove curse spell or similar magic; removing the armor fails to end the curse. While cursed you have vulnerability to bludgeoning and piercing damage."},
  ["feature.armor-training.uathemysticclass2014.mystic.avatar.1"]={title="Armor Training",subtitle="Caracteristica - UATheMysticClass - 2014",body="Pagina: 5\n\nAt 1st level, you gain proficiency with medium armor and shields."},
  ["creature.armored-saber-toothed-tiger.cos2014"]={title="Armored Saber-Toothed Tiger",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 84 (7d10 + 14)"},
  ["creature.armored-troglodyte.wdmm2014"]={title="Armored Troglodyte",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCA: 14\n\nIdiomas: understands Undercommon but can't speak"},
  ["subclass.armorer.efa2014.artificer.armorer.0"]={title="Armorer",subtitle="Subclasse - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 14"},
  ["feature.armorer.efa2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Armorer",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nCraft Magic Armor to Enhance Your Abilities\n\nAn Armorer modifies armor to function almost like a second skin. The armor is enhanced to hone the Armorer's magic, unleash potent attacks, and generate a formidable defense."},
  ["subclass.armorer.tce2014.artificer.armorer.0"]={title="Armorer",subtitle="Subclasse - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.armorer.tce2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Armorer",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nAn artificer who specializes as an Armorer modifies armor to function almost like a second skin. The armor is enhanced to hone the artificer's magic, unleash potent attacks, and generate a formidable defense. The artificer bonds with this armor, becoming one with it even as they experiment with it and refine its magical capabilities."},
  ["feature.armorer-spells.efa2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Armorer Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Armorer Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["feature.armorer-spells.tce2014.artificer.armorer.3"]={title="Armorer Spells",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\n3rd-level Armorer feature\n\nYou always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Armorer Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | magic missile, thunderwave\n\n5th | mirror image, shatter\n\n9th | hypnotic pattern, lightning bolt\n\n13th | fire shield, greater invisibility\n\n17th | passwall, wall of force"},
  ["spell.arms-of-hadar.phb2014"]={title="Arms of Hadar",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\nYou invoke the power of Hadar, the Dark Hunger. Tendrils of dark energy erupt from you and batter all creatures within 10 feet of you. Each creature in that area must make a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, a target takes 2d6 necrotic damage and can't take reactions until its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half damage, but suffers no other effect."},
  ["spell.arms-of-hadar.xphb2024"]={title="Arms of Hadar",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 243\n\nInvoking Hadar, you cause tendrils to erupt from yourself. Each creature in a 10-foot XPHB originating from you makes a Strength saving throw. On a failed save, a target takes 2d6 Necrotic damage and can't take Reactions until the start of its next turn. On a successful save, a target takes half as much damage only."},
  ["feature.arms-of-the-astral-self.tce2014.monk.astral-self.3"]={title="Arms of the Astral Self",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 50\n\n3rd-level Way of the Astral Self feature\n\nYour mastery of your ki allows you to summon a portion of your astral self. As a bonus action, you can spend 1 ki point to summon the arms of your astral self. When you do so, each creature of your choice that you can see within 10 feet of you must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take force damage equal to two rolls of your Martial Arts die.\n\nFor 10 minutes, these spectral arms hover near your shoulders or surround your arms (your choice). You determine the arms' appearance, and they vanish early if you are incapacitated or die.\n\nWhile the spectral arms are present, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• You can use your Wisdom modifier in place of your Strength modifier when making Strength checks and Strength saving throws.\n\n• You can use the spectral arms to make unarmed strikes.\n\n• When you make an unarmed strike with the arms on your turn, your reach for it is 5 feet greater than normal.\n\n• The unarmed strikes you make with the arms can use your Wisdom modifier in place of your Strength or Dexterity modifier for the attack and damage rolls, and their damage type is force."},
  ["deity.arms-of-the-betrayers.egw2014"]={title="Arms of the Betrayers",subtitle="Divindade - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\nBefore the Calamity, eight of the Betrayer Gods each forged a sentient weapon using the life force of a greater fiend and gave the weapon to a chosen champion in the kingdom of Ghor Dranas. The Calamity flung these weapons across Wildemount, burying them in mountains, forests, fields, and underground. Several of these weapons have been recovered, but a few have never been found and are highly sought-after. The weapons—or more properly, the fiends bound inside them—attract their own followings of mortal worshipers.\n\nWhen an Arm of the Betrayers is found, it grants its wielder some of the power of the Betrayer Gods and the wisdom of the fiend within. The bound fiends know that their war was lost long ago, but they still desire to be used in battle, win victories, and spill blood in the hands of skilled warriors. As a weapon's wielder becomes more powerful, so too does the weapon, which in turn is able to lend even more magic to the wielder. Whenever a weapon's wielder dies, the weapon disappears and reappears elsewhere.\n\nThe Betrayer Gods made the following weapons, which are described in more detail in EGW:\n\nEGW. This stone dagger of Tharizdun has yet to be found after the Calamity. It has the power to warp reality around its wielder. The life force of a glabrezu named Ragazuu was used to forge the weapon.\n\nEGW. This obsidian warhammer carries the tortured will of Torog and can raze whole structures with a single strike. The life force of an ultroloth named Ciria was used to forge the weapon.\n\nEGW. This Zehir-touched whip ends in five serpent heads that pump poisons of varying effects into the wielder's foes. The life force of a marilith named Sizlifeth was used to forge the weapon.\n\nEGW. This mace with a fiend's head of ruby carries the boon of Asmodeus, capable of summoning devils for the wielder to command and burning hot enough to melt steel. The life force of an erinyes named Xartaza was used to forge the weapon.\n\nEGW. This Gruumsh-blessed ivory spear can effortlessly pierce armor and transforms into lightning when hurled. The life force of a balor named Yarrowish was used to forge the weapon.\n\nEGW. This rapier has a blade forged from spider silk that gives the wielder Lolth's blessing. The life force of a yochlol named Sinnafex was used to forge the weapon.\n\nEGW. This adamantine morningstar bears the boon of Bane, and has yet to be found after the Calamity. It has the power to subjugate the wielder's enemies. The life force of a pit fiend named Izeelzee was used to forge the weapon.\n\nEGW. This war pick bears the mark of Tiamat and makes the wielder impervious to the elements and grants them the power of dragon breath. The life force of an bone devil named Ashtyrlon was used to forge the weapon."},
  ["creature.arrant-quill.cm2014"]={title="Arrant Quill",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 135 (18d8 + 54)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 18 | CON 16 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Undercommon\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nQuill makes two attacks with his dagger and uses Supreme Mockery.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nQuill's Fable {@recharge}\n\nQuill utters a short fable while targeting up to five creatures within 30 feet of him that he can see. Each target that can hear Quill's magical fable must make a 17 Wisdom saving throw, taking 36 (8d8) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nSupreme Mockery\n\nQuill hurls a string of insults laced with enchantments at a creature he can see within 60 feet of him. If the creature can hear Quill (though it need not understand him), it must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or take 66 (12d10) psychic damage and have disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.arrigal.cos2014"]={title="Arrigal",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 121\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.arrow.phb2014"]={title="Arrow",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.arrow.xphb2024"]={title="Arrow",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: none\n\nArrows are used with a weapon that has the ammunition property to make a ranged attack. Each time you attack with the weapon, you expend one piece of ammunition. Drawing the ammunition from a quiver, case, or other container is part of the attack (you need a free hand to load a one-handed weapon). At the end of the battle, you can recover half your expended ammunition by taking a minute to search the battlefield.\n\nArrows are typically stored in a XPHB (bought separately)."},
  ["magicitem.arrow-catching-shield.dmg2014"]={title="Arrow-Catching Shield",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to AC against ranged attacks while you wield this shield. This bonus is in addition to the shield's normal bonus to AC. In addition, whenever an attacker makes a ranged attack against a target within 5 feet of you, you can use your reaction to become the target of the attack instead."},
  ["magicitem.arrow-catching-shield.xdmg2024"]={title="Arrow-Catching Shield",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 231\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to XPHB against ranged attack rolls while you wield this Shield. This bonus is in addition to the Shield's normal bonus to AC.\n\nWhenever an attacker makes a ranged attack roll against a target within 5 feet of you, you can take a XPHB to become the target of the attack instead.\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["item.arrows-20.phb2014"]={title="Arrows (20)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.arrows-20.xphb2024"]={title="Arrows (20)",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: none\n\nArrows are used with a weapon that has the ammunition property to make a ranged attack. Each time you attack with the weapon, you expend one piece of ammunition. Drawing the ammunition from a quiver, case, or other container is part of the attack (you need a free hand to load a one-handed weapon). At the end of the battle, you can recover half your expended ammunition by taking a minute to search the battlefield.\n\nArrows are typically stored in a XPHB (bought separately)."},
  ["creature.art-elemental-mascot.scc2014"]={title="Art Elemental Mascot",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 185\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 18 (4d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 13 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 11 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Burst\n\nWhen the elemental dies, it explodes in a burst of colored light. Each creature within 5 feet of the elemental must succeed on a 11 Constitution saving throw or be blinded for 1 minute. A blinded creature can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nJoyful Flare\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) fire damage.\n\nMelancholic Bolt\n\nrw 3 to hit, range 30 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) cold damage.\n\nCaptivating Artistry (1/Day)\n\nThe elemental targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 12 Charisma saving throw or be charmed for 1 minute. The charmed target can repeat the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["deity.artemis.phb2014"]={title="Artemis",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 298"},
  ["class.artificer.efa2014"]={title="Artificer",subtitle="Classe - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\nSpellcasting|Artificer|EFA|1|EFA\n\nTinker's Magic|Artificer|EFA|1|EFA\n\nReplicate Magic Item|Artificer|EFA|2|EFA\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Artificer|EFA|4|EFA\n\nMagic Item Tinker|Artificer|EFA|6|EFA\n\nFlash of Genius|Artificer|EFA|7|EFA\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Artificer|EFA|8|EFA\n\nMagic Item Adept|Artificer|EFA|10|EFA\n\nSpell-Storing Item|Artificer|EFA|11|EFA\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Artificer|EFA|12|EFA\n\nAdvanced Artifice|Artificer|EFA|14|EFA\n\nAbility Score Improvement|Artificer|EFA|16|EFA\n\nMagic Item Master|Artificer|EFA|18|EFA\n\nEpic Boon|Artificer|EFA|19|EFA\n\nSoul of Artifice|Artificer|EFA|20|EFA\n\n=== CARACTERISTICAS DA CLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Magical Tinkering\n\nPagina: 9\n\n1st-level artificer feature\n\nYou've learned how to invest a spark of magic into mundane objects. To use this ability, you must have PHB or PHB in hand. You then touch a Tiny nonmagical object as an action and give it one of the following magical properties of your choice:\n\n• The object sheds bright light in a 5-foot radius and dim light for an additional 5 feet.\n\n• Whenever tapped by a creature, the object emits a recorded message that can be heard up to 10 feet away. You utter the message when you bestow this property on the object, and the recording can be no more than 6 seconds long.\n\n• The object continuously emits your choice of an odor or a nonverbal sound (wind, waves, chirping, or the like). The chosen phenomenon is perceivable up to 10 feet away.\n\n• A static visual effect appears on one of the object's surfaces. This effect can be a picture, up to 25 words of text, lines and shapes, or a mixture of these elements, as you like.\n\nThe chosen property lasts indefinitely. As an action, you can touch the object and end the property early.\n\nYou can bestow magic on multiple objects, touching one object each time you use this feature, though a single object can only bear one property at a time. The maximum number of objects you can affect with this feature at one time is equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of one object). If you try to exceed your maximum, the oldest property immediately ends, and then the new property applies.\n\nNivel 1 - Optional Rule: Firearm Proficiency\n\nPagina: 9\n\nThe secrets of creating and operating gunpowder weapons have been discovered in various corners of the D&D multiverse. If your Dungeon Master uses the rules on firearms in DMG of the DMG and your artificer has been exposed to the operation of such weapons, your artificer is proficient with them.\n\nNivel 1 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 7\n\nYou have learned how to channel magical energy through objects. See the XPHB for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you use those rules with Artificer spells, which appear in the spells later in the class's description.\n\nTools Required\n\nYou produce your Artificer spells through tools. You can use XPHB, XPHB, or another kind of XPHB with which you have proficiency as a XPHB, and you must have one of those focuses in hand when you cast an Artificer spell (meaning the spell has an M component when you cast it).\n\nCantrips\n\nYou know two spells of your choice. XPHB and XPHB are recommended.\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can replace one of your cantrips from this feature with another Artificer cantrip of your choice.\n\nWhen you reach Artificer levels 10 and 14, you learn another Artificer cantrip of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips column of the Artificer Features table.\n\nSpell Slots\n\nThe Artificer Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a XPHB.\n\nPrepared Spells of Level 1+\n\nYou prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose two spells. XPHB and XPHB are recommended.\n\nThe number of spells on your list increases as you gain Artificer levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Artificer Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number on the table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 5 Artificer, your list of prepared spells can include six Artificer spells of levels 1 and 2 in any combination.\n\nIf another Artificer feature gives you spells that you always have prepared, those don't count against the number of spells you can prepare with this feature, but those spells otherwise count as Artificer spells for you.\n\nChanging Your Prepared Spells\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can change your list of prepared spells, replacing any of the spells there with other Artificer spells for which you have spell slots.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nIntelligence is your spellcasting ability for your Artificer spells.\n\nNivel 1 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 9\n\n1st-level artificer feature\n\nYou've studied the workings of magic and how to cast spells, channeling the magic through objects. To observers, you don't appear to be casting spells in a conventional way; you appear to produce wonders from mundane items and outlandish inventions.\n\nTools Required\n\nYou produce your artificer spell effects through your tools. You must have a spellcasting focus—specifically phb or some kind of phb—in hand when you cast any spell with this Spellcasting feature (meaning the spell has an 'M' component when you cast it). You must be proficient with the tool to use it in this way. See PHB, \"Equipment,\" in the PHB for descriptions of these tools.\n\nAfter you gain the Infuse Item feature at 2nd level, you can also use any item bearing one of your infusions as a spellcasting focus.\n\nThe Magic of Artifice\n\nAs an artificer, you use tools when you cast your spells. When describing your spellcasting, think about how you're using a tool to perform the spell effect. If you cast cure wounds using PHB, you could be quickly producing a salve. If you cast it using PHB, you might have a miniature mechanical spider that binds wounds. When you cast poison spray, you could fling foul chemicals or use a wand that spits venom. The effect of the spell is the same as for a spellcaster of any other class, but your method of spellcasting is special.\n\nThe same principle applies when you prepare your spells. As an artificer, you don't study a spellbook or pray to prepare your spells. Instead, you work with your tools and create the specialized items you'll use to produce your effects. If you replace cure wounds with heat metal, you might be altering the device you use to heal—perhaps modifying a tool so that it channels heat instead of healing energy.\n\nSuch details don't limit you in any way or provide you with any benefit beyond the spell's effects. You don't have to justify how you're using tools to cast a spell. But describing your spellcasting creatively is a fun way to distinguish yourself from other spellcasters.\n\nCantrips (0-Level Spells)\n\nAt 1st level, you know two cantrips of your choice from the spells. At higher levels, you learn additional artificer cantrips of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips Known column of the Artificer table.\n\nWhen you gain a level in this class, you can replace one of the artificer cantrips you know with another cantrip from the artificer spell list.\n\nPreparing and Casting Spells\n\nThe Artificer table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your artificer spells. To cast one of your artificer spells of 1st level or higher, you must expend a slot of the spell's level or higher. You regain all expended spell slots when you finish a long rest.\n\nYou prepare the list of artificer spells that are available for you to cast, choosing from the spells. When you do so, choose a number of artificer spells equal to your Intelligence modifier + half your artificer level, rounded down (minimum of one spell). The spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots.\n\nFor example, if you are a 5th-level artificer, you have four 1st-level and two 2nd-level spell slots. With an Intelligence of 14, your list of prepared spells can include four spells of 1st or 2nd level, in any combination. If you prepare the 1st-level spell cure wounds, you can cast it using a 1st-level or a 2nd-level slot. Casting the spell doesn't remove it from your list of prepared spells.\n\nYou can change your list of prepared spells when you finish a long rest. Preparing a new list of artificer spells requires time spent tinkering with your spellcasting focuses: at least 1 minute per spell level for each spell on your list.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nIntelligence is your spellcasting ability for your artificer spells; your understanding of the theory behind magic allows you to wield these spells with superior skill. You use your Intelligence whenever an artificer spell refers to your spellcasting ability. In addition, you use your Intelligence modifier when setting the saving throw DC for an artificer spell you cast and when making an attack roll with one.\n\nSpell\n\nSpell\n\nRitual Casting\n\nYou can cast an artificer spell as a ritual if that spell has the ritual tag and you have the spell prepared.\n\nNivel 1 - Tinker's Magic\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYou know the XPHB cantrip.\n\nAs a XPHB action while holding XPHB, you can create one item in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of yourself, choosing the item from the following list:\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\n• XPHB\n\nSee the rules for the item in the XPHB. The item lasts until you finish a XPHB, at which point it vanishes.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 2 - Infuse Item\n\nPagina: 9\n\n2nd-level artificer feature\n\nYou've gained the ability to imbue mundane items with certain magical infusions, turning those objects into magic items.\n\nArtificer Infusions\n\nArtificers have invented numerous magical infusions, extraordinary processes that rapidly create magic items. To many, artificers seem like wonderworkers, accomplishing in hours what others need weeks to complete.\n\nThe description of each of the following infusions details the type of item that can receive it, along with whether the resulting magic item requires attunement.\n\nSome infusions specify a minimum artificer level. You can't learn such an infusion until you are at least that level.\n\nUnless an infusion's description says otherwise, you can't learn an infusion more than once.\n\nInfusing an Item\n\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a nonmagical object and imbue it with one of your artificer infusions, turning it into a magic item. An infusion works on only certain kinds of objects, as specified in the infusion's description. If the item requires attunement, you can attune yourself to it the instant you infuse the item. If you decide to attune to the item later, you must do so using the normal process for attunement (see \"DMG\" in chapter 7 of the DMG).\n\nYour infusion remains in an item indefinitely, but when you die, the infusion vanishes after a number of days have passed equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 day). The infusion also vanishes if you give up your knowledge of the infusion for another one.\n\nYou can infuse more than one nonmagical object at the end of a long rest; the maximum number of objects appears in the Infused Items column of the Artificer table. You must touch each of the objects, and each of your infusions can be in only one object at a time. Moreover, no object can bear more than one of your infusions at a time. If you try to exceed your maximum number of infusions, the oldest infusion immediately ends, and then the new infusion applies.\n\nIf an infusion ends on an item that contains other things, like a bag of holding, its contents harmlessly appear in and around its space.\n\nNivel 2 - Infuse Item\n\nNivel 2 - Infusions Known\n\nPagina: 9\n\nWhen you gain this feature, pick four artificer infusions to learn, choosing from the \"optionalfeatures\" section at the end of the class's description. You learn additional infusions of your choice when you reach certain levels in this class, as shown in the Infusions Known column of the Artificer table.\n\nWhenever you gain a level in this class, you can replace one of the artificer infusions you learned with a new one.\n\nNivel 2 - Infusions Known\n\nNivel 2 - Replicate Magic Item\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYou have learned arcane plans that you use to make magic items.\n\nPlans Known\n\nWhen you gain this feature, choose four plans to learn from the Magic Item Plans (Artificer Level 2+) table (see the XDMG for the items' descriptions). XDMG, XDMG, XDMG, and XDMG are recommended. Whenever you gain an Artificer level, you can replace one of the plans you know with a new plan for which you qualify.\n\nYou learn another plan of your choice when you reach certain Artificer levels, as shown in the Plans Known column of the Artificer Features table. When you choose a plan to learn, you choose it from any Magic Item Plans table for which you qualify; your qualification is based on your Artificer level.\n\nCreating an Item\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB, you can create one or two different magic items if you have XPHB in hand. Each item is based on one of the plans you know for this feature.\n\nIf a created item requires XPHB, you can attune yourself to it the instant you create it. If you decide to attune to the item later, you must do so using the normal process for XPHB.\n\nWhen you reach certain Artificer levels specified in the Magic Items column of the Artificer Features table, the number of magic items you can create at the end of a XPHB increases. Each item you create must be based on a different plan you know.\n\nYou can't have more magic items from this feature than the number shown in the Magic Items column of the Artificer Features table for your level. If you try to exceed your maximum number of magic items for this feature, the oldest item vanishes, and then the new item appears.\n\nDuration\n\nA magic item created by this feature functions as the normal magic item, except its magic isn't permanent; when you die, the magic item vanishes after 1d4 days. If you replace a plan you know with a new plan, any magic item created with the replaced plan immediately vanishes.\n\nIf an item that you created with this feature is a container, such as a XDMG, and it vanishes, its contents harmlessly appear in and around its space.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use any Wand or Weapon created by this feature as a XPHB in lieu of using a set of XPHB.\n\nCrafting More Magic Items\n\nThe Replicate Magic Item feature isn't the only way for an Artificer to make magic items. The XDMG provides rules for characters—not just Artificers—who want to make magic items of all sorts. Though many different characters can make magic items, Artificers can do it faster than others; each Artificer subclass improves a character's speed at making items of a certain category.\n\nWhen an Artificer crafts a magic item using the normal rules in the XDMG, the character gains no special connection to that item. Class features that refer to items created by your Replicate Magic Item feature don't apply to items you craft by other means.\n\nMagic Item Plan | Attunement\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nitems* | Varies\n\nXDMG | No\n\nEFA | Yes\n\nEFA | Yes\n\nEFA | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nMagic Item Plan | Attunement\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nEFA | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nEFA | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nEFA | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nEFA | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | No\n\nEFA | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nEFA | Yes\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nMagic Item Plan | Attunement\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | No\n\nitems* | Varies\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | No\n\nMagic Item Plan | Attunement\n\nXDMG | No\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nitems* | Varies\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nXDMG | Yes\n\nNivel 3 - Adventurer's Atlas\n\nPagina: 20\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB while holding XPHB, you can use that tool to create a set of magical maps by touching at least two creatures (one of whom can be yourself), up to a maximum number of creatures equal to 1 plus your Intelligence modifier (minimum of two creatures). Each target receives a magical map, which constantly updates to show the relative position of all the map holders but is illegible to all others. The maps last until you die or until you use this feature again, at which point any existing maps created by this feature immediately vanish.\n\nWhile carrying the map, a target gains the following benefits.\n\nAwareness\n\nThe target adds 1d4 to its XPHB rolls.\n\nPositioning\n\nThe target knows the location of all other map holders that are on the same plane of existence as itself. When casting a spell or creating another effect that requires being able to see the effect's target, a map holder can target another map holder regardless of sight or cover, so long as the other map holder is still within the effect's range.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 12\n\nCraft Magic Elixirs and Potions\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce magical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 14\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce mystical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away. Alchemy is the oldest of artificer traditions, and its versatility has long been valued during times of war and peace.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Alchemist Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 14\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Alchemist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | healing word, ray of sickness\n\n5th | flaming sphere, Melf's acid arrow\n\n9th | gaseous form, mass healing word\n\n13th | blight, death ward\n\n17th | cloudkill, raise dead\n\nNivel 3 - Arcane Armor\n\nPagina: 15\n\nAs a XPHB action while you have XPHB in hand, you can turn a suit of armor you are wearing into Arcane Armor. The armor continues to be Arcane Armor until you don another suit of armor or you die.\n\nYou gain the following benefits while wearing your Arcane Armor.\n\nNo Strength Requirement\n\nIf the armor normally has a Strength requirement, the Arcane Armor lacks this requirement for you.\n\nQuick Don and Doff\n\nYou can don or doff the armor as a XPHB action. The armor can't be removed against your will.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use the Arcane Armor as a XPHB for your Artificer spells.\n\nNivel 3 - Arcane Armor\n\nPagina: 15\n\n3rd-level Armorer feature\n\nYour metallurgical pursuits have led to you making armor a conduit for your magic. As an action, you can turn a suit of armor you are wearing into Arcane Armor, provided you have PHB in hand.\n\nYou gain the following benefits while wearing this armor:\n\n• If the armor normally has a Strength requirement, the arcane armor lacks this requirement for you.\n\n• You can use the arcane armor as a spellcasting focus for your artificer spells.\n\n• The armor attaches to you and can't be removed against your will. It also expands to cover your entire body, although you can retract or deploy the helmet as a bonus action. The armor replaces any missing limbs, functioning identically to a limb it replaces.\n\n• You can doff or don the armor as an action. The armor continues to be Arcane Armor until you don another suit of armor or you die.\n\nNivel 3 - Armor Model\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYou can customize your Arcane Armor. When you do so, choose one of the following armor models: Artificer, Artificer, or Artificer. The model you choose gives you special benefits while you wear it.\n\nEach model includes a special weapon. When you attack with that weapon, you can add your Intelligence modifier, instead of your Strength or Dexterity modifier, to the attack and damage rolls.\n\nYou can change the armor's model whenever you finish a XPHB or XPHB if you have XPHB in hand.\n\nNivel 3 - Armor Model\n\nPagina: 15\n\n3rd-level Armorer feature\n\nYou can customize your Arcane Armor. When you do so, choose one of the following armor models: Guardian or Infiltrator. The model you choose gives you special benefits while you wear it.\n\nEach model includes a special weapon. When you attack with that weapon, you can add your Intelligence modifier, instead of Strength or Dexterity, to the attack and damage rolls.\n\nYou can change the armor's model whenever you finish a short or long rest, provided you have PHB in hand.\n\nGuardian\n\nYou design your armor to be in the front line of conflict. It has the following features:\n\nInfiltrator\n\nYou customize your armor for subtle undertakings. It has the following features:\n\nNivel 3 - Armor Model\n\nNivel 3 - Armorer\n\nPagina: 14\n\nCraft Magic Armor to Enhance Your Abilities\n\nAn Armorer modifies armor to function almost like a second skin. The armor is enhanced to hone the Armorer's magic, unleash potent attacks, and generate a formidable defense.\n\nNivel 3 - Armorer\n\nPagina: 15\n\nAn artificer who specializes as an Armorer modifies armor to function almost like a second skin. The armor is enhanced to hone the artificer's magic, unleash potent attacks, and generate a formidable defense. The artificer bonds with this armor, becoming one with it even as they experiment with it and refine its magical capabilities.\n\nNivel 3 - Armorer Spells\n\nPagina: 15\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Armorer Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Armorer Spells\n\nPagina: 15\n\n3rd-level Armorer feature\n\nYou always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Armorer Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | magic missile, thunderwave\n\n5th | mirror image, shatter\n\n9th | hypnotic pattern, lightning bolt\n\n13th | fire shield, greater invisibility\n\n17th | passwall, wall of force\n\nNivel 3 - Artificer Specialist\n\nPagina: 9\n\n3rd-level artificer feature\n\nChoose the type of specialist you are, each of which is detailed at the end of the class's description. Your choice grants you features at 5th level and again at 9th and 15th level.\n\nNivel 3 - Artificer Subclass\n\nPagina: 10\n\nYou gain an Artificer subclass of your choice. The Artificer, Artificer, Artificer, Artificer, and Artificer subclasses are detailed after this class's description. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Artificer levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Artificer level or lower.\n\nNivel 3 - Artillerist\n\nPagina: 16\n\nWield Destructive Power from Afar\n\nAn Artillerist specializes in using magic to hurl energy, projectiles, and explosions on a battlefield.\n\nNivel 3 - Artillerist\n\nPagina: 17\n\nAn Artillerist specializes in using magic to hurl energy, projectiles, and explosions on a battlefield. This destructive power was valued by all the armies of the Last War. Now that the war is over, some members of this specialization have sought to build a more peaceful world by using their powers to fight the resurgence of strife in Khorvaire.\n\nThe gnome artificer Vi, an unlikely yet key member of House Cannith's warforged project, has been especially vocal about making things right: \"It's about time we fixed things instead of blowing them all to hell.\"\n\nNivel 3 - Artillerist Spells\n\nPagina: 16\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Artillerist Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Artillerist Spells\n\nPagina: 17\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Artillerist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | shield, thunderwave\n\n5th | scorching ray, shatter\n\n9th | fireball, wind wall\n\n13th | ice storm, wall of fire\n\n17th | cone of cold, wall of force\n\nNivel 3 - Battle Ready\n\nPagina: 18\n\nYour combat training and your experiments with magic have paid off in two ways.\n\nArcane Empowerment\n\nWhen you attack with a magic weapon, you can use your Intelligence modifier, instead of your Strength or Dexterity modifier, for the attack and damage rolls.\n\nWeapon Knowledge\n\nYou gain proficiency with items. You can use a weapon with which you have proficiency as a XPHB for your Artificer spells.\n\nNivel 3 - Battle Ready\n\nPagina: 18\n\nWhen you reach 3rd level, your combat training and your experiments with magic have paid off in two ways:\n\n• You gain proficiency with items.\n\n• When you attack with a magic weapon, you can use your Intelligence modifier, instead of Strength or Dexterity modifier, for the attack and damage rolls.\n\nNivel 3 - Battle Ready\n\nNivel 3 - Battle Ready\n\nNivel 3 - Battle Smith\n\nPagina: 18\n\nCommand a Construct Guardian\n\nA Battle Smith is a combination of protector and medic, an expert at defending others and repairing both materiel and personnel. To aid in their work, Battle Smiths are accompanied by a EFA, a protective companion of their own creation.\n\nNivel 3 - Battle Smith\n\nPagina: 18\n\nArmies require protection, and someone has to put things back together if defenses fail. A combination of protector and medic, a Battle Smith is an expert at defending others and repairing both material and personnel. To aid in their work, Battle Smiths are usually accompanied by a steel defender, a protective companion of their own creation. Many soldiers tell stories of nearly dying before being saved by a Battle Smith and a steel defender.\n\nBattle Smiths played a key role in House Cannith's work on battle constructs and the original warforged, and after the Last War, these artificers led efforts to aid those who were injured in the war's horrific battles.\n\nNivel 3 - Battle Smith Spells\n\nPagina: 18\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Battle Smith Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Battle Smith Spells\n\nPagina: 18\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Battle Smith Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | heroism, shield\n\n5th | branding smite, warding bond\n\n9th | aura of vitality, conjure barrage\n\n13th | aura of purity, fire shield\n\n17th | banishing smite, mass cure wounds\n\nNivel 3 - Cartographer\n\nPagina: 20\n\nChart Advantageous Courses through Turmoil\n\nCartographers are the premier navigators and reconnaissance agents. Using their creations, Cartographers can highlight threats, safeguard allies, and carve portals to distant locations.\n\nNivel 3 - Cartographer Spells\n\nPagina: 20\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Cartographer Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Dampening Field\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYou have advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. If the armor normally imposes disadvantage on such checks, the advantage and disadvantage cancel each other, as normal.\n\nNivel 3 - Defensive Field\n\nPagina: 15\n\nAs a bonus action, you can gain temporary hit points equal to your level in this class, replacing any temporary hit points you already have. You lose these temporary hit points if you doff the armor. You can use this bonus action a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 3 - Defensive Field\n\nNivel 3 - Dreadnaught\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYou design your armor to become a towering juggernaut in battle. It has the following features:\n\n• Force Demolisher An arcane wrecking ball or sledgehammer projects from your armor. The demolisher counts as a Simple Melee weapon with the XPHB property, and it deals 1d10 Force damage on a hit. If you hit a creature that is at least one size smaller than you with the demolisher, you can push the creature up to 10 feet straight away from yourself or pull the creature up to 10 feet toward yourself.\n\n• Giant Stature As a XPHB, you transform and enlarge your armor for 1 minute. For the duration, your reach increases by 5 feet, and if you are smaller than Large, you become Large, along with anything you are wearing. If there isn't enough room for you to increase your size, your size doesn't change. You can use this XPHB a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 3 - Eldritch Cannon\n\nPagina: 16\n\nUsing XPHB or XPHB, you can take a XPHB action to create a Small or Tiny EFA in an unoccupied space on a horizontal surface within 5 feet of yourself. You determine its appearance, including whether you carry it or not (and your choice of legs or wheels, for the latter). It disappears if it is reduced to 0 XPHB or after 1 hour. You can dismiss it early as a XPHB action.\n\nOnce you create a cannon, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB or expend a spell slot to create one. You can have only one cannon at a time and can't create one while you already have one.\n\nNivel 3 - Eldritch Cannon\n\nPagina: 17\n\nAt 3rd level, you learn how to create a magical cannon. Using PHB or PHB, you can take an action to magically create a Small or Tiny eldritch cannon in an unoccupied space on a horizontal surface within 5 feet of you. A Small eldritch cannon occupies its space, and a Tiny one can be held in one hand.\n\nOnce you create a cannon, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest or until you expend a spell slot of 1st level or higher. You can have only one cannon at a time and can't create one while your cannon is present.\n\nThe cannon is a magical object. Regardless of size, the cannon has an AC of 18 and a number of hit points equal to five times your artificer level. It is immune to poison damage and psychic damage, and all conditions. If it is forced to make an ability check or a saving throw, treat all its ability scores as 10 (+0). If the mending spell is cast on it, it regains 2d6 hit points. It disappears if it is reduced to 0 hit points or after 1 hour. You can dismiss it early as an action.\n\nWhen you create the cannon, you determine its appearance and whether it has legs. You also decide which type it is, choosing from the options on the Eldritch Cannons table. On each of your turns, you can take a bonus action to cause the cannon to activate if you are within 60 feet of it. As part of the same bonus action, you can direct the cannon to walk or climb up to 15 feet to an unoccupied space, provided it has legs.\n\nCannon | Activation\n\nTCE | The cannon exhales fire in an adjacent 15-foot cone that you designate. Each creature in that area must make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 2d8 fire damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. The fire ignites any flammable objects in the area that aren't being worn or carried.\n\nTCE | Make a ranged spell attack, originating from the cannon, at one creature or object within 120 feet of it. On a hit, the target takes 2d8 force damage, and if the target is a creature, it is pushed up to 5 feet away from the cannon.\n\nTCE | The cannon emits a burst of positive energy that grants itself and each creature of your choice within 10 feet of it a number of temporary hit points equal to 1d8 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).\n\nNivel 3 - Eldritch Cannon\n\nNivel 3 - Experimental Elixir\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB while holding XPHB, you can use that tool to magically produce two elixirs. For each elixir, roll on the Experimental Elixir table for the elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. The elixir appears in a vial, and the vial vanishes when the elixir is drunk or poured out. If any elixir remains when you finish a XPHB, the elixir and its vial vanish.\n\nDrinking an Elixir\n\nAs a XPHB, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to another creature within 5 feet of itself.\n\nCreating Additional Elixirs\n\nAs a XPHB action while holding XPHB, you can expend one spell slot to create another elixir. When you do so, you choose its effect from the Experimental Elixir table rather than rolling.\n\nWhen you reach certain Artificer levels, you can make an additional elixir at the end of each XPHB: a total of three at level 5, four at level 9, and five at level 15.\n\n1d6 | Effect\n\n1 | Healing. The drinker regains a number of XPHB equal to 2d8 plus your Intelligence modifier. The number of XPHB restored increases by 1d8 when you reach Artificer levels 9 (3d8) and 15 (4d8).\n\n2 | Swiftness. The drinker's XPHB increases by 10 feet for 1 hour. This bonus increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (15 feet) and 15 (20 feet).\n\n3 | Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes. The duration increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (1 hour) and 15 (8 hours).\n\n4 | Boldness. The drinker can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to every attack roll and saving throw they make for the next minute. The duration increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (10 minutes) and 15 (1 hour).\n\n5 | Flight. The drinker gains a XPHB of 10 feet for 10 minutes. The XPHB increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (20 feet) and 15 (30 feet).\n\n6 | You determine the elixir's effect by choosing one of the other rows in this table.\n\nNivel 3 - Experimental Elixir\n\nPagina: 14\n\nBeginning at 3rd level, whenever you finish a long rest, you can magically produce an experimental elixir in an empty flask you touch. Roll on the Experimental Elixir table for the elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. As an action, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to an incapacitated creature.\n\nCreating an experimental elixir requires you to have PHB on your person, and any elixir you create with this feature lasts until it is drunk or until the end of your next long rest.\n\nWhen you reach certain levels in this class, you can make more elixirs at the end of a long rest: two at 6th level and three at 15th level. Roll for each elixir's effect separately. Each elixir requires its own flask.\n\nYou can create additional experimental elixirs by expending a spell slot of 1st level or higher for each one. When you do so, you use your action to create the elixir in an empty flask you touch, and you choose the elixir's effect from the Experimental Elixir table.\n\nd6 | Effect\n\n1 | Healing. The drinker regains a number of hit points equal to 2d4 + your Intelligence modifier.\n\n2 | Swiftness. The drinker's walking speed increases by 10 feet for 1 hour.\n\n3 | Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes.\n\n4 | Boldness. The drinker can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to every attack roll and saving throw they make for the next minute.\n\n5 | Flight. The drinker gains a flying speed of 10 feet for 10 minutes.\n\n6 | Transformation. The drinker's body is transformed as if by the alter self spell. The drinker determines the transformation caused by the spell, the effects of which last for 10 minutes.\n\nNivel 3 - Guardian\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYou design your armor to be in the front line of conflict. It has the following features:\n\nThunder Pulse\n\nYou can discharge concussive blasts with strikes from your armor. The pulse counts as a Simple Melee weapon and deals 1d8 Thunder damage on a hit. A creature hit by the pulse has XPHB on attack rolls against targets other than you until the start of your next turn.\n\nDefensive Field\n\nWhile XPHB, you can take a XPHB to gain XPHB equal to your Artificer level. You lose these XPHB if you doff the armor.\n\nNivel 3 - Infiltrator\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYou customize your armor for subtler undertakings. It has the following features:\n\n• Lightning Launcher A gemlike node appears on your armor, from which you can shoot bolts of lightning. The launcher counts as a Simple Ranged weapon with a normal range of 90 feet and a long range of 300 feet, and it deals 1d6 Lightning damage on a hit. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with the launcher, you can deal an extra 1d6 Lightning damage to that target.\n\n• Powered Steps Your XPHB increases by 5 feet.\n\n• Dampening Field You have XPHB on Dexterity (XPHB) checks. If the armor imposes XPHB on such checks, the XPHB and XPHB cancel each other, as normal.\n\nNivel 3 - Lightning Launcher\n\nPagina: 15\n\nA gemlike node appears on one of your armored fists or on the chest (your choice). It counts as a simple ranged weapon, with a normal range of 90 feet and a long range of 300 feet, and it deals 1d6 lightning damage on a hit. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with it, you can deal an extra 1d6 lightning damage to that target.\n\nNivel 3 - Lightning Launcher\n\nNivel 3 - Mapping Magic\n\nPagina: 21\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nIlluminated Cartography\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot, outlining the affected creatures as if in ink. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nPortal Jump\n\nOn your turn, you can spend an amount of movement equal to half your XPHB (round down) to teleport to an unoccupied space you can see within 10 feet of yourself or within 5 feet of a creature that is within 30 feet of you and holding one of your Adventurer's Atlas maps. You can't use this benefit if your XPHB is 0.\n\nNivel 3 - Powered Steps\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYour walking speed increases by 5 feet.\n\nNivel 3 - Powered Steps\n\nNivel 3 - Reanimated Companion\n\nPagina: 15\n\nUsing XPHB or another type of XPHB with which you have proficiency, you can take a XPHB action to create a RHW through the power of necromancy and science. The companion manifests in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you. You determine the companion's appearance; your choices don't affect the companion's game statistics.\n\nThe companion is XPHB to you and your allies and obeys you. It lasts until you finish a XPHB or until you take a XPHB action to dismiss it early, at which point it harmlessly collapses into a pile of viscera. It immediately drops to 0 XPHB and dies (triggering its Death Burst trait) if you die.\n\nOnce you create a companion, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB or expend a spell slot to create one. You can have only one companion at a time and can't create one while your companion is present.\n\nThe Companion in Combat\n\nIn combat, the companion acts during your turn. It can move and take its XPHB on its own, but the only action it takes is the XPHB action unless you take a XPHB to command it to take an action. If you have the XPHB condition, the companion acts on its own and isn't limited to the XPHB action.\n\nNivel 3 - Reanimated Companion\n\nNivel 3 - Reanimator\n\nPagina: 15\n\nReassemble Corpses and Raise the Dead\n\nReanimators defy the laws of nature in pursuit of gruesome experiments. These grim Artificers stitch together servants from disparate corpses, use foul magic to strengthen the living, and transform the art of necromancy into a terrifying science.\n\nNivel 3 - Reanimator Spells\n\nPagina: 15\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Reanimator Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Reanimator's Skill Set\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nJolt to Life\n\nWhen you cast XPHB, you can modify the spell so that it sends a jolt of electricity through the target, reviving it. The target regains a number of XPHB equal to your Artificer level, and each creature of your choice in a 10-foot XPHB originating from the target makes a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 2d4 Lightning damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nYou can modify the spell this way a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB. The Lightning damage of this feature increases by 1d4 when you reach Artificer levels 11 (3d4) and 17 (4d4).\n\nReanimator's Tools\n\nYou gain proficiency with XPHB. If you already have this proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of XPHB of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Steel Defender\n\nPagina: 18\n\nYour tinkering has borne you a companion, a EFA. You determine the defender's appearance and whether it has two legs or four; your choices don't affect the defender's game statistics.\n\nThe EFA is XPHB to you and your allies and obeys you. It vanishes if you die.\n\nThe Defender in Combat\n\nIn combat, the defender acts during your turn. It can move and take its XPHB on its own, but the only action it takes is the XPHB action unless you take a XPHB to command it to take an action. If you have the XPHB condition, the defender acts on its own and isn't limited to the XPHB action.\n\nRestoring or Replacing the Defender\n\nIf the defender has died within the last hour, you can take a XPHB action to touch it and expend a spell slot. The defender returns to life after 1 minute with all its XPHB restored.\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can create a new EFA if you have XPHB in hand. If you already have a defender from this feature, the first one vanishes.\n\nNivel 3 - Steel Defender\n\nPagina: 18\n\nBy 3rd level, your tinkering has borne you a faithful companion, a tce. It is friendly to you and your companions, and it obeys your commands. See this creature's game statistics in the steel defender stat block, which uses your proficiency bonus (PB) in several places. You determine the creature's appearance and whether it has two legs or four; your choice has no effect on its game statistics.\n\nIn combat, the defender shares your initiative count, but it takes its turn immediately after yours. It can move and use its reaction on its own, but the only action it takes on its turn is the Dodge action, unless you take a bonus action on your turn to command it to take another action. That action can be one in its stat block or some other action. If you are incapacitated, the defender can take any action of its choice, not just Dodge.\n\nIf the mending spell is cast on it, it regains 2d6 hit points. If it has died within the last hour, you can use your PHB as an action to revive it, provided you are within 5 feet of it and you expend a spell slot of 1st level or higher. The steel defender returns to life after 1 minute with all its hit points restored.\n\nAt the end of a long rest, you can create a new steel defender if you have your PHB with you. If you already have a steel defender from this feature, the first one immediately perishes. The defender also perishes if you die.\n\nNivel 3 - Steel Defender\n\nNivel 3 - The Right Tool for the Job\n\nPagina: 9\n\n3rd-level artificer feature\n\nYou've learned how to produce exactly the tool you need: with PHB or PHB in hand, you can magically create one set of PHB in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you. This creation requires 1 hour of uninterrupted work, which can coincide with a short or long rest. Though the product of magic, the tools are nonmagical, and they vanish when you use this feature again.\n\nNivel 3 - Thunder Gauntlets\n\nPagina: 15\n\nEach of the armor's gauntlets counts as a simple melee weapon while you aren't holding anything in it, and it deals 1d8 thunder damage on a hit. A creature hit by the gauntlet has disadvantage on attack rolls against targets other than you until the start of your next turn, as the armor magically emits a distracting pulse when the creature attacks someone else.\n\nNivel 3 - Thunder Gauntlets\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nPagina: 14\n\nWhen you adopt this specialization at 3rd level, you gain proficiency with PHB. If you already have this proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of PHB of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nPagina: 17\n\nWhen you adopt this specialization at 3rd level, you gain proficiency with PHB. If you already have this proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of PHB of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nPagina: 18\n\nWhen you adopt this specialization at 3rd level, you gain proficiency with PHB. If you already have this proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of PHB of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nPagina: 12\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nTool Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency with XPHB and the XPHB. If you already have one of these proficiencies, you gain proficiency with one other type of XPHB of your choice (or with two other types if you have both).\n\nPotion Crafting\n\nWhen you brew a potion using the crafting rules in the XDMG, the amount of time required to craft it is halved.\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nArmor Training\n\nYou gain training with Heavy armor.\n\nTool Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency with XPHB. If you already have this tool proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of XPHB of your choice.\n\nArmor Crafting\n\nWhen you craft nonmagical or magic armor, the amount of time required to craft it is halved.\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nPagina: 16\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nRanged Weaponry\n\nYou gain proficiency with items.\n\nTool Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency with XPHB. If you already have this proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of XPHB of your choice.\n\nWand Crafting\n\nWhen you craft a magic XPHB, the amount of time required to craft it is halved.\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nPagina: 18\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nTool Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency with XPHB. If you already have this proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of XPHB of your choice.\n\nWeapon Crafting\n\nWhen you craft a nonmagical or magic weapon, the amount of time required to craft it is halved.\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nPagina: 20\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nTool Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency with XPHB and XPHB. If you already have one of these proficiencies, you gain proficiency with one other type of XPHB of your choice (or with two other types if you have both).\n\nScroll Crafting\n\nWhen you scribe a XDMG using the crafting rules in the PHB, the amount of time required to craft it is halved.\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nPagina: 15\n\n3rd-level Armorer feature\n\nYou gain proficiency with heavy armor. You also gain proficiency with PHB. If you already have this tool proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of PHB of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 10\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feat of your choice for which you qualify. You gain this feature again at Artificer levels 8, 12, and 16.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 9\n\n4th-level artificer feature\n\nWhen you reach 4th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 5 - Alchemical Savant\n\nPagina: 14\n\nWhenever you cast a spell using your XPHB as the XPHB, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore XPHB or be a damage roll that deals Acid, Fire, or Poison damage. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum bonus of +1).\n\nNivel 5 - Alchemical Savant\n\nPagina: 14\n\nAt 5th level, you develop masterful command of magical chemicals, enhancing the healing and damage you create through them. Whenever you cast a spell using your PHB as the spellcasting focus, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore hit points or be a damage roll that deals acid, fire, necrotic, or poison damage, and the bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).\n\nNivel 5 - Arcane Firearm\n\nPagina: 17\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB, you can use XPHB to carve special sigils into a XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, or items and thereby turn it into your Arcane Firearm. The sigils disappear from the object if you later carve them on a different item. The sigils otherwise last indefinitely.\n\nYou can use your Arcane Firearm as a XPHB for your Artificer spells. When you cast an Artificer spell through the firearm, roll 1d8, and you gain a bonus to one of the spell's damage rolls equal to the number rolled.\n\nNivel 5 - Arcane Firearm\n\nPagina: 17\n\nAt 5th level, you know how to turn a wand, staff, or rod into an arcane firearm, a conduit for your destructive spells. When you finish a long rest, you can use PHB to carve special sigils into a wand, staff, or rod and thereby turn it into your arcane firearm. The sigils disappear from the object if you later carve them on a different item. The sigils otherwise last indefinitely.\n\nYou can use your arcane firearm as a spellcasting focus for your artificer spells. When you cast an artificer spell through the firearm, roll a d8, and you gain a bonus to one of the spell's damage rolls equal to the number rolled.\n\nNivel 5 - Arcane Firearm\n\nNivel 5 - Artificer Specialist Feature\n\nPagina: 9\n\n5th-level artificer feature\n\nYou gain a feature granted by your Artificer Specialist choice.\n\nNivel 5 - Extra Attack\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYou can attack twice instead of once whenever you take the XPHB action on your turn.\n\nNivel 5 - Extra Attack\n\nPagina: 19\n\nYou can attack twice instead of once whenever you take the XPHB action on your turn. You can forgo one of your attacks when you take the XPHB action to command your EFA to take the Force-Empowered Rend action.\n\nNivel 5 - Extra Attack\n\nPagina: 15\n\n5th-level Armorer feature\n\nYou can attack twice, rather than once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.\n\nNivel 5 - Extra Attack\n\nPagina: 18\n\nStarting at 5th level, you can attack twice, rather than once, whenever you take the Attack action on your turn.\n\nNivel 5 - Guided Precision\n\nPagina: 21\n\nOnce per turn, whenever you cast a spell from your Cartographer Spells list or hit a creature affected by your XPHB with an attack roll, you can add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of the spell or attack.\n\nIn addition, taking damage can't cause you to lose XPHB on XPHB.\n\nNivel 5 - Strange Modifications\n\nPagina: 16\n\nWhenever you create a RHW, it gains one of the following options of your choice; choose when you create the companion.\n\nArcane Conduit\n\nYou can cast spells as though you were in the companion's space, but you must use your own senses. Once per turn, when you cast an Artificer spell from the Evocation or Necromancy school and deal damage while your companion is within 120 feet of you, you can add your Intelligence modifier to one damage roll of that spell.\n\nFerocity\n\nThe damage die of the companion's Dreadful Swipe increases to 1d6.\n\nNivel 5 - Subclass feature\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYou gain a feature from your Artificer Subclass.\n\nNivel 6 - Magic Item Tinker\n\nPagina: 10\n\nYour Artificer feature gains the following options.\n\nCharge Magic Item\n\nAs a XPHB, you can touch a magic item within 5 feet of yourself that you created with Replicate Magic Item and that uses charges. You expend a level 1+ spell slot and recharge the item. The number of charges the item regains is equal to the level of spell slot expended.\n\nDrain Magic Item\n\nAs a XPHB, you can touch a magic item within 5 feet of yourself that you created with Replicate Magic Item and cause the item to vanish, converting its magical energy into a spell slot. The slot is level 1 if the item is Common or level 2 if the item is Uncommon or Rare. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB. Any spell slot you create with this feature vanishes when you finish a XPHB.\n\nTransmute Magic Item\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can touch one magic item within 5 feet of yourself that you created with Replicate Magic Item and transform it into a different magic item. The resulting item must be based on a magic item plan you know. Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 6 - Tool Expertise\n\nPagina: 9\n\n6th-level artificer feature\n\nYour proficiency bonus is now doubled for any ability check you make that uses your proficiency with a tool.\n\nNivel 7 - Flash of Genius\n\nPagina: 10\n\nWhen you or a creature you can see within 30 feet of you fails an ability check or a saving throw, you can take a XPHB to add a bonus to the roll, potentially causing it to succeed. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).\n\nYou can take this XPHB a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 7 - Flash of Genius\n\nPagina: 9\n\n7th-level artificer feature\n\nYou've gained the ability to come up with solutions under pressure. When you or another creature you can see within 30 feet of you makes an ability check or a saving throw, you can use your reaction to add your Intelligence modifier to the roll.\n\nYou can use this feature a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 10\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feat of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 9\n\n8th-level artificer feature\n\nWhen you reach 8th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 9 - Arcane Jolt\n\nPagina: 19\n\nWhen either you hit a target with an attack roll using a magic weapon or your EFA hits a target, you can channel magical energy through the strike to create one of the following effects:\n\n• Destructive Energy The target takes an extra 2d6 Force damage.\n\n• Restorative Energy Choose one creature or object you can see within 30 feet of the target. Healing energy flows into the chosen recipient, restoring 2d6 XPHB to it.\n\nYou can use this energy a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), but you can do so no more than once per turn. You regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 9 - Arcane Jolt\n\nPagina: 18\n\nAt 9th level, you learn new ways to channel arcane energy to harm or heal. When either you hit a target with a magic weapon attack or your steel defender hits a target, you can channel magical energy through the strike to create one of the following effects:\n\n• The target takes an extra 2d6 force damage.\n\n• Choose one creature or object you can see within 30 feet of the target. Healing energy flows into the chosen recipient, restoring 2d6 hit points to it.\n\nYou can use this energy a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), but you can do so no more than once on a turn. You regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 9 - Armor Modifications\n\nPagina: 15\n\n9th-level Armorer feature\n\nYou learn how to use your artificer infusions to specially modify your Arcane Armor. That armor now counts as separate items for the purposes of your Infuse Items feature: armor (the chest piece), boots, helmet, and the armor's special weapon. Each of those items can bear one of your infusions, and the infusions transfer over if you change your armor's model with the Armor Model feature. In addition, the maximum number of items you can infuse at once increases by 2, but those extra items must be part of your Arcane Armor.\n\nNivel 9 - Artificer Specialist Feature\n\nPagina: 9\n\n9th-level artificer feature\n\nYou gain a feature granted by your Artificer Specialist choice.\n\nNivel 9 - Explosive Cannon\n\nPagina: 17\n\nEvery EFA you create is now more destructive. You gain the following benefits.\n\nDetonate\n\nWhen your cannon takes damage, you can take a XPHB to command the cannon to detonate if you are within 60 feet of it. Doing so destroys the cannon and forces each creature within 20 feet of it to make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 3d10 Force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nFirepower\n\nThe cannon's damage rolls and the number of XPHB granted by Protector increase by 1d8.\n\nNivel 9 - Explosive Cannon\n\nPagina: 17\n\nStarting at 9th level, every eldritch cannon you create is more destructive:\n\n• The cannon's damage rolls all increase by 1d8.\n\n• As an action, you can command the cannon to detonate if you are within 60 feet of it. Doing so destroys the cannon and forces each creature within 20 feet of it to make a Dexterity saving throw against your spell save DC, taking 3d8 force damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nNivel 9 - Improved Armorer\n\nPagina: 15\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nArmor Replication\n\nYou learn an additional plan for your Replicate Magic Item feature, and it must be in the Armor category. If you replace that plan, you must replace it with another Armor plan.\n\nIn addition, you can create an additional item with that feature, and the item must also be in the Armor category.\n\nImproved Arsenal\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with the special weapon of your Arcane Armor model.\n\nNivel 9 - Improved Reanimation\n\nPagina: 16\n\nThe damage of your RHW Death Burst increases to 4d4. Necrotic damage dealt by your companion ignores XPHB.\n\nNivel 9 - Ingenious Movement\n\nPagina: 21\n\nWhen you use your Artificer, you or a willing creature of your choice that you can see within 30 feet of yourself can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see as part of that same XPHB.\n\nNivel 9 - Macabre Modifications\n\nPagina: 16\n\nYou experiment and alter your companion further. Whenever you create a RHW, the companion now gains two options for Strange Modifications, instead of one. Additionally, when picking options for Strange Modifications, you can also choose from the following options.\n\nBloated\n\nThe companion becomes Large. Whenever it hits a Large or smaller creature with its Dreadful Swipe action, that creature is pushed up to 10 feet away from the companion. Additionally, you can add your Intelligence modifier to the damage dealt by the companion's Death Burst.\n\nGaunt\n\nThe companion's XPHB increases to 45 feet, and it gains a XPHB equal to its XPHB. It can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check. In addition, whenever a creature of your choice starts its turn within a 10-foot XPHB originating from your companion, the creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC or have the XPHB condition until the start of its next turn.\n\nMoist\n\nThe companion gains a XPHB equal to its XPHB, and it can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch without expending extra movement to do so. In addition, whenever the companion is hit by an attack roll from a creature within 10 feet of itself, the attacker takes Acid damage equal to your Intelligence modifier.\n\nNivel 9 - Restorative Reagents\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you use XPHB as the XPHB. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 9 - Restorative Reagents\n\nPagina: 14\n\nStarting at 9th level, you can incorporate restorative reagents into some of your works:\n\n• Whenever a creature drinks an experimental elixir you created, the creature gains temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 temporary hit point).\n\n• You can cast lesser restoration without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you use PHB as the spellcasting focus. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 9 - Subclass feature\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYou gain a feature from your Artificer Subclass.\n\nNivel 10 - Magic Item Adept\n\nPagina: 10\n\nYou can now attune to up to four magic items at once.\n\nNivel 10 - Magic Item Adept\n\nPagina: 9\n\n10th-level artificer feature\n\nYou've achieved a profound understanding of how to use and make magic items:\n\n• You can attune to up to four magic items at once.\n\n• If you craft a magic item with a rarity of common or uncommon, it takes you a quarter of the normal time, and it costs you half as much of the usual gold.\n\nNivel 11 - Spell-Storing Item\n\nPagina: 11\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB, you can touch one Simple or Martial weapon or one item that you can use as a XPHB, and you store a spell in it, choosing a level 1, 2, or 3 Artificer spell that has a casting time of an action and doesn't require a Material component that is consumed by the spell (you needn't have the spell prepared).\n\nWhile holding the object, a creature can take a XPHB action to produce the spell's effect from it, using your spellcasting ability modifier. If the spell requires XPHB, the creature must concentrate. Once a creature has used the object to produce the spell's effect, the object can't be used this way again until the start of the creature's next turn.\n\nThe spell stays in the object until it's been used a number of times equal to twice your Intelligence modifier (minimum of twice) or until you use this feature again to store a spell in an object.\n\nNivel 11 - Spell-Storing Item\n\nPagina: 9\n\n11th-level artificer feature\n\nYou can now store a spell in an object. Whenever you finish a long rest, you can touch one items or one item that you can use as a spellcasting focus, and you store a spell in it, choosing a 1st- or 2nd-level spell from the spells that requires 1 action to cast (you needn't have it prepared).\n\nWhile holding the object, a creature can take an action to produce the spell's effect from it, using your spellcasting ability modifier. If the spell requires concentration, the creature must concentrate. The spell stays in the object until it's been used a number of times equal to twice your Intelligence modifier (minimum of twice) or until you use this feature again to store a spell in an object.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 10\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feat of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 9\n\n12th-level artificer feature\n\nWhen you reach 12th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 14 - Advanced Artifice\n\nPagina: 11\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nMagic Item Savant\n\nYou can now attune to up to five magic items at once.\n\nRefreshed Genius\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB, you regain one expended use of your Artificer feature.\n\nNivel 14 - Magic Item Savant\n\nPagina: 9\n\n14th-level artificer feature\n\nYour skill with magic items deepens:\n\n• You can attune to up to five magic items at once.\n\n• You ignore all class, race, spell, and level requirements on attuning to or using a magic item.\n\nNivel 15 - Artificer Specialist Feature\n\nPagina: 9\n\n15th-level artificer feature\n\nYou gain a feature granted by your Artificer Specialist choice.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAlchemical Eruption\n\nWhen you cast an Artificer spell that deals Acid, Fire, or Poison damage to a target, you can also deal 2d8 Force damage to that target. You can use this benefit only once on each of your turns.\n\nChemical Resistance\n\nYou gain XPHB to Acid damage and Poison damage. You also gain XPHB to the XPHB condition.\n\nConjured Cauldron\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without Material components, provided you use XPHB as the XPHB. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nPagina: 14\n\nBy 15th level, you have been exposed to so many chemicals that they pose little risk to you, and you can use them to quickly end certain ailments:\n\n• You gain resistance to acid damage and poison damage, and you are immune to the poisoned condition.\n\n• You can cast greater restoration and heal without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without material components, provided you use PHB as the spellcasting focus. Once you cast either spell with this feature, you can't cast that spell with it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nNivel 15 - Fortified Position\n\nPagina: 17\n\nYou're a master at forming well-defended emplacements using your EFA. You gain the following benefits.\n\nDouble Firepower\n\nYou can now have two cannons at the same time, and you can create two with the same XPHB action. (If you expend a spell slot to create the first cannon, you must expend another spell slot to create the second.) You can activate both of them with the same XPHB, ordering them to use the same activation option or different ones. You can't create a third cannon while you have two.\n\nShimmering Field Projection\n\nYou and your allies have XPHB while within 10 feet of your EFA.\n\nNivel 15 - Fortified Position\n\nPagina: 17\n\nStarting at 15th level, you're a master at forming well-defended emplacements using Eldritch Cannon:\n\n• You and your allies have Cover while within 10 feet of a cannon you create with Eldritch Cannon, as a result of a shimmering field of magical protection that the cannon emits.\n\n• You can now have two cannons at the same time. You can create two with the same action (but not the same spell slot), and you can activate both of them with the same bonus action. You determine whether the cannons are identical to each other or different. You can't create a third cannon while you have two.\n\nNivel 15 - Guardian\n\nPagina: 15\n\nWhen a Huge or smaller creature you can see ends its turn within 30 feet of you, you can use your reaction to magically force it to make a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, you pull the creature up to 25 feet directly to an unoccupied space. If you pull the target to a space within 5 feet of you, you can make a melee weapon attack against it as part of this reaction.\n\nYou can use this reaction a number of times equal to your proficiency bonus, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 15 - Improved Defender\n\nPagina: 19\n\nYour Artificer and EFA have become more powerful, granting these benefits.\n\nImproved Jolt\n\nThe extra damage and healing of your Arcane Jolt both increase to 4d6.\n\nImproved Deflection\n\nWhenever your EFA uses its Deflect Attack, the attacker takes Force damage equal to 1d4 plus your Intelligence modifier.\n\nNivel 15 - Improved Defender\n\nPagina: 18\n\nAt 15th level, your Arcane Jolt and steel defender become more powerful:\n\n• The extra damage and the healing of your Arcane Jolt both increase to 4d6.\n\n• Your steel defender gains a +2 bonus to XPHB.\n\n• Whenever your steel defender uses its Deflect Attack, the attacker takes force damage equal to 1d4 + your Intelligence modifier.\n\nNivel 15 - Infiltrator\n\nPagina: 15\n\nAny creature that takes lightning damage from your Lightning Launcher glimmers with magical light until the start of your next turn. The glimmering creature sheds dim light in a 5-foot radius, and it has disadvantage on attack rolls against you, as the light jolts it if it attacks you. In addition, the next attack roll against it has advantage, and if that attack hits, the target takes an extra 1d6 lightning damage.\n\nNivel 15 - Perfected Armor\n\nPagina: 16\n\nYour Arcane Armor gains additional benefits based on its model, as detailed below.\n\nDreadnaught\n\nThe damage die of your Force Demolisher increases to 2d6 Force damage.\n\nIn addition, when you use your Giant Stature, your reach increases by 10 feet, your size can increase to Large or Huge (your choice), and you have XPHB on Strength checks and Strength saving throws for the duration.\n\nGuardian\n\nThe damage die of your Thunder Pulse increases to 1d10 Thunder damage.\n\nIn addition, when a Huge or smaller creature you can see ends its turn within 30 feet of you, you can take a XPHB to magically force that creature to make a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, you pull the creature up to 25 feet directly toward you to an unoccupied space. If you pull the target to a space within 5 feet of yourself, you can make a melee weapon attack against it as part of this XPHB.\n\nYou can take this XPHB a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nInfiltrator\n\nThe damage die of your Lightning Launcher increases to 2d6 Lightning damage. Any creature that takes Lightning damage from your Lightning Launcher glimmers with magical light until the start of your next turn. The glimmering creature sheds XPHB in a 5-foot radius, and it has XPHB on attack rolls against you, as the light jolts it if it attacks you.\n\nAdditionally, as a XPHB, you can gain a XPHB equal to twice your XPHB until the end of the current turn. You can take this XPHB a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 15 - Perfected Armor\n\nPagina: 15\n\n15th-level Armorer feature\n\nYour Arcane Armor gains additional benefits based on its model, as shown below.\n\nNivel 15 - Refined Reanimation\n\nPagina: 16\n\nYou have mastered the science of revivification, granting you the following benefits.\n\nFacilitated Revival\n\nYou can cast XPHB once without expending a spell slot and without Material components, provided you use XPHB or another type of XPHB with which you have proficiency as the XPHB. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nLife Transfer\n\nYou can siphon the animating magic of your RHW to bolster yourself. When you or your companion takes damage, you can take a XPHB to gain a number of XPHB equal to your companion's current XPHB. The companion then immediately drops to 0 XPHB and dies (triggering its Death Burst trait).\n\nSuperior Modifications\n\nWhenever you create a RHW, the companion now gains three options for Strange Modifications.\n\nNivel 15 - Refined Reanimation\n\nNivel 15 - Subclass feature\n\nPagina: 8\n\nYou gain a feature from your Artificer Subclass.\n\nNivel 15 - Superior Atlas\n\nPagina: 21\n\nYour Adventurer's Atlas improves, gaining the following benefits.\n\nSafe Haven\n\nWhen a map holder would be reduced to 0 XPHB but not killed outright, that creature can destroy its map. The creature's XPHB instead change to a number equal to twice your Artificer level, and the creature is teleported to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you or another map holder of its choice.\n\nUnerring Path\n\nIf you are one of the map holders for your Adventurer's Atlas, you can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without needing spell components. Once you use this benefit, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 10\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feat of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 9\n\n16th-level artificer feature\n\nWhen you reach 16th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 18 - Magic Item Master\n\nPagina: 11\n\nYou can now attune to up to six magic items at once.\n\nNivel 18 - Magic Item Master\n\nPagina: 9\n\n18th-level artificer feature\n\nYou can now attune to up to six magic items at once.\n\nNivel 19 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 9\n\n19th-level artificer feature\n\nWhen you reach 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nPagina: 11\n\nYou gain an Epic Boon feat or another feat of your choice for which you qualify. XPHB is recommended.\n\nNivel 20 - Soul of Artifice\n\nPagina: 11\n\nYou have developed a mystical connection to your magic items, which you can draw on for aid. You gain the following benefits.\n\nCheat Death\n\nIf you're reduced to 0 XPHB but not killed outright, you can disintegrate any number of Uncommon or Rare magic items created by your Replicate Magic Item feature. If you do so, your XPHB instead change to a number equal to 20 times the number of magic items disintegrated.\n\nMagical Guidance\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB, you regain all expended uses of your Artificer if you have XPHB to at least one magic item.\n\nNivel 20 - Soul of Artifice\n\nPagina: 9\n\n20th-level artificer feature\n\nYou have developed a mystical connection to your magic items, which you can draw on for protection:\n\n• You gain a +1 bonus to all saving throws per magic item you are currently attuned to.\n\n• If you're reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, you can use your reaction to end one of your artificer infusions, causing you to drop to 1 hit point instead of 0.\n\n=== SUBCLASSES ===\n\nAlchemist [TCE]\n\nPagina: 14\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 12\n\nCraft Magic Elixirs and Potions\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce magical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 14\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce mystical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away. Alchemy is the oldest of artificer traditions, and its versatility has long been valued during times of war and peace.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Alchemist Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 14\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Alchemist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | healing word, ray of sickness\n\n5th | flaming sphere, Melf's acid arrow\n\n9th | gaseous form, mass healing word\n\n13th | blight, death ward\n\n17th | cloudkill, raise dead\n\nNivel 3 - Experimental Elixir\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB while holding XPHB, you can use that tool to magically produce two elixirs. For each elixir, roll on the Experimental Elixir table for the elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. The elixir appears in a vial, and the vial vanishes when the elixir is drunk or poured out. If any elixir remains when you finish a XPHB, the elixir and its vial vanish.\n\nDrinking an Elixir\n\nAs a XPHB, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to another creature within 5 feet of itself.\n\nCreating Additional Elixirs\n\nAs a XPHB action while holding XPHB, you can expend one spell slot to create another elixir. When you do so, you choose its effect from the Experimental Elixir table rather than rolling.\n\nWhen you reach certain Artificer levels, you can make an additional elixir at the end of each XPHB: a total of three at level 5, four at level 9, and five at level 15.\n\n1d6 | Effect\n\n1 | Healing. The drinker regains a number of XPHB equal to 2d8 plus your Intelligence modifier. The number of XPHB restored increases by 1d8 when you reach Artificer levels 9 (3d8) and 15 (4d8).\n\n2 | Swiftness. The drinker's XPHB increases by 10 feet for 1 hour. This bonus increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (15 feet) and 15 (20 feet).\n\n3 | Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes. The duration increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (1 hour) and 15 (8 hours).\n\n4 | Boldness. The drinker can roll 1d4 and add the number rolled to every attack roll and saving throw they make for the next minute. The duration increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (10 minutes) and 15 (1 hour).\n\n5 | Flight. The drinker gains a XPHB of 10 feet for 10 minutes. The XPHB increases when you reach Artificer levels 9 (20 feet) and 15 (30 feet).\n\n6 | You determine the elixir's effect by choosing one of the other rows in this table.\n\nNivel 3 - Experimental Elixir\n\nPagina: 14\n\nBeginning at 3rd level, whenever you finish a long rest, you can magically produce an experimental elixir in an empty flask you touch. Roll on the Experimental Elixir table for the elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. As an action, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to an incapacitated creature.\n\nCreating an experimental elixir requires you to have PHB on your person, and any elixir you create with this feature lasts until it is drunk or until the end of your next long rest.\n\nWhen you reach certain levels in this class, you can make more elixirs at the end of a long rest: two at 6th level and three at 15th level. Roll for each elixir's effect separately. Each elixir requires its own flask.\n\nYou can create additional experimental elixirs by expending a spell slot of 1st level or higher for each one. When you do so, you use your action to create the elixir in an empty flask you touch, and you choose the elixir's effect from the Experimental Elixir table.\n\nd6 | Effect\n\n1 | Healing. The drinker regains a number of hit points equal to 2d4 + your Intelligence modifier.\n\n2 | Swiftness. The drinker's walking speed increases by 10 feet for 1 hour.\n\n3 | Resilience. The drinker gains a +1 bonus to AC for 10 minutes.\n\n4 | Boldness. The drinker can roll a d4 and add the number rolled to every attack roll and saving throw they make for the next minute.\n\n5 | Flight. The drinker gains a flying speed of 10 feet for 10 minutes.\n\n6 | Transformation. The drinker's body is transformed as if by the alter self spell. The drinker determines the transformation caused by the spell, the effects of which last for 10 minutes.\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nPagina: 14\n\nWhen you adopt this specialization at 3rd level, you gain proficiency with PHB. If you already have this proficiency, you gain proficiency with one other type of PHB of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Tool Proficiency\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nPagina: 12\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nTool Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency with XPHB and the XPHB. If you already have one of these proficiencies, you gain proficiency with one other type of XPHB of your choice (or with two other types if you have both).\n\nPotion Crafting\n\nWhen you brew a potion using the crafting rules in the XDMG, the amount of time required to craft it is halved.\n\nNivel 3 - Tools of the Trade\n\nNivel 5 - Alchemical Savant\n\nPagina: 14\n\nWhenever you cast a spell using your XPHB as the XPHB, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore XPHB or be a damage roll that deals Acid, Fire, or Poison damage. The bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum bonus of +1).\n\nNivel 5 - Alchemical Savant\n\nPagina: 14\n\nAt 5th level, you develop masterful command of magical chemicals, enhancing the healing and damage you create through them. Whenever you cast a spell using your PHB as the spellcasting focus, you gain a bonus to one roll of the spell. That roll must restore hit points or be a damage roll that deals acid, fire, necrotic, or poison damage, and the bonus equals your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1).\n\nNivel 9 - Restorative Reagents\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you use XPHB as the XPHB. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 9 - Restorative Reagents\n\nPagina: 14\n\nStarting at 9th level, you can incorporate restorative reagents into some of your works:\n\n• Whenever a creature drinks an experimental elixir you created, the creature gains temporary hit points equal to 2d6 + your Intelligence modifier (minimum of 1 temporary hit point).\n\n• You can cast lesser restoration without expending a spell slot and without preparing the spell, provided you use PHB as the spellcasting focus. You can do so a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum of once), and you regain all expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nPagina: 14\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nAlchemical Eruption\n\nWhen you cast an Artificer spell that deals Acid, Fire, or Poison damage to a target, you can also deal 2d8 Force damage to that target. You can use this benefit only once on each of your turns.\n\nChemical Resistance\n\nYou gain XPHB to Acid damage and Poison damage. You also gain XPHB to the XPHB condition.\n\nConjured Cauldron\n\nYou can cast XPHB without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without Material components, provided you use XPHB as the XPHB. Once you use this feature, you can't use it again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nPagina: 14\n\nBy 15th level, you have been exposed to so many chemicals that they pose little risk to you, and you can use them to quickly end certain ailments:\n\n• You gain resistance to acid damage and poison damage, and you are immune to the poisoned condition.\n\n• You can cast greater restoration and heal without expending a spell slot, without preparing the spell, and without material components, provided you use PHB as the spellcasting focus. Once you cast either spell with this feature, you can't cast that spell with it again until you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nNivel 15 - Chemical Mastery\n\nAlchemist [TCE]\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 12\n\nCraft Magic Elixirs and Potions\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce magical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist\n\nPagina: 14\n\nAn Alchemist is an expert at combining reagents to produce mystical effects. Alchemists use their creations to give life and to leech it away. Alchemy is the oldest of artificer traditions, and its versatility has long been valued during times of war and peace.\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhen you reach an Artificer level specified in the Alchemist Spells table, you thereafter always have the listed spells prepared.\n\nArtificer Level | Spells\n\n3 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n5 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n9 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n13 | XPHB, XPHB\n\n17 | XPHB, XPHB\n\nNivel 3 - Alchemist Spells\n\nPagina: 14\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you always have certain spells prepared after you reach particular levels in this class, as shown in the Alchemist Spells table. These spells count as artificer spells for you, but they don't count against the number of artificer spells you prepare.\n\nArtificer Level | Spell\n\n3rd | healing word, ray of sickness\n\n5th | flaming sphere, Melf's acid arrow\n\n9th | gaseous form, mass healing word\n\n13th | blight, death ward\n\n17th | cloudkill, raise dead\n\nNivel 3 - Experimental Elixir\n\nPagina: 13\n\nWhenever you finish a XPHB while holding XPHB, you can use that tool to magically produce two elixirs. For each elixir, roll on the Experimental Elixir table for the elixir's effect, which is triggered when someone drinks the elixir. The elixir appears in a vial, and the vial vanishes when the elixir is drunk or poured out. If any elixir remains when you finish a XPHB, the elixir and its vial vanish.\n\nDrinking an Elixir\n\nAs a XPHB, a creature can drink the elixir or administer it to another creature within 5 feet of itself.\n\nCreating Additional Elixirs\n\nAs a XPHB action while holding XPHB, you can expend one spell slot to create another elixir. When you do so, you choose its effect from the Experimental Elixir table rather than rolling.\n\nWhen you reach certain Artificer levels, you can make an additional elixir at the end of each XPHB: a total of three at level 5, four at level 9, and five at level 15.\n\n1d6 | Effect\n\n1 | Heali