Sudden Strike\n\nYou can make another attack with the same weapon against a different creature that is within 5 feet of the original target and that is within the weapon's range.\n\nMass Fear\n\nThe target and each creature within 10 feet of it must make a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failed save, a creature has the XPHB condition until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 11 - Stalker's Flurry\n\nNivel 15 - Shadowy Dodge\n\nPagina: 41\n\nStarting at 15th level, you can dodge in unforeseen ways, with wisps of supernatural shadow around you. Whenever a creature makes an attack roll against you and doesn't have advantage on the roll, you can use your reaction to impose disadvantage on it. You must use this feature before you know the outcome of the attack roll.\n\nNivel 15 - Shadowy Dodge\n\nPagina: 126\n\nWhen a creature makes an attack roll against you, you can take a XPHB to impose XPHB on that roll. Whether the attack hits or misses, you can then teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see.\n\nNivel 15 - Shadowy Dodge\n\nGloom Stalker [XPHB]\n\nPagina: 125\n\nNivel 3 - Dread Ambusher\n\nPagina: 41\n\nAt 3rd level, you master the art of the ambush. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Wisdom modifier.\n\nAt the start of your first turn of each combat, your walking speed increases by 10 feet, which lasts until the end of that turn. If you take the Attack action on that turn, you can make one additional weapon attack as part of that action. If that attack hits, the target takes an extra 1d8 damage of the weapon's damage type.\n\nNivel 3 - Dread Ambusher\n\nPagina: 125\n\nYou have mastered the art of creating fearsome ambushes, granting you the following benefits.\n\nAmbusher's Leap\n\nAt the start of your first turn of each combat, your XPHB increases by 10 feet until the end of that turn.\n\nDreadful Strike\n\nWhen you attack a creature and hit it with a weapon, you can deal an extra 2d6 Psychic 