following traits:\n\nPsychic Blade\n\nThe blade vanishes immediately after it hits or misses its target, and it leaves no mark if it deals damage.\n\nAfter you attack with the blade on your turn, you can make a melee or ranged attack with a second psychic blade as a XPHB on the same turn if your other hand is free to create it. The damage die of this bonus attack is 1d4 instead of 1d6.\n\nNivel 3 - Psychic Whispers\n\nPagina: 63\n\nYou can establish telepathic communication between yourself and others-perfect for quiet infiltration. As an action, choose one or more creatures you can see, up to a number of creatures equal to your proficiency bonus, and then roll one Psionic Energy die. For a number of hours equal to the number rolled, the chosen creatures can speak telepathically with you, and you can speak telepathically with them. To send or receive a message (no action required), you and the other creature must be within 1 mile of each other. A creature can't use this telepathy if it can't speak any languages, and a creature can end the telepathic connection at any time (no action required). You and the creature don't need to speak a common language to understand each other.\n\nThe first time you use this power after each long rest, you don't expend the Psionic Energy die. All other times you use the power, you expend the die.\n\nNivel 3 - Psychic Whispers\n\nPagina: 135\n\nYou can establish telepathic communication between yourself and others. As a XPHB action, choose one or more creatures you can see, up to a number of creatures equal to your XPHB, and then roll one Psionic Energy Die. For a number of hours equal to the number rolled, the chosen creatures can speak telepathically with you, and you can speak telepathically with them. To send or receive a message (no action required), you and the other creature must be within 1 mile of each other. A creature can end the telepathic connection at any time (no action required).\n\nNivel 3 - Psychic Whispers\n\nNivel 3 - Soulknife\n\nPagina: 63\n\nMost assassins strike with physical weapons, and many burglars and spies use PHB to infiltrate secure locations. In contrast, a Soulknife strikes and infiltrates with the mind, cutting through barriers both physical and psychic. These rogues discover psionic power within themselves and channel it to do their roguish work. They find easy employment as members of thieves' guilds, though they are often mistrusted by rogues who are leery of anyone using strange mind powers to conduct their business. Most governments would also be happy to employ a Soulknife as a spy.\n\nAmid the trees of ancient forests on the Material Plane and in the Feywild, some wood elves walk the path of the Soulknife, serving as silent, lethal guardians of their woods. In the endless war among the gith, a githzerai is encouraged to become a Soulknife when stealth is required against the githyanki foe.\n\nAs a Soulknife, your psionic abilities might have haunted you since you were a child, only revealing their full potential as you experienced the stress of adventure. Or you might have sought out a reclusive order of psychic adepts and spent years learning how to manifest your power.\n\nNivel 3 - Soulknife\n\nPagina: 135\n\nStrike Foes with Psionic Blades\n\nA Soulknife strikes with the mind, cutting through barriers both physical and psychic. These Rogues discover psionic power within themselves and channel it to do their roguish work. As a Soulknife, your psionic abilities might have haunted you since childhood, revealing their full potential only as you experienced the stress of adventure. Or you might have sought out an order of psychic adepts and spent years learning how to manifest your power.\n\nNivel 9 - Homing Strikes\n\nPagina: 63\n\nIf you make an attack roll with your Psychic Blades and miss the target, you can roll one Psionic Energy die and add the number rolled to the attack roll. If this causes the attack to hit, you expend the Psionic Energy die.\n\nNivel 9 - Homing Strikes\n\nPagina: 136\n\nIf you make an attack roll with your XPHB and miss the target, you can roll one Psionic Energy Die and add the number rolled to the attack roll. If this causes the attack to hit, the die is expended.\n\nNivel 9 - Homing Strikes\n\nNivel 9 - Psychic Teleportation\n\nPagina: 63\n\nAs a bonus action, you manifest one of your Psychic Blades, expend one Psionic Energy die and roll it, and throw the blade at an unoccupied space you can see, up to a number of feet away equal to 10 times the number rolled. You then teleport to that space, and the blade vanishes.\n\nNivel 9 - Psychic Teleportation\n\nPagina: 136\n\nAs a XPHB, you manifest a XPHB, expend one Psionic Energy Die and roll it, and throw the blade at an unoccupied space you can see up to a number of feet away equal to 10 times the number rolled. You then teleport to that space, and the blade vanishes.\n\nNivel 9 - Psychic Teleportation\n\nNivel 9 - Soul Blades\n\nPagina: 63\n\n9th-level Soulknife feature\n\nYour Psychic Blades are now an expression of your psi-suffused soul, giving you these powers that use your Psionic Energy dice:\n\nNivel 9 - Soul Blades\n\nPagina: 136\n\nYou can now use the following powers with your Psychic Blades.\n\nNivel 13 - Psychic Veil\n\nPagina: 63\n\n13th-level Soulknife feature\n\nYou can weave a veil of psychic static to mask yourself. As an action, you can magically become invisible, along with anything you are wearing or carrying, for 1 hour or until you dismiss this effect (no action required). This invisibility ends early immediately after you deal damage to a creature or you force a creature to make a saving throw.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend a Psionic Energy die to use this feature again.\n\nNivel 13 - Psychic Veil\n\nPagina: 136\n\nYou can weave a veil of psychic static to mask yourself. As a XPHB action, you gain the XPHB condition for 1 hour or until you dismiss this effect (no action required). This invisibility ends early immediately after you deal damage to a creature or you force a creature to make a saving throw.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB unless you expend a Psionic Energy Die (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nNivel 13 - Psychic Veil\n\nNivel 17 - Rend Mind\n\nPagina: 63\n\n17th-level Soulknife feature\n\nYou can sweep your Psychic Blades directly through a creature's mind. When you use your Psychic Blades to deal Sneak Attack damage to a creature, you can force that target to make a Wisdom saving throw (DC equal to 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Dexterity modifier). If the save fails, the target is stunned for 1 minute. The stunned target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest, unless you expend three Psionic Energy dice to use it again.\n\nNivel 17 - Rend Mind\n\nPagina: 136\n\nYou can sweep your Psychic Blades through a creature's mind. When you use your Psychic Blades to deal Sneak Attack damage to a creature, you can force that target to make a Wisdom saving throw (8 plus your Dexterity modifier and XPHB). If the save fails, the target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. The XPHB target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nOnce you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB unless you expend three Psionic Energy Dice (no action required) to restore your use of it.\n\nNivel 17 - Rend Mind\n\nSwashbuckler [XGE]\n\nPagina: 48\n\nNivel 3 - Fancy Footwork\n\nPagina: 48\n\nWhen you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you learn how to land a strike and then slip away without reprisal. During your turn, if you make a melee attack against a creature, that creature can't make opportunity attacks against you for the rest of your turn.\n\nNivel 3 - Rakish Audacity\n\nPagina: 48\n\nStarting at 3rd level, your confidence propels you into battle. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Charisma modifier.\n\nYou also gain an additional way to use your Sneak Attack; you don't need advantage on your attack roll to use Sneak Attack against a creature if you are within 5 feet of it, no other creatures are within 5 feet of you, and you don't have disadvantage on the attack roll. All the other rules for Sneak Attack still apply to you.\n\nNivel 3 - Swashbuckler\n\nPagina: 48\n\nYou focus your training on the art of the blade, relying on speed, elegance, and charm in equal parts. While some warriors are brutes clad in heavy armor, your method of fighting looks almost like a performance. Duelists and pirates typically belong to this archetype.\n\nA Swashbuckler excels in single combat, and can fight with two weapons while safely darting away from an opponent.\n\nNivel 9 - Panache\n\nPagina: 48\n\nAt 9th level, your charm becomes extraordinarily beguiling. As an action, you can make a Charisma (Persuasion) check contested by a creature's Wisdom (Insight) check. The creature must be able to hear you, and the two of you must share a language.\n\nIf you succeed on the check and the creature is hostile to you, it has disadvantage on attack rolls against targets other than you and can't make opportunity attacks against targets other than you. This effect lasts for 1 minute, until one of your companions attacks the target or affects it with a spell, or until you and the target are more than 60 feet apart.\n\nIf you succeed on the check and the creature isn't hostile to you, it is charmed by you for 1 minute. While charmed, it regards you as a friendly acquaintance. This effect ends immediately if you or your companions do anything harmful to it.\n\nNivel 13 - Elegant Maneuver\n\nPagina: 48\n\nStarting at 13th level, you can use a bonus action on your turn to gain advantage on the next Dexterity (Acrobatics) or Strength (Athletics) check you make during the same turn.\n\nNivel 17 - Master Duelist\n\nPagina: 48\n\nBeginning at 17th level, your mastery of the blade lets you turn failure into success in combat. If you miss with an attack roll, you can roll it again with advantage. Once you do so, you can't use this feature again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nSwashbuckler [XGE]\n\nNivel 3 - Fancy Footwork\n\nPagina: 48\n\nWhen you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you learn how to land a strike and then slip away without reprisal. During your turn, if you make a melee attack against a creature, that creature can't make opportunity attacks against you for the rest of your turn.\n\nNivel 3 - Rakish Audacity\n\nPagina: 48\n\nStarting at 3rd level, your confidence propels you into battle. You can give yourself a bonus to your initiative rolls equal to your Charisma modifier.\n\nYou also gain an additional way to use your Sneak Attack; you don't need advantage on your attack roll to use Sneak Attack against a creature if you are within 5 feet of it, no other creatures are within 5 feet of you, and you don't have disadvantage on the attack roll. All the other rules for Sneak Attack still apply to you.\n\nNivel 3 - Swashbuckler\n\nPagina: 48\n\nYou focus your training on the art of the blade, relying on speed, elegance, and charm in equal parts. While some warriors are brutes clad in heavy armor, your method of fighting looks almost like a performance. Duelists and pirates typically belong to this archetype.\n\nA Swashbuckler excels in single combat, and can fight with two weapons while safely darting away from an opponent.\n\nNivel 9 - Panache\n\nPagina: 48\n\nAt 9th level, your charm becomes extraordinarily beguiling. As an action, you can make a Charisma (Persuasion) check contested by a creature's Wisdom (Insight) check. The creature must be able to hear you, and the two of you must share a language.\n\nIf you succeed on the check and the creature is hostile to you, it has disadvantage on attack rolls against targets other than you and can't make opportunity attacks against targets other than you. This effect lasts for 1 minute, until one of your companions attacks the target or affects it with a spell, or until you and the target are more than 60 feet apart.\n\nIf you succeed on the check and the creature isn't hostile to you, it is charmed by you for 1 minute. While charmed, it regards you as a friendly acquaintance. This effect ends immediately if you or your companions do anything harmful to it.\n\nNivel 13 - Elegant Maneuver\n\nPagina: 48\n\nStarting at 13th level, you can use a bonus action on your turn to gain advantage on the next Dexterity (Acrobatics) or Strength (Athletics) check you make during the same turn.\n\nNivel 17 - Master Duelist\n\nPagina: 48\n\nBeginning at 17th level, your mastery of the blade lets you turn failure into success in combat. If you miss with an attack roll, you can roll it again with advantage. Once you do so, you can't use this feature again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nThief [PHB]\n\nPagina: 97\n\nNivel 3 - Fast Hands\n\nPagina: 97\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you can use the bonus action granted by your Cunning Action to make a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check, use your phb to disarm a trap or open a lock, or take the Use an Object action.\n\nNivel 3 - Fast Hands\n\nPagina: 137\n\nAs a XPHB, you can do one of the following.\n\nSleight of Hand\n\nMake a Dexterity (XPHB) check to pick a lock or disarm a trap with XPHB or to pick a pocket.\n\nUse an Object\n\nTake the XPHB action, or take the XPHB action to use a magic item that requires that action.\n\nNivel 3 - Fast Hands\n\nNivel 3 - Second-Story Work\n\nPagina: 97\n\nWhen you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain the ability to climb faster than normal; climbing no longer costs you extra movement.\n\nIn addition, when you make a running jump, the distance you cover increases by a number of feet equal to your Dexterity modifier.\n\nNivel 3 - Second-Story Work\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou've trained to get into especially hard-to-reach places, granting you these benefits.\n\nClimber\n\nYou gain a XPHB equal to your XPHB.\n\nJumper\n\nYou can determine your jump distance using your Dexterity rather than your Strength.\n\nNivel 3 - Thief\n\nPagina: 97\n\nYou hone your skills in the larcenous arts. Burglars, bandits, cutpurses, and other criminals typically follow this archetype, but so do rogues who prefer to think of themselves as professional treasure seekers, explorers, delvers, and investigators. In addition to improving your agility and stealth, you learn skills useful for delving into ancient ruins, reading unfamiliar languages, and using magic items you normally couldn't employ.\n\nNivel 3 - Thief\n\nPagina: 137\n\nHunt for Treasure as a Classic Adventurer\n\nA mix of burglar, treasure hunter, and explorer, you are the epitome of an adventurer. In addition to improving your agility and stealth, you gain abilities useful for delving into ruins and getting maximum benefit from the magic items you find there.\n\nNivel 9 - Supreme Sneak\n\nPagina: 97\n\nStarting at 9th level, you have advantage on a Dexterity (Stealth) check if you move no more than half your speed on the same turn.\n\nNivel 9 - Supreme Sneak\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou gain the following Cunning Strike option.\n\nStealth Attack (Cost: 1d6)\n\nIf you have the XPHB action's XPHB condition, this attack doesn't end that condition on you if you end the turn behind XPHB or XPHB.\n\nNivel 13 - Use Magic Device\n\nPagina: 97\n\nBy 13th level, you have learned enough about the workings of magic that you can improvise the use of items even when they are not intended for you. You ignore all class, race, and level requirements on the use of magic items.\n\nNivel 13 - Use Magic Device\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou've learned how to maximize use of magic items, granting you the following benefits.\n\nAttunement\n\nYou can attune to up to four magic items at once.\n\nCharges\n\nWhenever you use a magic item property that expends charges, roll 1d6. On a roll of 6, you use the property without expending the charges.\n\nScrolls\n\nYou can use any XDMG, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability for the spell. If the spell is a cantrip or a level 1 spell, you can cast it reliably. If the scroll contains a higher-level spell, you must first succeed on an Intelligence (XPHB) check (10 plus the spell's level). On a successful check, you cast the spell from the scroll. On a failed check, the scroll disintegrates.\n\nNivel 13 - Use Magic Device\n\nNivel 17 - Thief's Reflexes\n\nPagina: 97\n\nWhen you reach 17th level, you have become adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal initiative and your second turn at your initiative minus 10. You can't use this feature when you are surprised.\n\nNivel 17 - Thief's Reflexes\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou are adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal XPHB and your second turn at your XPHB minus 10.\n\nThief [PHB]\n\nNivel 3 - Fast Hands\n\nPagina: 97\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you can use the bonus action granted by your Cunning Action to make a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check, use your phb to disarm a trap or open a lock, or take the Use an Object action.\n\nNivel 3 - Fast Hands\n\nPagina: 137\n\nAs a XPHB, you can do one of the following.\n\nSleight of Hand\n\nMake a Dexterity (XPHB) check to pick a lock or disarm a trap with XPHB or to pick a pocket.\n\nUse an Object\n\nTake the XPHB action, or take the XPHB action to use a magic item that requires that action.\n\nNivel 3 - Fast Hands\n\nNivel 3 - Second-Story Work\n\nPagina: 97\n\nWhen you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain the ability to climb faster than normal; climbing no longer costs you extra movement.\n\nIn addition, when you make a running jump, the distance you cover increases by a number of feet equal to your Dexterity modifier.\n\nNivel 3 - Second-Story Work\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou've trained to get into especially hard-to-reach places, granting you these benefits.\n\nClimber\n\nYou gain a XPHB equal to your XPHB.\n\nJumper\n\nYou can determine your jump distance using your Dexterity rather than your Strength.\n\nNivel 3 - Thief\n\nPagina: 97\n\nYou hone your skills in the larcenous arts. Burglars, bandits, cutpurses, and other criminals typically follow this archetype, but so do rogues who prefer to think of themselves as professional treasure seekers, explorers, delvers, and investigators. In addition to improving your agility and stealth, you learn skills useful for delving into ancient ruins, reading unfamiliar languages, and using magic items you normally couldn't employ.\n\nNivel 3 - Thief\n\nPagina: 137\n\nHunt for Treasure as a Classic Adventurer\n\nA mix of burglar, treasure hunter, and explorer, you are the epitome of an adventurer. In addition to improving your agility and stealth, you gain abilities useful for delving into ruins and getting maximum benefit from the magic items you find there.\n\nNivel 9 - Supreme Sneak\n\nPagina: 97\n\nStarting at 9th level, you have advantage on a Dexterity (Stealth) check if you move no more than half your speed on the same turn.\n\nNivel 9 - Supreme Sneak\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou gain the following Cunning Strike option.\n\nStealth Attack (Cost: 1d6)\n\nIf you have the XPHB action's XPHB condition, this attack doesn't end that condition on you if you end the turn behind XPHB or XPHB.\n\nNivel 13 - Use Magic Device\n\nPagina: 97\n\nBy 13th level, you have learned enough about the workings of magic that you can improvise the use of items even when they are not intended for you. You ignore all class, race, and level requirements on the use of magic items.\n\nNivel 13 - Use Magic Device\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou've learned how to maximize use of magic items, granting you the following benefits.\n\nAttunement\n\nYou can attune to up to four magic items at once.\n\nCharges\n\nWhenever you use a magic item property that expends charges, roll 1d6. On a roll of 6, you use the property without expending the charges.\n\nScrolls\n\nYou can use any XDMG, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability for the spell. If the spell is a cantrip or a level 1 spell, you can cast it reliably. If the scroll contains a higher-level spell, you must first succeed on an Intelligence (XPHB) check (10 plus the spell's level). On a successful check, you cast the spell from the scroll. On a failed check, the scroll disintegrates.\n\nNivel 13 - Use Magic Device\n\nNivel 17 - Thief's Reflexes\n\nPagina: 97\n\nWhen you reach 17th level, you have become adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal initiative and your second turn at your initiative minus 10. You can't use this feature when you are surprised.\n\nNivel 17 - Thief's Reflexes\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou are adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal XPHB and your second turn at your XPHB minus 10.\n\nThief [XPHB]\n\nPagina: 137\n\nNivel 3 - Fast Hands\n\nPagina: 97\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you can use the bonus action granted by your Cunning Action to make a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check, use your phb to disarm a trap or open a lock, or take the Use an Object action.\n\nNivel 3 - Fast Hands\n\nPagina: 137\n\nAs a XPHB, you can do one of the following.\n\nSleight of Hand\n\nMake a Dexterity (XPHB) check to pick a lock or disarm a trap with XPHB or to pick a pocket.\n\nUse an Object\n\nTake the XPHB action, or take the XPHB action to use a magic item that requires that action.\n\nNivel 3 - Fast Hands\n\nNivel 3 - Second-Story Work\n\nPagina: 97\n\nWhen you choose this archetype at 3rd level, you gain the ability to climb faster than normal; climbing no longer costs you extra movement.\n\nIn addition, when you make a running jump, the distance you cover increases by a number of feet equal to your Dexterity modifier.\n\nNivel 3 - Second-Story Work\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou've trained to get into especially hard-to-reach places, granting you these benefits.\n\nClimber\n\nYou gain a XPHB equal to your XPHB.\n\nJumper\n\nYou can determine your jump distance using your Dexterity rather than your Strength.\n\nNivel 3 - Thief\n\nPagina: 97\n\nYou hone your skills in the larcenous arts. Burglars, bandits, cutpurses, and other criminals typically follow this archetype, but so do rogues who prefer to think of themselves as professional treasure seekers, explorers, delvers, and investigators. In addition to improving your agility and stealth, you learn skills useful for delving into ancient ruins, reading unfamiliar languages, and using magic items you normally couldn't employ.\n\nNivel 3 - Thief\n\nPagina: 137\n\nHunt for Treasure as a Classic Adventurer\n\nA mix of burglar, treasure hunter, and explorer, you are the epitome of an adventurer. In addition to improving your agility and stealth, you gain abilities useful for delving into ruins and getting maximum benefit from the magic items you find there.\n\nNivel 9 - Supreme Sneak\n\nPagina: 97\n\nStarting at 9th level, you have advantage on a Dexterity (Stealth) check if you move no more than half your speed on the same turn.\n\nNivel 9 - Supreme Sneak\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou gain the following Cunning Strike option.\n\nStealth Attack (Cost: 1d6)\n\nIf you have the XPHB action's XPHB condition, this attack doesn't end that condition on you if you end the turn behind XPHB or XPHB.\n\nNivel 13 - Use Magic Device\n\nPagina: 97\n\nBy 13th level, you have learned enough about the workings of magic that you can improvise the use of items even when they are not intended for you. You ignore all class, race, and level requirements on the use of magic items.\n\nNivel 13 - Use Magic Device\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou've learned how to maximize use of magic items, granting you the following benefits.\n\nAttunement\n\nYou can attune to up to four magic items at once.\n\nCharges\n\nWhenever you use a magic item property that expends charges, roll 1d6. On a roll of 6, you use the property without expending the charges.\n\nScrolls\n\nYou can use any XDMG, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability for the spell. If the spell is a cantrip or a level 1 spell, you can cast it reliably. If the scroll contains a higher-level spell, you must first succeed on an Intelligence (XPHB) check (10 plus the spell's level). On a successful check, you cast the spell from the scroll. On a failed check, the scroll disintegrates.\n\nNivel 13 - Use Magic Device\n\nNivel 17 - Thief's Reflexes\n\nPagina: 97\n\nWhen you reach 17th level, you have become adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal initiative and your second turn at your initiative minus 10. You can't use this feature when you are surprised.\n\nNivel 17 - Thief's Reflexes\n\nPagina: 137\n\nYou are adept at laying ambushes and quickly escaping danger. You can take two turns during the first round of any combat. You take your first turn at your normal XPHB and your second turn at your XPHB minus 10."},
  ["magicitem.rogue-card.bmt2014"]={title="Rogue Card",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 14\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nWhen you hit a target with a weapon attack while holding this card, you can deal an extra 6d6 force damage to that target. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["feature.rogue-subclass.xphb2024.rogue.base.3"]={title="Rogue Subclass",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 129\n\nYou gain a Rogue subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Rogue levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Rogue level or lower."},
  ["magicitem.rogue-s-mantle.bmt2014"]={title="Rogue's Mantle",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis dark, hooded mantle of thick cloth is infused with secretive and deceptive magic. While wearing it, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• Darkvision You gain darkvision within a range of 60 feet. If you already have darkvision, the mantle increases your darkvision's range by 60 feet instead.\n\n• Move in Shadows While you are in Vision and Light or darkness, you can use a bonus action to teleport, along with anything you are wearing or carrying, up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see that is also in Vision and Light or darkness. You then have advantage on the first melee attack you make before the end of the turn.\n\n• Willful Enmity You can cast the BMT spell (save 15) from the mantle. Once the mantle has cast the spell, it can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["feature.roguish-archetype.phb2014.rogue.base.3"]={title="Roguish Archetype",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nAt 3rd level, you choose an archetype that you emulate in the exercise of your rogue abilities from the list of available archetypes. Your archetype choice grants you features at 3rd level and then again at 9th, 13th, and 17th level."},
  ["feature.roguish-archetype-feature.phb2014.rogue.base.9"]={title="Roguish Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nAt 9th level, you gain a feature granted by your Roguish Archetype."},
  ["feature.roguish-archetype-feature.phb2014.rogue.base.13"]={title="Roguish Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nAt 13th level, you gain a feature granted by your Roguish Archetype."},
  ["feature.roguish-archetype-feature.phb2014.rogue.base.17"]={title="Roguish Archetype feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nAt 17th level, you gain a feature granted by your Roguish Archetype."},
  ["deity.roknar.mtf2014"]={title="Roknar",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 73"},
  ["traphazard.rolling-sphere.dmg2014"]={title="Rolling Sphere",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 123\n\nWhen 20 or more pounds of pressure are placed on this trap's pressure plate, a hidden trapdoor in the ceiling opens, releasing a 10-foot-diameter rolling sphere of solid stone.\n\nWith a successful 15 Wisdom (Perception) check, a character can spot the trapdoor and pressure plate.\n\nA search of the floor accompanied by a successful 15 Intelligence (Investigation) check reveals variations in the mortar and stone that betray the pressure plate's presence. The same check made while inspecting the ceiling notes variations in the stonework that reveal the trapdoor. Wedging an iron spike or other object under the pressure plate prevents the trap from activating.\n\nActivation of the sphere requires all creatures present to roll initiative. The sphere rolls initiative with a +8 bonus. On its turn, it moves 60 feet in a straight line.\n\nThe sphere can move through creatures' spaces, and creatures can move through its space, treating it as difficult terrain. Whenever the sphere enters a creature's space or a creature enters its space while it's rolling, that creature must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 55 (10d10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone.\n\nThe sphere stops when it hits a wall or similar barrier. It can't go around corners, but smart dungeon builders incorporate gentle, curving turns into nearby passages that allow the sphere to keep moving.\n\nAs an action, a creature within 5 feet of the sphere can attempt to slow it down with a 20 Strength check. On a successful check, the sphere's speed is reduced by 15 feet. If the sphere's speed drops to 0, it stops moving and is no longer a threat."},
  ["traphazard.rolling-stone.xdmg2024"]={title="Rolling Stone",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 102\n\nWhen a creature moves onto a hidden pressure plate, a 5-foot-radius orb of solid stone is released from a secret compartment and begins to roll. The stone and all creatures nearby roll Initiative; the stone gets a +8 bonus on its Initiative roll.\n\nOn its turn, the stone moves 60 feet in one direction, changing course if redirected by an obstacle. The stone can move through creatures' spaces, and creatures can move through the stone's space, treating it as XPHB. Whenever the stone enters a creature's space for the first time on a turn or a creature enters the stone's space while the stone is rolling, that creature must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 55 (10d10) Bludgeoning damage and have the XPHB condition.\n\nThe stone stops when it hits a wall or similar barrier. It can't go around corners, but creative dungeon builders incorporate curving turns into nearby passages that allow the stone to keep moving.\n\nDetect and Disarm\n\nAs a XPHB action, a creature can examine the section of floor that forms the pressure plate and make a 15 Intelligence (XPHB) check, deducing the pressure plate's function on a successful check. Wedging an Iron Spike or a similar object under the pressure plate prevents the trap from triggering.\n\nDestroy the Stone\n\nThe stone is a Large object that has AC 17, HP 100, a XPHB of 10, and XPHB to Poison and Psychic damage.\n\nSlow the Stone\n\nAs an action, a creature can try to slow down the stone with a 20 Strength (XPHB) check. If the check is successful, the distance the stone moves on its turn is reduced by 15 feet. If that distance drops to 0, it stops moving and is no longer a threat."},
  ["creature.ront.oota2014"]={title="Ront",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.rool.skt2014"]={title="Rool",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.rooster.jttrc2014"]={title="Rooster",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10"},
  ["item.rope.xphb2024"]={title="Rope",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAs a XPHB action, you can tie a knot with Rope if you succeed on a 10 Dexterity (XPHB) check. The Rope can be burst with a successful 20 Strength (XPHB) check.\n\nYou can bind an unwilling creature with the Rope only if the creature has the XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB condition. If the creature's legs are bound, the creature has the XPHB condition until it escapes. Escaping the Rope requires the creature to make a successful 15 Dexterity (XPHB) check as an action."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-climbing.dmg2014"]={title="Rope of Climbing",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis 60-foot length of silk rope weighs 3 pounds and can hold up to 3,000 pounds. If you hold one end of the rope and use an action to speak the command word, the rope animates. As a bonus action, you can command the other end to move toward a destination you choose. That end moves 10 feet on your turn when you first command it and 10 feet on each of your turns until reaching its destination, up to its maximum length away, or until you tell it to stop. You can also tell the rope to fasten itself securely to an object or to unfasten itself, to knot or unknot itself, or to coil itself for carrying.\n\nIf you tell the rope to knot, large knots appear at 1-foot intervals along the rope. While knotted, the rope shortens to a 50-foot length and grants advantage on checks made to climb it.\n\nThe rope has AC 20 and 20 hit points. It regains 1 hit point every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 hit point. If the rope drops to 0 hit points, it is destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-climbing.xdmg2024"]={title="Rope of Climbing",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 301\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis 60-foot length of rope can hold up to 3,000 pounds. While holding one end of the rope, you can take a XPHB action to command the other end of the rope to animate and move toward a destination you choose, up to the rope's length away from you. That end moves 10 feet on your turn when you first command it and 10 feet at the start of each of your subsequent turns until reaching its destination or until you tell it to stop. You can also tell the rope to fasten itself securely to an object or to unfasten itself, to knot or unknot itself, or to coil itself for carrying.\n\nIf you tell the rope to knot, large knots appear at 1-foot intervals along the rope. While knotted, the rope shortens to a 50-foot length and grants XPHB on ability checks made to climb using the rope.\n\nThe rope has AC 20, HP 20, and XPHB to Poison and Psychic damage. It regains 1 XPHB every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 XPHB. If the rope drops to 0 XPHB, it is destroyed.\n\nreplicate magic item|artificer|efa|2|efa"},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-entanglement.dmg2014"]={title="Rope of Entanglement",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis rope is 30 feet long and weighs 3 pounds. If you hold one end of the rope and use an action to speak its command word, the other end darts forward to entangle a creature you can see within 20 feet of you. The target must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or become restrained.\n\nYou can release the creature by using a bonus action to speak a second command word. A target restrained by the rope can use an action to make a 15 Strength or Dexterity check (target's choice). On a success, the creature is no longer restrained by the rope.\n\nThe rope has AC 20 and 20 hit points. It regains 1 hit point every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 hit point. If the rope drops to 0 hit points, it is destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-entanglement.xdmg2024"]={title="Rope of Entanglement",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 301\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis rope is 30 feet long. While holding one end of the rope, you can take a XPHB action to command the other end to dart forward and entangle one creature you can see within 20 feet of yourself. The target must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or have the XPHB condition. You can release the target by letting go of your end of the rope (causing the rope to coil up in the target's space) or by using a XPHB to repeat the command (causing the rope to coil up in your hand).\n\nA target XPHB by the rope can take an action to make its choice of a 15 Strength (XPHB) or Dexterity (XPHB) check. On a successful check, the target is no longer XPHB by the rope. If you're still holding onto the rope when a target escapes from it, you can take a XPHB to command the rope to coil up in your hand; otherwise, the rope coils up in the target's space.\n\nThe rope has AC 20, HP 20, and XPHB to Poison and Psychic damage. It regains 1 XPHB every 5 minutes as long as it has at least 1 XPHB. If the rope drops to 0 XPHB, it is destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-mending.xdmg2024"]={title="Rope of Mending",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 302\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nThis 50-foot coil of rope can repair itself when cut into any number of smaller pieces. As a XPHB action, you can cause all pieces of the rope that are in contact with each other and not otherwise in use to knit back together. A Rope of Mending is forever shortened if a section of it is lost or destroyed."},
  ["magicitem.rope-of-mending.xge2024"]={title="Rope of Mending",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 138\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nYou can cut this 50-foot coil of hempen rope into any number of smaller pieces, and then use an action to speak a command word and cause the pieces to knit back together. The pieces must be in contact with each other and not otherwise in use. A rope of mending is forever shortened if a section of it is lost or destroyed."},
  ["spell.rope-trick.phb2014"]={title="Rope Trick",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\nYou touch a length of rope that is up to 60 feet long. One end of the rope then rises into the air until the whole rope hangs perpendicular to the ground. At the upper end of the rope, an invisible entrance opens to an extradimensional space that lasts until the spell ends.\n\nThe extradimensional space can be reached by climbing to the top of the rope. The space can hold as many as eight Medium or smaller creatures. The rope can be pulled into the space, making the rope disappear from view outside the space.\n\nAttacks and spells can't cross through the entrance into or out of the extradimensional space, but those inside can see out of it as if through a 3-foot-by-5-foot window centered on the rope.\n\nAnything inside the extradimensional space drops out when the spell ends."},
  ["spell.rope-trick.xphb2024"]={title="Rope Trick",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 312\n\nYou touch a rope. One end of it hovers upward until the rope hangs perpendicular to the ground or the rope reaches a ceiling. At the rope's upper end, an XPHB 3-foot-by-5-foot portal opens to an extradimensional space that lasts until the spell ends. That space can be reached by climbing the rope, which can be pulled into or dropped out of it.\n\nThe space can hold up to eight Medium or smaller creatures. Attacks, spells, and other effects can't pass into or out of the space, but creatures inside it can see through the portal. Anything inside the space drops out when the spell ends."},
  ["creature.roper.mm2014"]={title="Roper",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 261\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 10\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 8 | CON 17 | INT 7 | WIS 16 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the roper remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal cave formation, such as a stalagmite.\n\nGrasping Tendrils\n\nThe roper can have up to six tendrils at a time. Each tendril can be attacked (AC 20; 10 hit points; immunity to poison and psychic damage). Destroying a tendril deals no damage to the roper, which can extrude a replacement tendril on its next turn. A tendril can also be broken if a creature takes an action and succeeds on a 15 Strength check against it.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe roper can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe roper makes four attacks with its tendrils, uses Reel, and makes one attack with its bite.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h22 (4d8 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nTendril\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 50 ft., one creature. hThe target is grappled (escape 15). Until the grapple ends, the target is restrained and has disadvantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws, and the roper can't use the same tendril on another target.\n\nReel\n\nThe roper pulls each creature grappled by it up to 25 feet straight toward it."},
  ["creature.roper.xmm2024"]={title="Roper",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 262\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, climb: 20\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 8 | CON 17 | INT 7 | WIS 16 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe roper can climb difficult surfaces, including along ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe roper makes two Tentacle attacks, uses Reel, and makes two Bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h17 (3d8 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\nTentacle\n\nm 7, reach 60 ft. hThe target has the XPHB condition (escape 14) from one of six tentacles, and the target has the XPHB condition until the grapple ends.\n\nThe tentacle can be damaged, freeing a creature it has XPHB when destroyed (AC 20, HP 10, XPHB to Poison and Psychic damage). Damaging the tentacle deals no damage to the roper, and a destroyed tentacle regrows at the start of the roper's next turn.\n\nReel\n\nThe roper pulls each creature XPHB by it up to 30 feet straight toward it."},
  ["creature.rosavalda-rose-durst.cos2014"]={title="Rosavalda \"Rose\" Durst",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: S\n\nCR: 3\n\nPV: 35 (10d6)\n\nIdiomas: Common"},
  ["creature.rosie-beestinger.ai2014"]={title="Rosie Beestinger",subtitle="Criatura - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 203\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 45 (10d6 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Halfling\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBrave\n\nRosie has advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\nHalfling Nimbleness\n\nRosie can move through the space of any creature that is of a size larger than hers.\n\nEvasion\n\nIf Rosie is subjected to an effect that allows her to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, she instead takes no damage if she succeeds on the saving throw, and only half damage if she fails. She can't use this trait if she's incapacitated.\n\nShadow Step\n\nWhen Rosie is in dim light or darkness, she can use a bonus action to teleport 60 feet to an unoccupied space she can see that is also in dim light or darkness. She then has advantage on the first melee attack she makes before the end of the turn.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nRosie makes three attacks, then makes two unarmed strike attacks.\n\nStaff of the Master (+1 Quarterstaff)\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage, or 8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage if used with two hands.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage. Rosie's unarmed strikes are magical.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeflect Missiles\n\nIn response to being hit by a ranged weapon attack, Rosie deflects the missile. The damage she takes from the attack is reduced by 1d10 + 9. If the damage is reduced to 0, she catches the missile if it's small enough to hold in one hand and she has a hand free."},
  ["feature.rot-and-violence.rhw2014.ranger.hollow-warden.11"]={title="Rot and Violence",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nYour dedication to wild eldritch beings alters you further. When transformed using Wrath of the Wild, you gain the following additional benefits.\n\nMenacing Aura\n\nWhen a creature fails its saving throw against your Unnerving Aura, it also can't regain XPHB or take XPHB until the start of your next turn.\n\nStrangling Roots\n\nWhen you hit a creature with an attack roll using a weapon, you can activate the Sap or Slow mastery property in addition to a different mastery property you're using with that weapon."},
  ["traphazard.rot-grub.vgm2014"]={title="Rot Grub",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRot grubs are finger-sized maggots that eat living and dead creatures, although they can survive on vegetation. They infest corpses and piles of decaying matter and attack anyone that disturbs them. After burrowing into a creature, rot grubs instinctively chew their way toward vital parts.\n\nRot grubs recoil from flames, and fire is the main weapon against rot grubs once they're inside a body. Magic that neutralizes poison can also stop them before they kill their host.\n\nSingle Rot Grub\n\nRot grubs pose a threat both singly and as a swarm. See the MPMM for the mechanics of a swarm of rot grubs. A single rot grub has no stat block.\n\nAny creature that comes into contact with a single rot grub must succeed on a 10 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned, as the rot grub burrows into the creature. The poisoned creature takes 3 (1d6) poison damage at the end of each of its turns. Whenever the poisoned creature takes fire damage, the creature can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. If the poisoned creature ends its turn with 0 hit points, it dies, as the rot grub kills it."},
  ["creature.rot-troll.mpmm2014"]={title="Rot Troll",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 247\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d10 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 22 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRancid Degeneration\n\nAt the end of each of the troll's turns, each creature within 5 feet of it takes 11 (2d10) necrotic damage, unless the troll has taken acid or fire damage since the end of its last turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe troll makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) necrotic damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.rot-troll.mtf2014"]={title="Rot Troll",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 244\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d10 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 13 | CON 22 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\nImunidades: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRancid Degeneration\n\nAt the end of each of the troll's turns, each creature within 5 feet of it takes 11 (2d10) necrotic damage, unless the troll has taken acid or fire damage since the end of its last turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe troll makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) necrotic damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 5 (1d10) necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.rothe.coa2014"]={title="Rothé",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 15 (2d10 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage. If the rothé moved at least 20 feet straight towards this target immediately before the hit, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.rothe.vgm2014"]={title="Rothé",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 15 (2d10 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 4\n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCharge\n\nIf the rothé moves at least 20 feet straight toward a target and then hits it with a gore attack on the same turn, the target takes an extra 7 (2d6) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage."},
  ["magicitem.rotor-of-return.ai2014"]={title="Rotor of Return",subtitle="Item Magico - AI - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile attuned to this device, you have a +1 bonus to Constitution saving throws. You periodically receive flashbacks of old memories, and you can unerringly recall any event that took place within the previous 30 days.\n\nBorrow Object\n\nYou name a mundane item with a value of 50 gp or less and it appears in your hand or at your feet. This can be any item that appears in chapter 5, \"PHB,\" of the Player's Handbook, or any similar item selected with the DM's permission. The summoned item is transported to you from somewhere else in the world, but it is generic in nature, so that you might call for a longsword but you cannot borrow a specific creature's longsword. The item vanishes 10 minutes after it appears. Once you use this feature of the rotor of return, it cannot be used again until the next dawn.\n\nRecall Code\n\nAs an action, you can set your current location as a point of return locked to the rotor. Anytime thereafter, you can use a bonus action to teleport to the rotor's point of return as long as you are within 500 feet of that point. Once you use the rotor of return to teleport, this feature cannot be used again until the next dawn.\n\nPart of a Whole\n\nWhile this component is not installed in the AI, its magic might function sporadically or with unpredictable side effects, as determined by the DM."},
  ["creature.rotter.rtg2014"]={title="Rotter",subtitle="Criatura - RtG - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 75 (10d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Club\n\nIn the rotter's hand, its club is magical and deals 7 (3d4) extra damage (included in its attacks).\n\nPlant Camouflage\n\nThe rotter has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks it makes in terrain with ample obscuring plant life.\n\nRegeneration\n\nThe rotter regains 10 hit points at the start of its turn if it is in contact with the ground. If the rotter takes fire damage, this trait doesn't function at the start of the rotter's next turn. The rotter dies only if it starts its turn with 0 hit points and doesn't regenerate.\n\nShared Senses\n\nThe rotter can see and hear what any plant within 120 ft can see and hear. In addition, the rotter can communicate telepathically with any plant within this range.\n\nTree Stride\n\nOnce on each of its turns, the rotter can use 10 feet of its movement to step magically into one copse of mushrooms within 5 feet of it and emerge from a second copse of mushrooms within 60 feet of it, appearing in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the second copse. Both copses of mushrooms must be Large or bigger. The rotter doesn't need to be able to see the second copse to use this ability.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe rotter makes two attacks with its club.\n\nClub\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (4d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["language.roushoum.scag2014"]={title="Roushoum",subtitle="Idioma - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 112\n\nOption: Human Languages\n\nMany human ethnicities and nations in Faerûn have their own language, in addition to Common. Most human languages are written in Thorass, the alphabet of Old Common, derived from the Chondathan language that traders used as their common tongue. A few human languages use other alphabets, including Draconic, Dethek, and Espruar.\n\nIf your Dungeon Master allows this option, then any human from an ethnic group that has its own language is assumed to know that language as well as Common. This ethnic language is treated as a free additional language for such individuals."},
  ["feature.roving.xphb2024.ranger.base.6"]={title="Roving",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["item.rowboat.dmg2014"]={title="Rowboat",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: none\n\nKeelboats and rowboats are used on lakes and rivers, If going downstream, add the speed of the current (typically 3 miles per hour) to the speed of the vehicle. These vehicles can't be rowed against any significant current, but they can be pulled upstream by draft animals on the shores. A rowboat weighs 100 pounds, in case adventurers carry it over land."},
  ["vehicle.rowboat.gos2014"]={title="Rowboat",subtitle="Veiculo - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 190\n\nOn its turn, the rowboat can take the move action below. It can't take this action if it has no crew.\n\n• Move"},
  ["item.rowboat.xphb2024"]={title="Rowboat",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 230\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.rowboat-mimic.wdmm2014"]={title="Rowboat Mimic",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: L\n\nPV: 67 (9d10 + 18)"},
  ["feature.royal-envoy.scag2014.fighter.purple-dragon-knight-banneret.7"]={title="Royal Envoy",subtitle="Caracteristica - SCAG - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.rubblebelt-stalker.ggr2014"]={title="Rubblebelt Stalker",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 239\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmbusher\n\nIn the first round of a combat, the stalker has advantage on attack rolls against any creature that hasn't taken a turn yet.\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe stalker can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of its turns.\n\nRuin Dweller\n\nThe stalker has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide in ruins, and its speed is not reduced in difficult terrain composed of rubble.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe stalker deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe stalker makes three attacks with its shortsword.\n\nShortsword\n\nm 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["item.ruby.dmg2014"]={title="Ruby",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA transparent clear red to deep crimson gemstone."},
  ["item.ruby.xdmg2024"]={title="Ruby",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA clear red to deep crimson gemstone."},
  ["magicitem.ruby-of-the-war-mage.xdmg2024"]={title="Ruby of the War Mage",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 302\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nEtched with eldritch runes, this 1-inch-diameter ruby allows you to use a Simple or Martial weapon as a XPHB for your spells. For this property to work, you must attach the ruby to the weapon by pressing the ruby against it for at least 10 minutes. Thereafter, the ruby can't be removed unless you detach it as a XPHB action, the weapon is destroyed, or your XPHB to the ruby ends."},
  ["magicitem.ruby-of-the-war-mage.xge2024"]={title="Ruby of the War Mage",subtitle="Item Magico - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 138\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nEtched with eldritch runes, this 1-inch-diameter ruby allows you to use a items as a spellcasting focus for your spells. For this property to work, you must attach the ruby to the weapon by pressing the ruby against it for at least 10 minutes. Thereafter, the ruby can't be removed unless you detach it as an action or the weapon is destroyed. Not even an antimagic field causes it to fall off. The ruby does fall off the weapon if your attunement to the ruby ends."},
  ["magicitem.ruby-rod-of-asmodeus.coa2014"]={title="Ruby Rod of Asmodeus",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 274\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nAsmodeus's Ruby Rod is said to have been constructed from a shard of pure evil, a ruby soaked in the blood of the innocents, the drool from a draconic deity, and the tears of 777 angels. It is a magic rod that functions as a morningstar and you have a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it. All damage dealt with it is converted to necrotic, and when you hit a good aligned creature, that creature takes an extra 2d12 necrotic damage.\n\nThe Ruby Rod of Asmodeus has 66 charges and regains 6d6 charges each nightfall. Asmodeus is always capable of perceiving through the rod and knows the exact location of any creature attuned to it. If a creature uses the special abilities of the rod without Asmodeus's permission, they take 2d12 necrotic damage each use, doubled if they're good aligned. This damage ignores resistances and immunities, and if it kills the user, Asmodeus permanently claims their soul.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Ruby Rod of Asmodeus has the following random properties:\n\n• 1 dmg property\n\n• 1 dmg property\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\nAsmodeus is immune to the detrimental properties of the weapon.\n\nBow to the King\n\nYou may use an action to expend 33 charges to use the rod to force all creatures within a 150-foot-radius to bow to you. A creature must succeed on a 21 Charisma saving throw or be forced to kneel for up to 1 hour. Creatures immune to the charmed condition have advantage on their save. Each time a kneeling creature takes damage, they may repeat the save, ending the effect on a success. The effect also ends early for kneeling creatures if they're touched by the Ruby Rod.\n\nAcid, Cold, and Lightning\n\nAt a cost of 9 charges each use, you may use an action to trigger one of the following effects:\n\n• You project acid in a 60-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 12d8 acid damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n• You project an icy blast in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 19 Constitution saving throw, taking 12d8 cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n• You shoot lightning in a 90-foot line that is 5 feet wide. Each creature in that line must make a 19 Dexterity saving throw, taking 12d10 lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nReactions\n\nAs a reaction to suffering a detrimental effect, you may cast Lesser Restoration (expending 3 charges) or Greater Restoration (expending 12 charges.)\n\nAdditionally, if you're the sole target of a spell, you may use a reaction to attempt to use the rod to absorb the spell and cancel its effect. You roll 1d20 + 2, and if the result is higher than the spell level + 10, the spell is absorbed into the rod. The rod regains charges equal to the spell level it absorbed. If the absorbed charges go over the maximum of 66 charges, it overloads, dealing 1d6 necrotic damage per charge to you and expending all charges.\n\nDestroying the Rod\n\nWhile Asmodeus lives, the Ruby Rod of Asmodeus can't be destroyed, and if attempted it simply returns to Asmodeus. If he were defeated, the rod could be destroyed by bringing it to the Abyss from whence it was created, then performing a ritual known only to Asmodeus."},
  ["magicitem.ruby-weave-gem.ftd2014"]={title="Ruby Weave Gem",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nWhile you are holding this gem, you can use it as a spellcasting focus for your spells.\n\nThe gem has 3 charges and regains all expended charges daily at dawn. When you cast a spell while holding this gem, you can expend up to 3 charges to ignore the spell's material components with a gold piece cost, up to 500 gp per charge expended.\n\nWhen you finish a long rest, choose a spell from any class list. The spell you choose must be of a level you can cast. You know the chosen spell and can cast it with your spell slots of the appropriate level until the end of your next long rest."},
  ["creature.rudolph-van-richten.rhw2014"]={title="Rudolph van Richten",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 105 (14d8 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 17 | WIS 18 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Elvish, Infernal\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShield of Erasmus\n\nWhile XPHB, Rudolph has XPHB to Force, Poison, and Psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nRudolph makes three attacks, using Silver Sword Cane or Hand Crossbow in any combination.\n\nSilver Sword Cane\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Slashing damage plus 5 (2d4) Radiant damage. Critical hThe target has the XPHB condition until it finishes a XPHB. It makes a 15 Constitution saving throw at end of each hour, ending the effect on a success.\n\nHand Crossbow\n\nr 5, range 30/120 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage plus 5 (2d4) Radiant damage.\n\nRepel Evil {@recharge 5}\n\ncha 15, each creature of Rudolph's choice in a 30-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 18 (4d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of Rudolph's next turn. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nOccult Aid (2/Day)\n\nRudolph casts XPHB, XPHB, or XPHB, using Wisdom as the spellcasting modifier (spell save 15)."},
  ["creature.rudolph-von-aubrecker.pl2014"]={title="Rudolph von Aubrecker",subtitle="Criatura - PL - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 19 | WIS 14 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nForcefield Generator\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nRudolph makes one Taser attack and uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB or XPHB.\n\nTaser\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h14 (4d6) Lightning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of Rudolph's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nX-Ray Scanning\n\nRudolph gains Blindsight to a range of 60 feet. This Blindsight ignores XPHB created by up to 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or 3 feet of wood or dirt. Thicker substances or thin sheets of lead block the Blindsight as usual. This benefit lasts for 1 minute or until Rudolph has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.rug-of-smothering.mm2014"]={title="Rug of Smothering",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 33 (6d10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 3 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAntimagic Susceptibility\n\nThe rug is incapacitated while in the area of an antimagic field. If targeted by dispel magic, the rug must succeed on a Constitution saving throw against the caster's spell save DC or fall unconscious for 1 minute.\n\nDamage Transfer\n\nWhile it is grappling a creature, the rug takes only half the damage dealt to it, and the creature grappled by the rug takes the other half.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the rug remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal rug.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSmother\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller creature. hThe creature is grappled (escape 13). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, blinded, and at risk of suffocating, and the rug can't smother another target. In addition, at the start of each of the target's turns, the target takes 10 (2d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.ruidium-elephant.crcotn2014"]={title="Ruidium Elephant",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 95\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 138 (12d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 9 | CON 21 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nTrampling Charge\n\nIf the elephant moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a Gore attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 16 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the elephant can make one Stomp attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nGore\n\nmw 10 to hit (with advantage if the target is a creature missing any hit points), reach 10 ft., one target. h25 (4d8 + 7) piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one prone creature. h29 (4d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage."},
  ["magicitem.ruidium-shield.crcotn2014"]={title="Ruidium Shield",subtitle="Item Magico - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nTendrils of ruidium extend across the metal surface of this shield. While this shield is on your person, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• You have resistance to psychic damage.\n\n• You can breathe water.\n\n• You gain a swimming speed equal to your walking speed.\n\nPsychic Reflection\n\nWhen you take psychic damage while holding the shield, you can use your reaction to choose another creature you can see within 30 feet of you. That creature takes the psychic damage you would have taken.\n\nRuidium Corruption\n\nWhen you use the shield's Psychic Reflection property, you must make a 20 Charisma saving throw. On a failed save, you gain 1 level of exhaustion. If you are not already suffering from ruidium corruption, you become corrupted when you fail this save.\n\nIf Ruidium Is Destroyed\n\nIf the Apotheon is killed or redeemed, all the ruidium in Exandria is destroyed instantly, and a ruidium shield becomes a +2 shield."},
  ["magicitem.ruin-card.bmt2014"]={title="Ruin Card",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nAs an action, you can brandish this card and use it to cast the Disintegrate spell (save 17). Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.ruin-grinder.scc2014"]={title="Ruin Grinder",subtitle="Criatura - SCC - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 82 (11d10 + 22)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 30\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 13 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFire Absorption\n\nWhenever the ruin grinder is subjected to fire damage, it regains a number of hit points equal to half the fire damage dealt.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe ruin grinder deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe ruin grinder can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and leaves a 10-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe ruin grinder makes two Excavator attacks.\n\nExcavator\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) force damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 17 Strength saving throw or be pushed up to 10 feet away and knocked prone."},
  ["creature.ruin-spider.bmt2014"]={title="Ruin Spider",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 182\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 105 (14d10 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 4\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: acid\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRuinous Acid\n\nAny nonmagical weapon that hits the spider corrodes. After dealing damage, the weapon takes a permanent and cumulative -1 penalty to damage rolls. If its penalty drops to -5, the weapon is destroyed. Nonmagical ammunition made of metal that hits the spider is destroyed after dealing damage.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe spider can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWeb Sense\n\nWhile in contact with a web, the spider knows the exact location of any other creature in contact with the same web.\n\nWeb Walker\n\nThe spider ignores movement restrictions caused by webbing.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe spider makes two Ruinous Bite attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Web.\n\nRuinous Bite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage and 9 (2d8) acid damage. In addition, if the target is a creature wearing nonmagical armor, the armor takes a permanent and cumulative -1 penalty to the AC it offers. Armor reduced to an Armor Class of 10 is destroyed.\n\nWeb {@recharge 5}\n\nrw 7 to hit, range 30/60 ft., one creature. hThe target has the restrained condition. As an action, a restrained target can make a 13 Strength check, bursting the webbing on a successful check. The webbing can also be destroyed (AC 10; 5 hit points; vulnerability to fire damage; immunity to acid, bludgeoning, poison, and psychic damage)."},
  ["item.ruin-s-wake-awakened.egw2014"]={title="Ruin's Wake (Awakened)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.ruin-s-wake-dormant.egw2014"]={title="Ruin's Wake (Dormant)",subtitle="Item Magico - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 277\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nThis spear is made from the ivory bone of an ancient gold dragon and carved with an Orc hymn to Gruumsh.\n\nSentience\n\nRuin's Wake is a sentient chaotic evil weapon with an Intelligence of 20, a Wisdom of 16, and a Charisma of 22. It has hearing and darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.\n\nThe weapon communicates telepathically with its wielder and can speak, read, and understand Abyssal, Common, and Orc.\n\nPersonality\n\nA slaughter-loving balor named Yarrowish lives within Ruin's Wake. The weapon desires only to draw blood and pushes its wielder to solve problems with violence.\n\nDormant\n\nThe spear grants the following benefits in its dormant state:\n\n• You can speak, read, and write Abyssal and Orc.\n\n• You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon, and it deals an extra 1d8 piercing damage to any target it hits. Immediately after you make a ranged attack with this weapon, it flies back to your hand.\n\n• As a reaction when you are hit by a melee attack, you can make a melee attack with Ruin's Wake with advantage against the attacker. You can't use this property again until you finish a short or long rest.\n\nBetrayer Artifact Properties\n\nThe Arms of the Betrayers advance in power in the same manner as the Vestiges of Divergence. In its dormant state, each of these artifacts has one dmg property and one dmg property. When the artifact attains an awakened state, it gains an additional dmg property and an additional dmg property. When the item reaches its exalted state, it gains a dmg property. See \"Artifact Properties\" in chapter 7 of the Dungeon Master's Guide for more information."},
  ["item.ruin-s-wake-exalted.egw2014"]={title="Ruin's Wake (Exalted)",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.ruinblade.imr2014"]={title="Ruinblade",subtitle="Item Magico - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 95\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nRuinblade is a unique weapon possessed by IMR, the architect of the Tomb of Horrors. A symbol of his authority, Moghadam carries the weapon during the time frame of the adventure to intimidate the tomb's workers. (In later years, after ToA trapped Moghadam in the completed tomb as an undead archwraith, Moghadam was able to use the weapon as his own phylactery.)\n\nA small jade version of the green devil face of the Tomb of Horrors is fashioned into the hilt of the weapon, with the blade extending from its open mouth. The blade always appears ruined and rusting, and causes its surroundings to appear reflected in the blade as if in a state of decay.\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. When you hit an undead creature with it, the attack deals an extra 1d8 force damage.\n\nIn addition, the weapon has the following properties:\n\nBlighted Ruin\n\nYou can cast the blight spell from the weapon (15). Once used, this property of the weapon can't be used until the next dawn.\n\nDestructive Ruin\n\nYou can cast the disintegrate spell from the weapon, but can target only a nonmagical object or a creation of magical force. Once used, this property of the weapon can't be used until dawn seven days later.\n\nCurse\n\nThis weapon is cursed, and becoming attuned to it extends the curse to you. Until the curse is broken with a remove curse spell or similar magic, you are unwilling to part with the weapon.\n\nThe weapon must take direct part in the destruction of 1,000 gp worth of materials and objects every seven days, or a conflict arises between you and the weapon at the end of the seventh day.\n\nSentience\n\nRuinblade is a sentient lawful evil weapon with an Intelligence of 15, a Wisdom of 8, and a Charisma of 16. It has hearing and darkvision out to a range of 120 feet.\n\nThe weapon can speak, read, and understand Common, and can communicate with its wielder telepathically. Its voice is a rough, ruined echo. While you are attuned to it, Ruinblade also understands every language you know.\n\nPersonality\n\nRuinblade speaks either with a dolorous or frenetic tone, depending on its mood. That mood improves when the sword is actively engaged in acts of destruction, but worsens if the blade is left inactive too long.\n\nThe weapon's purpose is to ruin and unmake existing objects, so that its owner can rebuild the world from a blank slate. It thus encourages its wielder to engage in constant destruction, claiming that this will allow the creation of a more superior vision from the ruin of what came before."},
  ["background.ruined.bmt2014"]={title="Ruined",subtitle="Background - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 58\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies: One items of your choice (such as playing cards or three-dragon ante cards)\n\nFeature: Still Standing\n\nYou have weathered ruinous misfortune, and you possess hidden reserves others don't expect. You gain the Alert, Skilled, or Tough feat (your choice). Your choice of feat reflects how you've dealt with the terrible loss that changed your life forever. If you've kept your senses sharp for every opportunity and climbed your way out of misery by seizing the tiniest scrap of hope, choose Alert. If you've redoubled your efforts to reclaim what was once yours, choose Skilled. If you've stoically persevered through your misfortune, select Tough.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nRising above misfortune shapes one's perspective. The Ruined Personality Traits table suggests traits you might adopt for your character (and ruinous cards that might have prompted this trait).\n\nd6 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I've changed from my past, and I work to live up to my new path. (Balance, Throne)\n\n2 | Every moment is a gift I refuse to squander. (Euryale, Skull)\n\n3 | Now that I've overcome having nothing, I can survive anything. (Fool, Ruin, Talons)\n\n4 | I know enemies are set against me, and I always prepare for the worst. (Flames, Rogue)\n\n5 | I interpret every event as part of a larger pattern I just haven't worked out yet. (Puzzle, Star)\n\n6 | I must make up for so much time I've already lost. (Donjon, Void)\n\nBuilding a Ruined Character\n\nRuined characters were on top of the world before misfortune struck. Many were wealthy. Others come from modest backgrounds, but they were surrounded by friends, family, and loved ones. They might have been famous, or simply never encountered serious hardship before. Some were born to privilege or rose to prominence through trickery or a false reputation. Now a Deck of Many Things—or another calamity—has knocked them down like a house of cards.\n\nIf your character's life was ruined by a Deck of Many Things, consider which card was responsible. Perhaps your character was imprisoned for years by the Donjon or Void card, and now everyone they knew has died. Maybe your character drew the Rogue card, and the person closest to them—a spouse, child, or parent—turned against them. A devil unleashed by the Flames card might have destroyed their life. The Ruin or Talons card might have stolen the character's material goods or saddled them with vast debt.\n\nRuined Trinkets\n\nWhen you make your character, you can roll once on the Ruined Trinkets table instead of on the Trinkets table in the PHB.\n\nd6 | Trinket\n\n1 | A rusted scrap of a once-beloved family heirloom\n\n2 | A land deed, but all the names and markings that once tied it to you have faded into obscurity\n\n3 | A bauble once imbued with powerful magic\n\n4 | A battered playing card with a hole pierced in it, its face depicting the card that affected you\n\n5 | A yellowed Humanoid tooth that whispers eerily when placed under a pillow\n\n6 | A keepsake from someone you were once close to but who is now your enemy"},
  ["magicitem.ruinous-flail.bmt2014"]={title="Ruinous Flail",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis ash-gray flail is cold to the touch. You gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon, and it deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\nAdditionally, when you hit a creature with this weapon, you can force the creature to make a 15 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature has the poisoned condition for 1 minute. The poisoned creature takes 2d4 necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Once this property is used in this way, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.ruinstone.dc2014"]={title="Ruinstone",subtitle="Item Magico - DC - 2014",body="Raridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nA fiery red crystal the size of a human palm.\n\nOnce per day as a bonus action, a villain can activate the ruinstone to undo one deed they have performed. The possibilities here are broad, but in combat it's simplest to allow them the opportunity to \"rewind\" one action and take it again, or to reroll a failed saving throw (if it can still take actions).\n\nEach use of the artifact has a terrible side effect: someone known to the wielder is also erased from reality. After the villain uses the ruinstone, roll a d20: on a 5-20, one of their allies disintegrates, on an 1-4, one of the player characters disintegrates.\n\nIf a creature bound its soul to the ruinstone in the \"Thalivar's Beacon\" quest, the artifact explodes when used and the creature who is bound to it disintegrates, disappearing from reality and can only be brought back with a wish spell, or similar magic."},
  ["creature.rumpadump.oota2014"]={title="Rumpadump",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.runara.dosi2014"]={title="Runara",subtitle="Criatura - DoSI - 2014",body="Pagina: 40\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 13"},
  ["charoption.runaway-author.idrotf2014"]={title="Runaway Author",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\nI penned a notorious exposé called \"The Hellbent Highborn,\" which accused several prominent patriars in Baldur's Gate and nobles in Waterdeep of being devil worshipers. Although my accusations were well founded, I made a lot of enemies and was forced to seek refuge in Icewind Dale."},
  ["background.rune-carver.bgg2014"]={title="Rune Carver",subtitle="Background - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nRune Styles\n\nEach rune carver has a unique style and preferred medium. To determine how you make your runes, you can roll on the Rune Style table.\n\nd6 | Style\n\n1 | You inscribe runes in wax or clay with a fine metal needle.\n\n2 | You whittle pieces of wood into small figurines you mark with runes.\n\n3 | You engrave runes onto glass beads and thread them onto necklaces and bracelets.\n\n4 | You stitch runes into the hems of clothing.\n\n5 | You carve runes on a set of animal bones you can throw in different formations.\n\n6 | You draw runes into candles, melting the wax to smooth over the engravings.\n\nBuilding a Rune Carver Character\n\nScholarly pursuits, ancient mysteries, or a fateful encounter might inspire a character to pursue the secrets of a rune carver.\n\nFeature: Rune Shaper\n\nYou gain the BGG feat.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nThe Rune Carver Personality Traits table suggests a variety of traits you might adopt for your character.\n\nd6 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | Is it practical to learn an ancient language that is rarely spoken? No. But is it fun? Very.\n\n2 | I learned one of my ancestors was a lauded rune carver whose story was lost to time. I seek to rekindle that legacy.\n\n3 | The old, traditional markings of runecraft look so boring. Why not give my runes some flair?\n\n4 | In my studies of runes, I strive to understand how great civilizations of the past fell, so I can prevent it from happening to societies of the present.\n\n5 | Life may be a whirlwind of chaos, but whenever I create my runes, I feel at peace.\n\n6 | My brain struggles to process words written in ink, but the feeling of carved runes makes my mind sing."},
  ["feature.rune-carver.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.3"]={title="Rune Carver",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="3rd-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou can use magic runes to enhance your gear. You learn two runes of your choice, from among the runes described below, and each time you gain a level in this class, you can replace one rune you know with a different one from this feature. When you reach certain levels in this class, you learn additional runes, as shown in the Runes Known table.\n\nWhenever you finish a long rest, you can touch a number of objects equal to the number of runes you know, and you inscribe a different rune onto each of the objects. To be eligible, an object must be a weapon, a suit of armor, a shield, a piece of jewelry, or something else you can wear or hold in a hand. Your rune remains on an object until you finish a long rest, and an object can bear only one of your runes at a time.\n\nFighter Level | Number of Runes\n\n3rd | 2\n\n7th | 3\n\n10th | 4\n\n15th | 5\n\nIf a rune has a level requirement, you must be at least that level in this class to learn the rune. If a rune requires a saving throw, your Rune Magic save DC equals 8 + your proficiency bonus + your Constitution modifier."},
  ["subclass.rune-knight.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.0"]={title="Rune Knight",subtitle="Subclasse - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.rune-knight.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.3"]={title="Rune Knight",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\nRune Knights enhance their martial prowess using the supernatural power of runes, an ancient practice that originated with giants. Rune cutters can be found among any family of giants, and you likely learned your methods first or second hand from such a mystical artisan. Whether you found the giant's work carved into a hill or cave, learned of the runes from a sage, or met the giant in person, you studied the giant's craft and learned how to apply magic runes to empower your equipment."},
  ["feat.rune-shaper.bgg2014"]={title="Rune Shaper",subtitle="Feat - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 18\n\nYou've studied the magic of Giant runes, granting you the following benefits:\n\n• Comprehend Languages You learn the comprehend languages spell. You can cast this spell without expending a spell slot, and you must finish a long rest before you can cast it in this way again. You can also cast this spell using any spell slots you have.\n\n• Rune Magic You know a number of runes equal to half your proficiency bonus (rounded down), chosen from the Rune Spells table. Whenever you finish a long rest, you can inscribe each rune you know onto one nonmagical weapon, armor, piece of clothing, or other object you touch. You temporarily learn the 1st-level spells that correspond to the runes you inscribed, as specified on the Rune Spells table, and you know those spells until you finish a long rest, when the runes fade. While you are wearing or carrying any rune-marked object, you can cast the spells associated with those runes using any spell slots you have. You can also invoke a rune inscribed on an object you are wearing or carrying and cast its associated spell without expending a spell slot or using material components. Once you cast the spell in this way, you can't do so again until you finish a long rest. Your spellcasting ability for this feat is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat). Each time you gain a level, you can replace one of the runes you know with another one from the Rune Spells table. Rune | Spell Cloud | Fog cloud Death | Inflict wounds Dragon | Chromatic orb Enemy | Disguise self Fire | Burning hands Friend | Speak with animals Frost | Armor of Agathys Hill | Goodberry Journey | Longstrider King | Command Mountain | Entangle Stone | Sanctuary Storm | Thunderwave"},
  ["creature.runed-behir.wdmm2014"]={title="Runed Behir",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 158\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nLesser Magic\n\nGreater Magic (Costs 2 Actions)"},
  ["creature.runic-colossus.bgg2014"]={title="Runic Colossus",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 163\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / G\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 315 (18d20 + 126)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 9 | CON 24 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Giant but can't speak\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe colossus is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe colossus has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe colossus deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe colossus makes two Slam attacks and then uses Stomp.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h26 (3d12 + 7) bludgeoning damage.\n\nStomp\n\nmw 14 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h29 (4d10 + 7) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 22 Dexterity saving throw or have the prone condition. Until the colossus uses its Stomp again or moves, the creature has the restrained condition. The restrained creature or another creature within 5 feet of it can use its action to make a 22 Strength check. On a successful check, the affected creature relocates to an unoccupied space of its choice within 5 feet of the colossus and is no longer restrained.\n\nArcane Beam {@recharge 5}\n\nThe colossus fires a beam of magical force from its chest, hands, or head in a 150-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw, taking 58 (9d12) force damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nSpell Reflection (2/Day)\n\nrs 14 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature casting a spell of 5th level or lower. h26 (4d12) force damage, and the target must succeed on a 15 Intelligence saving throw or the spell fails and has no effect."},
  ["feature.runic-juggernaut.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.18"]={title="Runic Juggernaut",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 44\n\n18th-level Rune Knight feature\n\nYou learn how to amplify your rune-powered transformation. As a result, the extra damage you deal with the Giant's Might feature increases to 1d10. Moreover, when you use that feature, your size can increase to Huge, and while you are that size, your reach increases by 5 feet."},
  ["feature.runic-shield.tce2014.fighter.rune-knight.7"]={title="Runic Shield",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["optionalfeature.rush-of-the-gale-spirits.phb2014"]={title="Rush of the Gale Spirits",subtitle="Opcao/Feature - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\nYou can spend 2 ki points to cast gust of wind."},
  ["traphazard.russet-mold.vgm2014"]={title="Russet Mold",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 196\n\nFew know for sure where russet mold came from. One historical account tells of adventurers in a mountain range discovering russet mold and bestiary in a peculiar metal dungeon full of strange life. Another story says that explorers found russet mold in a crater left by a falling star, with MPMM infesting the forest nearby.\n\nThe mold is found only in places that are dark, warm, and wet. Russet mold that spreads out across a metal object can be mistaken for rust, and a successful 15 Intelligence (Nature) or Wisdom (Survival) check is required to identify it.\n\nEffects of the Mold\n\nAny creature that comes within 5 feet of russet mold must make a 13 Constitution saving throw as the mold emits a puff of spores. On a failed save, the creature is poisoned. While poisoned in this way, the creature takes 7 (2d6) poison damage at the start of each of its turns. The creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Any magic that neutralizes poison or cures disease kills the infestation. A creature reduced to 0 hit points by the mold dies. If the dead creature is a Beast, a Giant, or a Humanoid, one or more vegepygmies emerge from its body 24 hours later: one from a Small corpse, two from a Medium corpse, four from a Large corpse, eight from a Huge corpse, or sixteen from a Gargantuan corpse.\n\nDestroying the Mold\n\nRusset mold can be hard to kill, since weapons and most types of damage do it no harm. Effects that deal acid, necrotic, or radiant damage kill 1 square foot of russet mold per 1 damage dealt. A pound of salt, a gallon of alcohol, or magic that cures disease kills russet mold in a square area that is 10 feet on a side. Sunlight kills any russet mold in the light's area."},
  ["creature.rust-monster.mm2014"]={title="Rust Monster",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 262\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 27 (5d8 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIron Scent\n\nThe rust monster can pinpoint, by scent, the location of ferrous metal within 30 feet of it.\n\nRust Metal\n\nAny nonmagical weapon made of metal that hits the rust monster corrodes. After dealing damage, the weapon takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to damage rolls. If its penalty drops to −5, the weapon is destroyed. Non magical ammunition made of metal that hits the rust monster is destroyed after dealing damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage.\n\nAntennae\n\nThe rust monster corrodes a nonmagical ferrous metal object it can see within 5 feet of it. If the object isn't being worn or carried, the touch destroys a 1-foot cube of it. If the object is being worn or carried by a creature, the creature can make a 11 Dexterity saving throw to avoid the rust monster's touch.\n\nIf the object touched is either metal armor or a metal shield being worn or carried, it takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to the AC it offers. Armor reduced to an AC of 10 or a shield that drops to a +0 bonus is destroyed. If the object touched is a held metal weapon, it rusts as described in the Rust Metal trait."},
  ["creature.rust-monster.xmm2024"]={title="Rust Monster",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 263\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 12 | CON 13 | INT 2 | WIS 13 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIron Scent\n\nThe rust monster can pinpoint the location of ferrous metal within 30 feet of itself.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe rust monster makes one Bite attack and uses Antennae twice.\n\nBite\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d8 + 1) Piercing damage.\n\nAntennae\n\nThe rust monster targets one nonmagical metal object—armor or a weapon—worn or carried by a creature within 5 feet of itself. dex 11, the creature with the object. actSaveFail The object takes a -1 penalty to the AC it offers (armor) or to its attack rolls (weapon). Armor is destroyed if the penalty reduces its AC to 10, and a weapon is destroyed if its penalty reaches -5. The penalty can be removed by casting the XPHB spell on the armor or weapon.\n\nDestroy Metal\n\nThe rust monster touches a nonmagical metal object within 5 feet of itself that isn't being worn or carried. The touch destroys a 1-foot XPHB of the object.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nReflexive Antennae\n\nactTrigger An attack roll hits the rust monster. actResponse The rust monster uses Antennae."},
  ["creature.rusted-behemoth.fraif2014"]={title="Rusted Behemoth",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 157 (15d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 10 | CON 19 | INT 6 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Giant\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Rusted makes three attacks, using Slam or Rusted Shot Put in any combination.\n\nSlam\n\nm 10, reach 10 ft. h20 (4d6 + 6) Bludgeoning damage.\n\nRusted Shot Put\n\nr 10, range 60/240 ft. h15 (2d8 + 6) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nRust-Riddled Hide\n\nactTrigger The Rusted is hit by an attack roll that deals Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage. dcon 16, each creature of the Rusted's choice in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the Rusted. actSaveFail the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the target's next turn."},
  ["creature.rusted-berserker.fraif2014"]={title="Rusted Berserker",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 82 (11d8 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 17 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 6\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Rusted makes two attacks, using Greatsword or Javelin in any combination.\n\nGreatsword\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn.\n\nJavelin\n\nm,r 6, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Piercing damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn."},
  ["item.rusted-hulk.fraif2014"]={title="Rusted Hulk",subtitle="Item - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 166\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.rusted-wyrm.fraif2014"]={title="Rusted Wyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / G\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 231 (14d20 + 84)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, swim: 60\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 13 | CON 22 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, frightened, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the Rusted fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Rusted makes two Bite attacks.\n\nBite\n\nm 12, reach 20 ft. h29 (4d10 + 7) Piercing damage.\n\nSteam Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 19, each creature and flammable object that isn't being worn or carried in a 60-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 45 (7d12) Fire damage, and the target starts XPHB. actSaveSuccess Half damage only. actSaveSuccessOrFail Being underwater doesn't grant XPHB to this Fire damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEncasing Rust\n\ncon 19, one creature within 20 feet of the Rusted. actSaveFail 14 (4d6) Poison damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.rutterkin.mpmm2014"]={title="Rutterkin",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 37 (5d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 15 | CON 17 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmobilizing Fear\n\nWhen a creature that isn't a demon starts its turn within 30 feet of one or more rutterkins, that creature must make a 11 Wisdom saving throw. The creature has disadvantage on the save if it's within 30 feet of six or more rutterkins. On a failed save, the creature becomes frightened of the rutterkins for 1 minute. While frightened in this way, the creature is restrained. At the end of each of the frightened creature's turns, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. On a successful save, the creature is immune to the Crippling Fear of all rutterkins for 24 hours.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (3d6 + 2) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw against disease or become poisoned. At the end of each long rest, the poisoned target can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. If the target is reduced to 0 hit points while poisoned in this way, it dies and instantly transforms into a living manes. The transformation can be undone only by a wish spell."},
  ["creature.rutterkin.mtf2014"]={title="Rutterkin",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 136\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 37 (5d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 15 | CON 17 | INT 5 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCrippling Fear\n\nWhen a creature that isn't a demon starts its turn within 30 feet of three or more rutterkins, it must make a 11 Wisdom saving throw. The creature has disadvantage on the save if it's within 30 feet of six or more rutterkins. On a successful save, the creature is immune to the Crippling Fear of all rutterkins for 24 hours. On a failed save, the creature becomes frightened for 1 minute. While frightened in this way, the creature is restrained. At the end of each of the frightened creature's turns, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (3d6 + 2) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw against disease or become poisoned. At the end of each long rest, the poisoned target can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success. If the target is reduced to 0 hit points while poisoned in this way, it dies and instantly transforms into a living mtf. The transformation of the body can be undone only by a wish spell."},
  ["creature.ruxithid-the-chosen.pabtso2014"]={title="Ruxithid the Chosen",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 99\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 88 (16d8 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 19 | CON 12 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Goblin, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (2/Day)\n\nWhen Ruxithid fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMental Fortitude\n\nRuxithid has advantage on saving throws against the charmed and frightened conditions.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nRuxithid makes two Psi-Charged Scimitar attacks.\n\nPsi-Charged Scimitar\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) psychic damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nBrain Tendrils {@recharge 5}\n\nRuxithid unleashes a flurry of crystalline psychic tendrils from his brain, targeting one creature that he can see within 30 feet of himself. The target must succeed on a 15 Dexterity saving throw or take 9 (2d8) psychic damage and have the stunned condition until the start of Ruxithid's next turn.\n\nCombat Command\n\nRuxithid commands one allied creature he can see within 60 feet of himself to strike. The creature can immediately use its reaction to make one melee weapon attack against a target within its reach."},
  ["item.ryath-root.toa2014"]={title="Ryath Root",subtitle="Item - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\nRaridade: unknown\n\nAny creature that ingests a ryath root gains 2d4 temporary hit points. A creature that consumes more than one ryath root in a 24-hour period must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or suffer the poisoned condition for 1 hour."},
  ["creature.rystia-zav.oota2014"]={title="Rystia Zav",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.saber-toothed-tiger.mm2014"]={title="Saber-Toothed Tiger",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 336\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 52 (7d10 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Smell\n\nThe tiger has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on smell.\n\nPounce\n\nIf the tiger moves at least 20 feet straight toward a creature and then hits it with a claw attack on the same turn, that target must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone. If the target is prone, the tiger can make one bite attack against it as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (1d10 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.saber-toothed-tiger.xmm2024"]={title="Saber-Toothed Tiger",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 369\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 52 (7d10 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 17 | CON 15 | INT 3 | WIS 12 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRunning Leap\n\nWith a 10-foot running start, the tiger can XPHB up to 25 feet.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe tiger makes two Rend attacks.\n\nRend\n\nm 6, reach 5 ft. h11 (2d6 + 4) Slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nThe tiger takes the XPHB or XPHB action."},
  ["creature.sabrina-kilgore-levels-1-4.kftgv2014"]={title="Sabrina Kilgore (Levels 1-4)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.sabrina-kilgore-levels-5-8.kftgv2014"]={title="Sabrina Kilgore (Levels 5-8)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["creature.sabrina-kilgore-levels-9-11.kftgv2014"]={title="Sabrina Kilgore (Levels 9-11)",subtitle="Criatura - KftGV - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.sack.phb2014"]={title="Sack",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA sack can hold up to 1 cubic foot or 30 pounds of gear."},
  ["item.sack.xphb2024"]={title="Sack",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Sack holds up to 30 pounds within 1 cubic foot."},
  ["spell.sacred-flame.phb2014"]={title="Sacred Flame",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\nFlame-like radiance descends on a creature that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d8 radiant damage. The target gains no benefit from cover for this saving throw.\n\nThe spell's damage increases by 1d8 when you reach 5th level (2d8), 11th level (3d8), and 17th level (4d8)."},
  ["spell.sacred-flame.xphb2024"]={title="Sacred Flame",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 313\n\nFlame-like radiance descends on a creature that you can see within range. The target must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 1d8 Radiant damage. The target gains no benefit from XPHB or Three-Quarters XPHB for this save."},
  ["feature.sacred-oath.phb2014.paladin.base.3"]={title="Sacred Oath",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\nWhen you reach 3rd level, you swear the oath that binds you as a paladin forever. Up to this time you have been in a preparatory stage, committed to the path but not yet sworn to it. Now you choose from the list of available oaths.\n\nYour choice grants you features at 3rd level and again at 7th, 15th, and 20th level. Those features include oath spells and the Channel Divinity feature.\n\nOath Spells\n\nEach oath has a list of associated spells. You gain access to these spells at the levels specified in the oath description. Once you gain access to an oath spell, you always have it prepared. Oath spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare each day.\n\nIf you gain an oath spell that doesn't appear on the paladin spell list, the spell is nonetheless a paladin spell for you.\n\nBreaking Your Oath\n\nA paladin tries to hold to the highest standards of conduct, but even the most virtuous paladin is fallible. Sometimes the right path proves too demanding, sometimes a situation calls for the lesser of two evils, and sometimes the heat of emotion causes a paladin to transgress his or her oath.\n\nA paladin who has broken a vow typically seeks absolution from a cleric who shares his or her faith or from another paladin of the same order. The paladin might spend an all-night vigil in prayer as a sign of penitence, or undertake a fast or similar act of self-denial. After a rite of confession and forgiveness, the paladin starts fresh.\n\nIf a paladin willfully violates his or her oath and shows no sign of repentance, the consequences can be more serious. At the DM's discretion, an impenitent paladin might be forced to abandon this class and adopt another, or perhaps to take the Oathbreaker paladin option that appears in the Dungeon Master's Guide."},
  ["feature.sacred-oath-feature.phb2014.paladin.base.7"]={title="Sacred Oath feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\nAt 7th level, you gain a feature granted to you by your Sacred Oath."},
  ["feature.sacred-oath-feature.phb2014.paladin.base.15"]={title="Sacred Oath feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\nAt 15th level, you gain a feature granted to you by your Sacred Oath."},
  ["feature.sacred-oath-feature.phb2014.paladin.base.20"]={title="Sacred Oath feature",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 82\n\nAt 20th level, you gain a feature granted to you by your Sacred Oath."},
  ["creature.sacred-statue.mpmm2014"]={title="Sacred Statue",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 114\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 95 (10d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 8 | CON 19 | INT 14 | WIS 19 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages the {@creature eidolon|MPMM} knew in life\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: cold, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the statue is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the statue move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the statue isn't an object.\n\nGhostly Inhabitant\n\nThe MPMM that enters the statue remains inside it until the statue drops to 0 hit points, the eidolon uses a bonus action to move out of the statue, or the eidolon is turned or forced out by an effect such as the dispel evil and good spell. When the eidolon leaves the statue, it appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the statue.\n\nInert\n\nWithout an MPMM inside, the statue is an object.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe statue doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe statue makes two Slam or Rock attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h43 (6d12 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 8 to hit, range 60 ft./240 ft., one target. h37 (6d10 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.sacred-statue.mtf2014"]={title="Sacred Statue",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 194\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 95 (10d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 8 | CON 19 | INT 14 | WIS 19 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: the languages the eidolon knew in life\n\nResistencias: acid, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: cold, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the statue remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a normal statue.\n\nGhostly Inhabitant\n\nThe MTF that enters the sacred statue remains inside it until the statue drops to 0 hit points, the eidolon uses a bonus action to move out of the statue, or the eidolon is turned or forced out by an effect such as the dispel evil and good spell. When the eidolon leaves the statue, it appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the statue.\n\nInert\n\nWhen not inhabited by an MTF, the statue is an object.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe statue makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h43 (6d12 + 4) bludgeoning damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 8 to hit, range 60/240 ft., one target. h37 (6d10 + 4) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.sacred-stone-monk.pota2014"]={title="Sacred Stone Monk",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 196\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 15 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: tremorsense 10 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUnarmored Defense\n\nWhile the monk is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its AC includes its Wisdom modifier.\n\nUnarmored Movement\n\nWhile the monk is wearing no armor and wielding no shield, its walking speed increases by 10 feet (included in its speed).\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe monk makes two melee attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nThe monk adds 2 to its AC against one melee or ranged weapon attack that would hit it. To do so, the monk must see the attacker."},
  ["feature.sacred-weapon.phb2014.paladin.devotion.3"]={title="Sacred Weapon",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.sacred-weapon.xphb2024.paladin.devotion.3"]={title="Sacred Weapon",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["magicitem.saddle-of-the-cavalier.dmg2014"]={title="Saddle of the Cavalier",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 199\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile in this saddle on a mount, you can't be dismounted against your will if you're conscious, and attack rolls against the mount have disadvantage."},
  ["magicitem.saddle-of-the-cavalier.xdmg2024"]={title="Saddle of the Cavalier",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 302\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile in this saddle on a mount, you can't be dismounted against your will if you're conscious, and attack rolls against the mount have disadvantage."},
  ["item.saddlebags.phb2014"]={title="Saddlebags",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.saemon-havarian.mabjov2014"]={title="Saemon Havarian",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 14/17\n\nPV: 156 (24d8 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 18 | WIS 11 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nSaemon wears a quiver of Ehlonna (holding PHB).\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSaemon makes three Handaxe attacks.\n\nHandaxe\n\nmw,rw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) force damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nArcane Shield\n\nSaemon conjures a swirling yellow barrier and until the start of his next turn he adds +5 to his AC, including against the triggering attack, and he takes no damage from magic missile.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nHurl\n\nSaemon makes a ranged Handaxe attack.\n\nCast a Spell (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nSaemon uses Spellcasting.\n\nAnimate Objects (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nSaemon casts animate objects, targeting up to 10 handaxes he has thrown at enemies. If there are not 10 handaxes available, then he provides the remaining handaxes from his quiver of Ehlonna. Handaxes are Tiny objects."},
  ["creature.saeth-cromley.wdh2014"]={title="Saeth Cromley",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nCHA 14\n\nIdiomas: Common"},
  ["item.saffron.phb2014"]={title="Saffron",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.saffron.xdmg2024"]={title="Saffron",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.sage.cm2014"]={title="Sage",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 9\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 22 (5d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 10 | CON 10 | INT 18 | WIS 15 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any four languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShocking Grasp (Cantrip)\n\nms 6 to hit (with advantage if the target is wearing armor made of metal), reach 5 ft., one creature. h9 (2d8) lightning damage, and the target can't take reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nShield (1st-Level Spell; 3/Day)\n\nWhen the sage is hit by an attack or targeted by a magic missile spell, it calls forth an invisible barrier of magical force that protects it. Until the start of its next turn, the sage has a +5 bonus to AC, including against the triggering attack, and it takes no damage from magic missile."},
  ["background.sage.phb2014"]={title="Sage",subtitle="Background - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 137\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Languages:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Researcher\n\nWhen you attempt to learn or recall a piece of lore, if you do not know that information, you often know where and from whom you can obtain it. Usually, this information comes from a library, scriptorium, university, or a sage or other learned person or creature. Your DM might rule that the knowledge you seek is secreted away in an almost inaccessible place, or that it simply cannot be found. Unearthing the deepest secrets of the multiverse can require an adventure or even a whole campaign.\n\nSpecialty\n\nTo determine the nature of your scholarly training, roll a d8 or choose from the options in the table below.\n\nd8 | Field of Study\n\n1 | Alchemist\n\n2 | Astronomer\n\n3 | Discredited academic\n\n4 | Librarian\n\n5 | Professor\n\n6 | Researcher\n\n7 | Wizard's apprentice\n\n8 | Scribe\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nSages are defined by their extensive studies, and their characteristics reflect this life of study. Devoted to scholarly pursuits, a sage values knowledge highly—sometimes in its own right, sometimes as a means toward other ideals.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I use polysyllabic words that convey the impression of great erudition.\n\n2 | I've read every book in the world's greatest libraries—or I like to boast that I have.\n\n3 | I'm used to helping out those who aren't as smart as I am, and I patiently explain anything and everything to others.\n\n4 | There's nothing I like more than a good mystery.\n\n5 | I'm willing to listen to every side of an argument before I make my own judgment.\n\n6 | I... speak... slowly... when talking... to idiots,... which... almost... everyone... is... compared... to me.\n\n7 | I am horribly, horribly awkward in social situations.\n\n8 | I'm convinced that people are always trying to steal my secrets.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Knowledge. The path to power and self-improvement is through knowledge. (Neutral)\n\n2 | Beauty. What is beautiful points us beyond itself toward what is true. (Good)\n\n3 | Logic. Emotions must not cloud our logical thinking. (Lawful)\n\n4 | No Limits. Nothing should fetter the infinite possibility inherent in all existence. (Chaotic)\n\n5 | Power. Knowledge is the path to power and domination. (Evil)\n\n6 | Self-Improvement. The goal of a life of study is the betterment of oneself. (Any)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | It is my duty to protect my students.\n\n2 | I have an ancient text that holds terrible secrets that must not fall into the wrong hands.\n\n3 | I work to preserve a library, university, scriptorium, or monastery.\n\n4 | My life's work is a series of tomes related to a specific field of lore.\n\n5 | I've been searching my whole life for the answer to a certain question.\n\n6 | I sold my soul for knowledge. I hope to do great deeds and win it back.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | I am easily distracted by the promise of information.\n\n2 | Most people scream and run when they see a demon. I stop and take notes on its anatomy.\n\n3 | Unlocking an ancient mystery is worth the price of a civilization.\n\n4 | I overlook obvious solutions in favor of complicated ones.\n\n5 | I speak without really thinking through my words, invariably insulting others.\n\n6 | I can't keep a secret to save my life, or anyone else's."},
  ["background.sage.xphb2024"]={title="Sage",subtitle="Background - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 183\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiency:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["magicitem.sage-card.bmt2014"]={title="Sage Card",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nAs an action, you can brandish this card and use it to cast the Contact Other Plane spell. When you cast the spell in this way, your questions are answered by the mysterious figure depicted on the card. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.sage-s-mirror.coa2014"]={title="Sage's Mirror",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 269\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis item has 3 charges and regains all charges at dusk. You can use an action and expend 1 of the mirror's charges to cast one of the following spells:\n\n• Find the Path\n\n• Legend Lore\n\nWith each use, it is apparent that the information gleaned from the mirror comes from a chamber in the Nine Hells where sages and scholars are tortured for the answers to each question."},
  ["magicitem.sage-s-signet-bear.bmt2014"]={title="Sage's Signet (Bear)",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis gilded ring bears a beautiful engraving and is imbued with powers of keen wisdom and foresight. While wearing this ring, you can use an action to cast the Augury spell from the ring. Once you use the ring to cast the spell, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn.\n\nWhile wearing the Sage's Signet, you can cast the Enlarge/Reduce and Polymorph once each from the ring using your Intelligence as the spellcasting ability. Once you cast each spell from the ring, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.sage-s-signet-hart.bmt2014"]={title="Sage's Signet (Hart)",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis gilded ring bears a beautiful engraving and is imbued with powers of keen wisdom and foresight. While wearing this ring, you can use an action to cast the Augury spell from the ring. Once you use the ring to cast the spell, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn.\n\nWhile wearing the Sage's Signet, you can cast the Aura of Vitality and Mass Cure Wounds once each from the ring using your Intelligence as the spellcasting ability. Once you cast each spell from the ring, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.sage-s-signet-lion.bmt2014"]={title="Sage's Signet (Lion)",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis gilded ring bears a beautiful engraving and is imbued with powers of keen wisdom and foresight. While wearing this ring, you can use an action to cast the Augury spell from the ring. Once you use the ring to cast the spell, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn.\n\nWhile wearing the Sage's Signet, you can cast the Destructive Wave and Fireball once each from the ring using your Intelligence as the spellcasting ability. Once you cast each spell from the ring, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.sage-s-signet-serpent.bmt2014"]={title="Sage's Signet (Serpent)",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis gilded ring bears a beautiful engraving and is imbued with powers of keen wisdom and foresight. While wearing this ring, you can use an action to cast the Augury spell from the ring. Once you use the ring to cast the spell, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn.\n\nWhile wearing the Sage's Signet, you can cast the Fear and Hex once each from the ring using your Intelligence as the spellcasting ability. Once you cast each spell from the ring, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.sage-s-signet-songbird.bmt2014"]={title="Sage's Signet (Songbird)",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis gilded ring bears a beautiful engraving and is imbued with powers of keen wisdom and foresight. While wearing this ring, you can use an action to cast the Augury spell from the ring. Once you use the ring to cast the spell, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn.\n\nWhile wearing the Sage's Signet, you can cast the Charm Person and Hypnotic Pattern once each from the ring using your Intelligence as the spellcasting ability. Once you cast each spell from the ring, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["magicitem.sage-s-signet-wolf.bmt2014"]={title="Sage's Signet (Wolf)",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 37\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis gilded ring bears a beautiful engraving and is imbued with powers of keen wisdom and foresight. While wearing this ring, you can use an action to cast the Augury spell from the ring. Once you use the ring to cast the spell, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn.\n\nWhile wearing the Sage's Signet, you can cast the Freedom of Movement and Pass without Trace once each from the ring using your Intelligence as the spellcasting ability. Once you cast each spell from the ring, the ring can't cast the spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.sahuagin.mm2014"]={title="Sahuagin",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 263\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe sahuagin has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe sahuagin can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe sahuagin can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sahuagin makes two melee attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws or spear.\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) slashing damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) piercing damage, or 5 (1d8 + 1) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack."},
  ["language.sahuagin.mm2014"]={title="Sahuagin",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 263"},
  ["language.sahuagin.xmm2024"]={title="Sahuagin",subtitle="Idioma - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 265"},
  ["creature.sahuagin-baron.mm2014"]={title="Sahuagin Baron",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 76 (9d10 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 50\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe sahuagin has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe sahuagin can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe sahuagin can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sahuagin makes three attacks: one with his bite and two with his claws or trident.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d4 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nTrident\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-baron.xmm2024"]={title="Sahuagin Baron",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 76 (9d10 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 50\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\nResistencias: acid, cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe sahuagin has XPHB on attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its XPHB.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe sahuagin can breathe air and water, but it must be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating outside water.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe sahuagin can magically control sharks within 120 feet of itself, using a special telepathy.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sahuagin makes three Trident attacks.\n\nTrident\n\nm,r 7, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFiendish Blood\n\nactTrigger The sahuagin takes Piercing or Slashing damage. dcon 14, each creature of the sahuagin's choice in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the sahuagin. actSaveFail 10 (3d6) Acid damage, and the target is cursed until it finishes a XPHB or XPHB. While cursed, the target can't benefit from the XPHB condition, its XPHB decreases by 10 feet, and all Fiends within 120 feet of the target can sense its location regardless of interposing obstacles."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-blademaster.gos2014"]={title="Sahuagin Blademaster",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 249\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 97 (15d8 + 30)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 12 | WIS 11 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe blademaster has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe blademaster can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe blademaster can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe blademaster makes three attacks with its wavecutter blade, or one attack with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nWavecutter Blade\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-champion.gos2014"]={title="Sahuagin Champion",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 249\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 71 (13d8 + 13)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe champion has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe champion can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe champion can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe champion makes three attacks with its spear, or one attack with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage, or 7 (1d8 + 3) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-coral-smasher.gos2014"]={title="Sahuagin Coral Smasher",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 249\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe coral smasher has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe coral smasher can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe coral smasher can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe coral smasher deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe coral smasher makes two attacks with its warhammer, or one attack with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nWarhammer\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-deep-diver.gos2014"]={title="Sahuagin Deep Diver",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 250\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 91 (14d8 + 28)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe deep diver has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nBrine Lurker\n\nThe deep diver has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made while submerged in water.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe deep diver can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nLure\n\nThe deep diver can cause its lure to light up or darken at will. While the lure is lit, the deep diver sheds bright light in a 30-foot radius centered on itself and dim light for an additional 20 feet.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe deep diver can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe deep diver makes two attacks with its glaive, or one attack with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nGlaive\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h13 (2d10 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nLight of Sekolah\n\nThe deep diver pulses magical light from its lure. Any creature within 30 feet of the deep diver that can see the light must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed until the end of its next turn. A creature charmed in this way is incapacitated as it stares at the light."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-hatchling-swarm.gos2014"]={title="Sahuagin Hatchling Swarm",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 250\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / L\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 52 (8d10 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, swim: 40\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: bludgeoning, piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, prone, restrained, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe swarm has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nSeething\n\nOnce it enters combat, the swarm deals 10 slashing damage to itself at the end of its turn if it did not make an attack on that turn. This damage ignores resistance, and it cannot reduce the swarm to 0 hit points.\n\nSwarm\n\nThe swarm can occupy another creature's space and vice versa, and it can move through any opening large enough for a Tiny creature. The swarm can't regain hit points or gain temporary hit points.\n\nWater Breathing\n\nThe swarm can breathe only underwater.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBites\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 0 ft., one creature in the swarm's space. h14 (4d6) piercing damage, or 7 (2d6) piercing damage if the swarm has half of its hit points or fewer."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-high-priestess.gos2014"]={title="Sahuagin High Priestess",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 251\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 71 (11d8 + 22)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 12 | CON 14 | INT 12 | WIS 16 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe high priestess has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe high priestess can breathe air and water, but she needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe high priestess can magically command any shark within 120 feet of her, using a limited telepathy.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe high priestess makes two attacks with her toothsome staff, or one attack with her bite and one with her claws.\n\nToothsome Staff\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-priest.xmm2024"]={title="Sahuagin Priest",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 265\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 38 (7d8 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 13\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\nResistencias: acid, cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe sahuagin has XPHB on attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its XPHB.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe sahuagin can breathe air and water, but it must be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating outside water.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe sahuagin can magically control sharks within 120 feet of itself, using a special telepathy.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nFiendish Aid (2/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sahuagin makes two Spectral Jaws attacks.\n\nSpectral Jaws\n\nm,r 4, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h11 (2d8 + 2) Force damage."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-priestess.mm2014"]={title="Sahuagin Priestess",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 13\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe sahuagin has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe sahuagin can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe sahuagin can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sahuagin makes two melee attacks: one with her bite and one with her claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-warlock-of-uk-otoa.egw2014"]={title="Sahuagin Warlock of Uk'otoa",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 297\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 22 (5d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 10 | CON 11 | INT 8 | WIS 8 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe warlock has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe warlock can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe warlock can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe warlock makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its Sword of Fathoms.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nSword of Fathoms\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) slashing damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or begin choking. The choking creature is incapacitated until the end of its next turn, when the effect ends on it.\n\nEldritch Blast (Cantrip)\n\nrs 5 to hit, range 120 ft., one creature. h5 (1d10) force damage."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-warrior.xmm2024"]={title="Sahuagin Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 264\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 11 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\nResistencias: acid, cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe sahuagin has XPHB on attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its XPHB.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe sahuagin can breathe air and water, but it must be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating outside water.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe sahuagin can magically control sharks within 120 feet of itself, using a special telepathy.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sahuagin makes two Claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d6 + 1) Slashing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAquatic Charge\n\nThe sahuagin swims up to its XPHB straight toward an enemy it can see."},
  ["creature.sahuagin-wave-shaper.gos2014"]={title="Sahuagin Wave Shaper",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 251\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 60 (11d8 + 11)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 16 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sahuagin\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBlood Frenzy\n\nThe wave shaper has advantage on melee attack rolls against any creature that doesn't have all its hit points.\n\nLimited Amphibiousness\n\nThe wave shaper can breathe air and water, but it needs to be submerged at least once every 4 hours to avoid suffocating.\n\nShark Telepathy\n\nThe wave shaper can magically command any shark within 120 feet of it, using a limited telepathy.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe wave shaper makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d8 + 1) piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) cold damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d8 + 1) slashing damage plus 13 (3d8) cold damage.\n\nWhirlpool (1/Day)\n\nThe wave shaper targets a body of water at least 50 feet square and 25 feet deep, causing a whirlpool to form in the center of the area. The whirlpool forms a vortex that is 5 feet wide at the base, up to 50 feet wide at the top, 25 feet tall, and lasts for 1 minute or until the wave shaper is incapacitated. Any creature or object in the water and within 25 feet of the vortex is pulled 10 feet toward it. A creature can swim away from the vortex by succeeding on a 14 Strength (Athletics) check.\n\nWhen a creature enters the vortex for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it must make a 14 Strength saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 9 (2d8) bludgeoning damage and is caught in the vortex until it ends. On a success, the creature takes half damage and isn't caught in the vortex. A creature caught in the vortex can use its action to try to swim away from the vortex as described above, but it has disadvantage on the Strength (Athletics) check to do so.\n\nThe first time each turn that an object enters the vortex, the object takes 9 (2d8) bludgeoning damage. This damage occurs each round it remains in the vortex."},
  ["creature.saidra-d-honaire.rhw2014"]={title="Saidra d'Honaire",subtitle="Criatura - RHW - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 90 (12d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, fly: 60\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 17 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: acid, bludgeoning, cold, fire, piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDarklord Restoration\n\nIf Saidra dies, she revives with all her XPHB in 1d10 weeks somewhere in Dementlieu.\n\nIncorporeal Movement\n\nSaidra can move through other creatures and objects as if they were XPHB. She takes 5 (1d10) Force damage if she ends her turn inside an object.\n\nLie Detector\n\nSaidra knows whether she hears a lie.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day, or 4/Day in Domain)\n\nIf Saidra fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, Saidra has XPHB on ability checks and attack rolls\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nTruth or Die (1/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSaidra makes three Necrotic Burst attacks. She can replace one of these attacks with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nNecrotic Burst\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft. h14 (2d10 + 3) Necrotic damage.\n\nLife Drain\n\ncon 15, one creature Saidra can see within 30 feet. actSaveFail 28 (8d6) Necrotic damage, and its XPHB maximum decreases by an amount equal to the damage taken. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\nAt Will:\n\nXPHB (duchess form only), XPHB (Red Death form only).\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nShape-Shift\n\nSaidra shape-shifts into the Red Death, or she returns to her true form as the duchess. Her game statistics are the same in each form. Any equipment she is wearing or carrying isn't transformed.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nLash Out\n\nSaidra makes one Necrotic Burst attack.\n\nShadow Veil\n\nSaidra gives herself the XPHB condition until the start of her next turn and can fly up to half her XPHB. The condition ends early immediately after Saidra deals damage. Saidra can't take this action again until the start of her next turn."},
  ["creature.sailback.psx2014"]={title="Sailback",subtitle="Criatura - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.sailing-ship.dmg2014"]={title="Sailing Ship",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["vehicle.sailing-ship.gos2014"]={title="Sailing Ship",subtitle="Veiculo - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\nOn its turn, the ship can take 3 actions, choosing from the options below. It can take only 2 actions if it has fewer than twenty crew and only 1 action if it has fewer than ten. It can't take these actions if it has fewer than three crew.\n\n• Fire Ballista\n\n• Fire Mangonel\n\n• Move"},
  ["item.sailing-ship.xphb2024"]={title="Sailing Ship",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 230\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["background.sailor.phb2014"]={title="Sailor",subtitle="Background - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 139\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Ship's Passage\n\nWhen you need to, you can secure free passage on a sailing ship for yourself and your adventuring companions. You might sail on the ship you served on, or another ship you have good relations with (perhaps one captained by a former crewmate). Because you're calling in a favor, you can't be certain of a schedule or route that will meet your every need. Your Dungeon Master will determine how long it takes to get where you need to go. In return for your free passage, you and your companions are expected to assist the crew during the voyage.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nSailors can be a rough lot, but the responsibilities of life on a ship make them generally reliable as well. Life aboard a ship shapes their outlook and forms their most important attachments.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | My friends know they can rely on me, no matter what.\n\n2 | I work hard so that I can play hard when the work is done.\n\n3 | I enjoy sailing into new ports and making new friends over a flagon of ale.\n\n4 | I stretch the truth for the sake of a good story.\n\n5 | To me, a tavern brawl is a nice way to get to know a new city.\n\n6 | I never pass up a friendly wager.\n\n7 | My language is as foul as an otyugh nest.\n\n8 | I like a job well done, especially if I can convince someone else to do it.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Respect. The thing that keeps a ship together is mutual respect between captain and crew. (Good)\n\n2 | Fairness. We all do the work, so we all share in the rewards. (Lawful)\n\n3 | Freedom. The sea is freedom—the freedom to go anywhere and do anything. (Chaotic)\n\n4 | Mastery. I'm a predator, and the other ships on the sea are my prey. (Evil)\n\n5 | People. I'm committed to my crewmates, not to ideals. (Neutral)\n\n6 | Aspiration. Someday, I'll own my own ship and chart my own destiny. (Any)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | I'm loyal to my captain first, everything else second.\n\n2 | The ship is most important—crewmates and captains come and go.\n\n3 | I'll always remember my first ship.\n\n4 | In a harbor town, I have a paramour whose eyes nearly stole me from the sea.\n\n5 | I was cheated out of my fair share of the profits, and I want to get my due.\n\n6 | Ruthless pirates murdered my captain and crewmates, plundered our ship, and left me to die. Vengeance will be mine.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | I follow orders, even if I think they're wrong.\n\n2 | I'll say anything to avoid having to do extra work.\n\n3 | Once someone questions my courage, I never back down no matter how dangerous the situation.\n\n4 | Once I start drinking, it's hard for me to stop.\n\n5 | I can't help but pocket loose coins and other trinkets I come across.\n\n6 | My pride will probably lead to my destruction."},
  ["background.sailor.xphb2024"]={title="Sailor",subtitle="Background - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 184\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiency:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["magicitem.saint-markovia-s-thighbone.cos2014"]={title="Saint Markovia's Thighbone",subtitle="Item Magico - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nSaint Markovia's thighbone has the properties of a mace of disruption. If it scores one or more hits against a vampire or a vampire spawn in the course of a single battle, the thighbone crumbles into dust once the battle concludes.\n\nAs a youth, Markovia followed her heart and became a priest of the Morninglord soon after her eighteenth birthday. She proved to be a charismatic proselytizer and, before the age of thirty, had gained a reputation for allowing no evil to stand before her.\n\nMarkovia had long considered Strahd a mad tyrant, but only after his transformation into a vampire did she dare to challenge him. As she rallied her followers and prepared to march on Castle Ravenloft, Strahd sent a group of vampire spawn to her abbey. They confronted Markovia and were destroyed to a one.\n\nSuffused with confidence born of a righteous victory, Markovia advanced on Castle Ravenloft. A great battle raged from the catacombs to the parapets. In the end, Markovia never returned to Barovia, and Strahd long afterward walked with a limp and a grimace of pain. It is said that he trapped Markovia in a crypt beneath his castle, and her remains linger there yet.\n\nThe essence of Markovia's saintliness passed partly into her bones as the rest of her body decomposed. Her remaining thighbone is imbued with power that inflicts grievous injury on the undead.\n\nMace of Disruption. When you hit a fiend or an undead with this magic weapon, that creature takes an extra 2d6 radiant damage. If the target has 25 hit points or fewer after taking this damage, it must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or be destroyed. On a successful save, the creature becomes frightened of you until the end of your next turn.\n\nWhile you hold this weapon, it sheds bright light in a 20-foot radius and dim light for an additional 20 feet."},
  ["feature.saint-of-forge-and-fire.xge2024.cleric.forge.17"]={title="Saint of Forge and Fire",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.salamander.mm2014"]={title="Salamander",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 266\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 12\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Ignan\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: fire\n\nVulnerabilidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHeated Body\n\nA creature that touches the salamander or hits it with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 7 (2d6) fire damage.\n\nHeated Weapons\n\nAny metal melee weapon the salamander wields deals an extra 3 (1d6) fire damage on a hit (included in the attack).\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe salamander makes two attacks: one with its spear and one with its tail.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack, plus 3 (1d6) fire damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) fire damage, and the target is grappled (escape 14). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, the salamander can automatically hit the target with its tail, and the salamander can't make tail attacks against other targets."},
  ["creature.salamander.xmm2024"]={title="Salamander",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 267\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 12\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Ignan)\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nVulnerabilidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFire Aura\n\nAt the end of each of the salamander's turns, each creature of the salamander's choice in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the salamander takes 7 (2d6) Fire damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe salamander makes two Flame Spear attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Constrict.\n\nFlame Spear\n\nm,r 7, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Piercing damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage. homThe spear magically returns to the salamander's hand immediately after a ranged attack.\n\nConstrict\n\nstr 15, one Large or smaller creature the salamander can see within 10 feet. actSaveFail 11 (2d6 + 4) Bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) Fire damage. The target has the XPHB condition (escape 14), and it has the XPHB condition until the grapple ends."},
  ["creature.salamander-fire-snake.xmm2024"]={title="Salamander Fire Snake",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 266\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 11 | INT 7 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Primordial but can't speak\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nVulnerabilidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFire Aura\n\nAt the end of each of the salamander's turns, each creature of the salamander's choice in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the salamander takes 3 (1d6) Fire damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Fire damage."},
  ["creature.salamander-inferno-master.xmm2024"]={title="Salamander Inferno Master",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 267\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / L\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 256 (27d10 + 108)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 24 | DEX 16 | CON 18 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Ignan)\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nVulnerabilidades: cold\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFire Aura\n\nAt the end of each of the salamander's turns, each creature of the salamander's choice in a 10-foot XPHB originating from the salamander takes 10 (3d6) Fire damage.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe salamander has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe salamander makes two Flame Trident attacks.\n\nFlame Trident\n\nm,r 12, reach 5 ft. or range 30/90 ft. h16 (2d8 + 7) Piercing damage plus 14 (4d6) Fire damage. homThe trident magically returns to the salamander's hand immediately after a ranged attack.\n\nInferno Blast {@recharge 5}\n\ndex 18, each creature in a 30-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the salamander can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail 35 (10d6) Fire damage, and the target starts XPHB, taking 5 (1d10) Fire damage at the start of each of its turns instead of the normal XPHB damage. The target gains 1 XPHB level whenever it takes this XPHB damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nBlazing Movement\n\nThe salamander moves up to its XPHB without provoking XPHB. During this movement, fire fills a 5-foot XPHB originating from the salamander. When the XPHB enters a creature's space, that creature takes 7 (2d6) Fire damage. A creature can take this damage only once per turn."},
  ["creature.saleeth-the-couatl.awm2014"]={title="Saleeth the Couatl",subtitle="Criatura - AWM - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 19\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 90\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 20 | CON 17 | INT 18 | WIS 20 | CHA 18\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe couatl's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nShielded Mind\n\nThe couatl is immune to scrying and to any effect that would sense its emotions, read its thoughts, or detect its location.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h8 (1d6 + 5) piercing damage. Target must make a 13 Constitution save, or fall unconscious. Another creature can use an action to shake the target awake.\n\nConstrict\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one Medium or smaller creature. h10 (2d6 + 3) bludgeoning damage. Target is grappled (escape 15). The couatl can constrain only one target at a time.\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe couatl magically polymorphs into bestiary, or back into its true form. It reverts to its true form if it dies. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying is absorbed or borne by the new form (the couatl's choice).\n\nIn a new form, the couatl retains its game statistics and ability to speak, but its AC, movement modes, Strength, Dexterity, and other actions are replaced by those of the new form, and it gains any statistics and capabilities (except class features, legendary actions, and lair actions) that the new form has but that it lacks. If the new form has a bite attack, the couatl can use its bite in that form."},
  ["creature.salida.toa2014"]={title="Salida",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nPericias:"},
  ["item.salt.phb2014"]={title="Salt",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.salt.xdmg2024"]={title="Salt",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.samara-strongbones.wdh2014"]={title="Samara Strongbones",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 104\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.samira-arah.jttrc2014"]={title="Samira Arah",subtitle="Criatura - JttRC - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.sammaster-dracolich-form.fraif2014"]={title="Sammaster (Dracolich Form)",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 275\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / H\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 276 (24d12 + 120)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, burrow: 30, fly: 80\n\nSTR 25 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 23 | WIS 15 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Infernal\n\nImunidades: acid, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Sammaster fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nLife Suppression\n\nCreatures within 60 feet of Sammaster can't regain XPHB.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSammaster has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSoul Gem\n\nSammaster has a magical soul gem as his dracolich heart. The gem can't be damaged or removed until he is reduced to 0 XPHB. If Sammaster is reduced to 0 XPHB, his dracolich form dissolves to dust. After 1d10 days, he appears in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of his soul gem (so long as the gem still exists), using the Sammaster (Lich Form) stat block. The gem is a Tiny object that has AC 20; HP 50; and XPHB to Acid, Necrotic, Poison, and Psychic damage. The gem regains all its XPHB at the end of every turn, but it turns to dust if reduced to 0 XPHB.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSammaster makes three Rend attacks. He can replace one attack with a use of Spellcasting to cast XPHB or XPHB (level 6 version).\n\nRend\n\nm 14, reach 10 ft. h18 (2d10 + 7) Slashing damage plus 18 (4d8) Necrotic damage.\n\nCorroding Breath {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 20, each creature in a 90-foot XPHB. actSaveFail 52 (8d12) Acid or Necrotic damage (Sammaster's choice). actSaveSuccess Half damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nPounce\n\nSammaster moves up to half his XPHB, and he makes one Rend attack.\n\nSickening Ray\n\nSammaster uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB (level 6 version).\n\nTerrifying Presence\n\nwis 21, each creature in a 20-foot XPHB originating from Sammaster. actSaveFail 13 (2d12) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail Sammaster can't take this action again until the start of his next turn."},
  ["creature.sammaster-lich-form.fraif2014"]={title="Sammaster (Lich Form)",subtitle="Criatura - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 322 (43d8 + 129)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 23 | WIS 15 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Blindsight 60 ft., Darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Infernal\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, lightning\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Sammaster fails a saving throw, he can choose to succeed instead.\n\nLife Suppression\n\nCreatures within 60 feet of Sammaster can't regain XPHB.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSammaster has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSoul Gem\n\nIf Sammaster is reduced to 0 XPHB while his magical soul gem exists, his lich form dissolves to dust. After 1d10 days, he appears in the space of his soul gem, using the Sammaster (Dracolich Form) stat block. The gem is a Tiny object that has AC 20; HP 50; and XPHB to Acid, Necrotic, Poison, and Psychic damage. The gem regains all its XPHB at the end of every turn, but it turns to dust if reduced to 0 XPHB. If the gem is destroyed, Sammaster can create a new one by completing an 8-hour ritual using a gem worth 1,000+ GP, which the ritual consumes, and by expending 5,000 GP.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nProtective Magic\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSammaster makes three attacks, using Corrosive Burst or Paralyzing Touch in any combination. He can replace two attacks with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nCorrosive Burst\n\nm,r 13, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft. h38 (5d12 + 6) Acid or Necrotic damage (Sammaster's choice).\n\nParalyzing Touch\n\nm 13, reach 5 ft. h16 (3d6 + 6) Cold damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of Sammaster's next turn.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nDeathly Teleport\n\nSammaster teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space he can see, and each creature within 10 feet of the space he left takes 19 (3d12) Necrotic damage.\n\nDissolve\n\nSammaster makes one Corrosive Burst attack.\n\nTerrifying Presence\n\nwis 21, each creature in a 20-foot XPHB originating from Sammaster. actSaveFail 13 (2d12) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. actSaveSuccessOrFail Sammaster can't take this action again until the start of his next turn."},
  ["subclass.samurai.xge2024.fighter.samurai.0"]={title="Samurai",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.samurai.xge2024.fighter.samurai.3"]={title="Samurai",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 31\n\nThe Samurai is a fighter who draws on an implacable fighting spirit to overcome enemies. A Samurai's resolve is nearly unbreakable, and the enemies in a Samurai's path have two choices: yield or die fighting."},
  ["creature.sanbalet.gos2014"]={title="Sanbalet",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 252\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 11 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["spell.sanctuary.phb2014"]={title="Sanctuary",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\nYou ward a creature within range against attack. Until the spell ends, any creature who targets the warded creature with an attack or a harmful spell must first make a Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature must choose a new target or lose the attack or spell. This spell doesn't protect the warded creature from area effects, such as the explosion of a fireball.\n\nIf the warded creature makes an attack, casts a spell that affects an enemy, or deals damage to another creature, this spell ends."},
  ["spell.sanctuary.xphb2024"]={title="Sanctuary",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 313\n\nYou ward a creature within range. Until the spell ends, any creature who targets the warded creature with an attack roll or a damaging spell must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or either choose a new target or lose the attack or spell. This spell doesn't protect the warded creature from areas of effect.\n\nThe spell ends if the warded creature makes an attack roll, casts a spell, or deals damage."},
  ["reward.sanctuary-charm.xdmg2024"]={title="Sanctuary Charm",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 345\n\nAfter spending a XPHB in your XDMG, you gain a magical Charm (see \"XDMG\" in XDMG) that lasts for 7 days or until you use it. The Charm allows you to cast XPHB once without expending a spell slot. You can't gain this Charm again while you still have it."},
  ["feature.sanctuary-vessel.tce2014.warlock.genie.10"]={title="Sanctuary Vessel",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body=""},
  ["magicitem.sanctum-amulet.bgg2014"]={title="Sanctum Amulet",subtitle="Item Magico - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nA black opal pendant hangs at the base of this pearlescent chain. The sacred rune is inscribed on the back of the pendant.\n\nWhile wearing this item, you have resistance to necrotic damage. Additionally, you can cast the spare the dying cantrip using either an action or a bonus action.\n\nInvoking the Rune\n\nWhen a creature you can see within 60 feet of you is reduced to 0 hit points as a result of taking damage, you can use your reaction to invoke the item's rune, causing the pendant to flash with pale light. The creature then instead drops to 1 hit point.\n\nOnce the rune has been invoked, it can't be invoked again until the next dawn."},
  ["reward.sanctum-charm.xdmg2024"]={title="Sanctum Charm",subtitle="Recompensa - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 346\n\nAfter spending a XPHB in your XDMG, you gain a magical Charm (see \"XDMG\" in XDMG) that lasts for 7 days or until you use it. The Charm allows you to cast XPHB once without expending a spell slot. You can't gain this Charm again while you still have it."},
  ["creature.sandesyl-morgia.hotdq2014"]={title="Sandesyl Morgia",subtitle="Criatura - HotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.sandwurm.psa2014"]={title="Sandwurm",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 35\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.sangora.veor2014"]={title="Sangora",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.sangzor.cos2014"]={title="Sangzor",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 160\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 1\n\nPV: 33 (3d10 + 3)\n\nINT 6\n\nResistencias:"},
  ["magicitem.sapphire-buckler.ftd2014"]={title="Sapphire Buckler",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThis crystalline blue shield is fashioned from a sapphire dragon's scale and is created to aid in rooting out the influence of Aberrations. While wielding the shield, you have resistance to psychic and thunder damage. Also, when you take damage from a creature that is within 5 feet of you, you can use your reaction to deal 2d6 thunder damage to that creature.\n\nAs an action, you can use the shield to help you locate Aberrations until the end of your next turn. If any Aberrations are within 1 mile of you, the shield emits a low humming tone for a moment, and you know the direction of all Aberrations within that range. Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.sapphire-dragon-wyrmling.ftd2014"]={title="Sapphire Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 216\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 45 (6d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 15, climb: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft., darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe dragon can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nTunneler\n\nThe dragon can burrow through solid rock at half its burrowing speed and can leave a 5-foot-diameter tunnel in its wake.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) thunder damage.\n\nDebilitating Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a pulse of high-pitched, nearly inaudible sound in a 15-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 13 Constitution saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 22 (4d10) thunder damage and is incapacitated until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, the creature takes half as much damage and isn't incapacitated."},
  ["creature.sapphire-greatwyrm.ftd2014"]={title="Sapphire Greatwyrm",subtitle="Criatura - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / G\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 507 (26d20 + 234)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, burrow: 60, fly: 120, swim: 60\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 14 | CON 29 | INT 30 | WIS 24 | CHA 25\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\nImunidades: thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGem Awakening (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nIf the greatwyrm would be reduced to 0 hit points, its current hit point total instead resets to 400 hit points, it recharges its Breath Weapon, and it regains any expended uses of Legendary Resistance. Additionally, the greatwyrm can now use its Mass Telekinesis action during the next hour. Award a party an additional 90,000 XP (180,000 XP total) for defeating the greatwyrm after its Gem Awakening activates.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the greatwyrm fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe greatwyrm doesn't require food or drink.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Psionics)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Bite attack and two Claw attacks.\n\nBite\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h20 (2d10 + 9) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) force damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (2d8 + 9) slashing damage. If the target is a Huge or smaller creature, it is grappled (escape 19) and is restrained until this grapple ends. The greatwyrm can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\nBreath Weapon {@recharge 5}\n\nThe greatwyrm exhales crushing force in a 300-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, the creature takes 71 (11d12) force damage and is knocked prone. On a successful save, it takes half as much damage and isn't knocked prone. On a success or failure, the creature's speed becomes 0 until the end of its next turn.\n\nMass Telekinesis (Gem Awakening Only; Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe greatwyrm targets any number of creatures and objects it can see within 120 feet of it. No one target can weigh more than 4,000 pounds, and objects can't be targeted if they're being worn or carried. Each targeted creature must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or be restrained in the greatwyrm's telekinetic grip. At the end of a creature's turn, it can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nAt the end of the greatwyrm's turn, it can move each creature or object it has in its telekinetic grip up to 60 feet in any direction, but not beyond 120 feet of itself. In addition, it can choose any number of creatures restrained in this way and deal 45 (7d12) force damage to each of them.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nChange Shape\n\nThe greatwyrm magically transforms into any creature that is Medium or Small, while retaining its game statistics (other than its size). This transformation ends if the greatwyrm is reduced to 0 hit points or uses a bonus action to end it.\n\nPsychic Step\n\nThe greatwyrm magically teleports to an unoccupied space it can see within 60 feet of it.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nClaw\n\nThe greatwyrm makes one Claw attack.\n\nPsionics (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm uses Psychic Step or Spellcasting.\n\nPsychic Beam (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe greatwyrm emits a beam of psychic energy in a 90-foot line that is 10 feet wide. Each creature in that area must make a 26 Intelligence saving throw, taking 27 (5d10) psychic damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.sapphire-sentinel.cm2014"]={title="Sapphire Sentinel",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 178 (17d10 + 85)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 9 | CON 20 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe golem has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe golem's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe golem makes two slam attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h19 (3d8 + 6) bludgeoning damage.\n\nSlow {@recharge 5}\n\nThe golem targets one or more creatures it can see within 10 feet of it. Each target must make a 17 Wisdom saving throw against this magic. On a failed save, a target can't use reactions, its speed is halved, and it can't make more than one attack on its turn. In addition, the target can take either an action or a bonus action on its turn, not both. These effects last for 1 minute. A target can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\nSapphire\n\nThe sapphire has 3 charges. As an action, the golem can expend 1 charge to cast dispel magic (as a 9th-level spell) from the sapphire using Constitution as its spellcasting ability. The sapphire ceases to glow if all its charges are expended, but it regains 1d3 expended charges daily at dawn and glows again once it has 1 or more charges."},
  ["spell.sapping-sting.egw2014"]={title="Sapping Sting",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 0 - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 189\n\nYou sap the vitality of one creature you can see in range. The target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 1d4 necrotic damage and fall prone.\n\nThis spell's damage increases by 1d4 when you reach 5th level (2d4), 11th level (3d4), and 17th level (4d4)."},
  ["creature.sarcelle-malinosh.veor2014"]={title="Sarcelle Malinosh",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["item.sardonyx.dmg2014"]={title="Sardonyx",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none\n\nAn opaque bands of red and white gemstone."},
  ["item.sardonyx.xdmg2024"]={title="Sardonyx",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 214\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA bands of red and white gemstone."},
  ["creature.sarevok.coa2014"]={title="Sarevok",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 48\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 190 (20d8 + 100)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 10 | CON 21 | INT 11 | WIS 18 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\nImunidades: acid, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSarevok has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nIf Sarevok is killed, he gains a new body in 24 hours, regaining all his hit points. The new body appears on the altar of the temple of Bhaal beneath Baldur's Gate. This ability ceases to function if a cleric of good alignment casts Hallow on the altar in the temple of Bhaal.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSarevok makes three Longsword attacks. He can replace one of the attacks with Flames of Bhaal or Spellcasting.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 12 to hit, reach 5ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) slashing damage or 11 (1d10 + 6) if wielded in two hands. The target must succeed on a 18 Constitution saving throw or be cursed by Bhaal, preventing it from regaining hit points. The curse lasts until removed by the Remove Curse spell or similar effect.\n\nFlames of Bhaal\n\nSarevok causes flames to engulf one creature that he can see within 60 feet. The target must succeed on a 18 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) necrotic damage. This damage can't be restored except by a Lesser Restoration spell or similar effect.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nSlash\n\nSarevok makes a Longsword attack.\n\nUnholy Flame\n\nSarevok uses Flames of Bhaal.\n\nChannel Bhaal's Hate (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nSarevok unleashes Bhaal's power. Creatures within 30 feet of Sarevok, including ones behind barriers and around corners, can't regain hit points until the end of Sarevok's next turn."},
  ["creature.sarevok.mabjov2014"]={title="Sarevok",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 153 (18d8 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\nImunidades: acid, necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSarevok has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nRejuvenation\n\nIf Sarevok is killed he gains a new body in 24 hours, regaining all his hit points and becoming active again. The new body appears on the altar of the temple of Bhaal beneath Baldur's Gate. This ability ceases to function if a cleric of good alignment casts Hallow on the altar in the temple of Bhaal.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSarevok makes two Longsword attacks. He may replace one of the attacks with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) slashing damage or 10 (1d10 + 5) if wielded in two hands. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or be cursed by Bhaal. The cursed target can't regain hit points. The curse lasts until removed by the remove curse spell or other magic.\n\nAssassin's Strike\n\nSarevok makes a Longsword attack. If he hits the target and has advantage on the attack roll, then he deals an additional 21 (6d6) poison damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 16 Constitution saving throw or have the poisoned condition for 10 minutes.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nSarevok makes a Longsword attack.\n\nUnholy Flame\n\nSarevok casts sacred flame.\n\nChannel Bhaal's Hate (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nSarevok unleashes Bhaal's power. Creatures within 30 feet of Sarevok, including ones behind barriers and around corners, can't regain hit points until the end of Sarevok's next turn."},
  ["deity.sargonnas.dsotdq2014"]={title="Sargonnas",subtitle="Divindade - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\nSargonnas is the unpredictable god of flame, vengeance, and wrath. Though he's a consort to Takhisis, he schemes against her as often as he fights on her behalf. He is worshiped by those who seek retribution. His true form is that of a monstrous minotaur, and many minotaurs revere him under the name Sargas."},
  ["deity.sargonnas.phb2014"]={title="Sargonnas",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["creature.sarith-kzekarit.oota2014"]={title="Sarith Kzekarit",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 7\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.sarlamir.dsotdq2014"]={title="Sarlamir",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 102\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.sarlona-trinket.erlw2014"]={title="Sarlona Trinket",subtitle="Item - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 138\n\nRaridade: none\n\nd8 | Trinket\n\n1 | A polished crystal sphere; when you clutch it in your fist, a telepathic voice recites a story in your mind\n\n2 | A teardrop pendant made from polished shell; when you hold it, you see the image of a young Riedran man\n\n3 | A six-sided crystal die; when you roll it, you feel a surge of emotion for six seconds\n\n4 | A sealed vial filled with faintly luminescent blue mist\n\n5 | A crystal disk engraved with a labyrinthine pattern\n\n6 | A leather-bound collection of kalashtar poetry called Shards of the Light\n\n7 | A sphere of polished crystal; when you hold it in your palm, you feel that it knows you and understands you\n\n8 | A cup and ball toy; when you successfully catch the ball in the cup, you feel a momentary surge of joy"},
  ["creature.sarrukh-tyrant.aud2014"]={title="Sarrukh Tyrant",subtitle="Criatura - AUD - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 17\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 256 (27d8 + 135)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 15 | CON 20 | INT 23 | WIS 19 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the sarrukh fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe sarrukh has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sarrukh makes two attacks, using Bite or Fearsome Fauchard in any combination.\n\nBite\n\nm 12, reach 5 ft. h13 (2d6 + 6) Piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) Poison damage.\n\nFearsome Fauchard\n\nm,r 12, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft. h17 (2d10 + 6) Piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it has the XPHB condition. If the target already has the XPHB condition, it takes an additional 10 (3d6) Psychic damage. homThe fauchard magically returns to the sarrukh's hand immediately after a ranged attack.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nShape Control\n\nactTrigger A creature the sarrukh can see shape-shifts. actResponse The sarrukh chooses the resulting form from among the options available to the shape-shifting creature or prevents the creature from shape-shifting.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nFearsome Glance\n\nwis 20, one creature the sarrukh can see within 30 feet. actSaveFail 18 (4d8) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition. actSaveSuccess Half damage only.\n\nSlither\n\nThe sarrukh moves up to half its XPHB without provoking XPHB, and it makes one Bite attack.\n\nTwisted Transformation\n\nThe sarrukh uses Spellcasting to cast XPHB, and if the target fails its saving throw, the target also has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn. The sarrukh can't take this action again until the start of its next turn."},
  ["deity.sarula-iliene.mtf2014"]={title="Sarula Iliene",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["creature.sarusanda-allester.veor2014"]={title="Sarusanda Allester",subtitle="Criatura - VEoR - 2014",body="Pagina: 95\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid\n\nIdiomas: Celestial, Common, Draconic, Elvish, any four languages, telepathy 120 ft."},
  ["creature.satyr.mm2014"]={title="Satyr",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 267\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 31 (7d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 11 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nRam\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["species.satyr.mot2014"]={title="Satyr",subtitle="Especie - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nAge\n\nSatyrs mature and age at about the same rate as humans.\n\nAlignment\n\nSatyrs delight in living a life free of the mantle of law. They gravitate toward being good, but some have devious streaks and enjoy causing dismay.\n\nSize\n\nSatyrs range from just under 5 feet to about 6 feet in height, with generally slender builds. Your size is Medium.\n\nFey\n\nYour creature type is fey, rather than humanoid.\n\nRam\n\nYou can use your head and horns to make unarmed strikes. If you hit with them, you deal bludgeoning damage equal to 1d4 + your Strength modifier.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMirthful Leaps\n\nWhenever you make a long or high jump, you can roll a d8 and add the number rolled to the number of feet you cover, even when making a standing jump. This extra distance costs movement as normal.\n\nReveler\n\nYou have proficiency in the Performance and Persuasion skills, and you have proficiency with one PHB of your choice.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and Sylvan."},
  ["species.satyr.mpmm2014"]={title="Satyr",subtitle="Especie - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\nCreature Type\n\nYou are a Fey.\n\nRam\n\nYou can use your head and horns to make unarmed strikes. When you hit with them, the strike deals 1d6 + your Strength modifier bludgeoning damage, instead of the bludgeoning damage normal for an unarmed strike.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against spells.\n\nMirthful Leaps\n\nWhenever you make a long jump or a high jump, you can roll a d8 and add the number rolled to the number of feet you cover, even when making a standing jump. This extra distance costs movement as usual.\n\nReveler\n\nAs an embodiment of revelry, you have proficiency in the Performance and Persuasion skills, and you have proficiency with one PHB of your choice."},
  ["creature.satyr.xmm2024"]={title="Satyr",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 268\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 31 (7d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 11 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nHooves\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d4 + 3) Bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Medium or smaller creature, the satyr pushes the target up to 10 feet straight away from itself.\n\nMockery\n\nwis 12, one creature the satyr can see within 90 feet. actSaveFail 5 (1d6 + 2) Psychic damage."},
  ["creature.satyr-reveler.mot2014"]={title="Satyr Reveler",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 242\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 33 (6d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEnthralling Performance\n\nIf the satyr performs for at least 1 minute, it chooses up to four humanoids within 60 feet of it who watched or listened to the entire performance. Each target must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or be charmed. While charmed in this way, the target idolizes the satyr and will take part in the satyr's revels. The charmed condition ends for the creature after 1 hour, if it takes any damage, if the satyr attacks the target, or if the target witnesses the satyr attacking or damaging any of the target's allies.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSleepless Reveler\n\nMagic can't put the satyr to sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe satyr makes two ram attacks or two shortbow attacks.\n\nRam\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.satyr-revelmaster.xmm2024"]={title="Satyr Revelmaster",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 268\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 82 (15d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 12 | WIS 14 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe satyr makes three Prance attacks.\n\nPrance\n\nm 7, reach 5 ft. h13 (2d8 + 4) Bludgeoning damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the start of the satyr's next turn.\n\nFey Melody {@recharge 4}\n\nThe satyr conjures a charming or frightening song. wis 14, each enemy in a 60-foot XPHB originating from the satyr. actSaveFail The target is subjected to the song's effect:\n\n• Charming The target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition and uses all its movement to dance in place. The effect ends on the target if it takes any damage.\n\n• Frightening 10 (2d6 + 3) Psychic damage, and the target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. If the target ends its turn out of line of sight from the satyr, the condition ends on it."},
  ["creature.satyr-thornbearer.mot2014"]={title="Satyr Thornbearer",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 38 (7d8 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe satyr has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSleepless Reveler\n\nMagic can't put the satyr to sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe satyr makes three ram attacks or three shortbow attacks.\n\nRam\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) bludgeoning damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nHail of Arrows (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe satyr fires an arrow that magically transforms into a flurry of missiles in a 30-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 14 Dexterity saving throw, taking 17 (5d6) piercing damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.sauriv.gos2014"]={title="Sauriv",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 79\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCA: 13\n\nWIS 18\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic"},
  ["feat.savage-attacker.phb2014"]={title="Savage Attacker",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\nOnce per turn when you roll damage for a melee weapon attack, you can reroll the weapon's damage dice and use either total."},
  ["feat.savage-attacker.xphb2024"]={title="Savage Attacker",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 201\n\nYou've trained to deal particularly damaging strikes. Once per turn when you hit a target with a weapon, you can roll the weapon's damage dice twice and use either roll against the target."},
  ["creature.savid.cos2014"]={title="Savid",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 133\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid"},
  ["deity.savras.phb2014"]={title="Savras",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 294"},
  ["deity.savras.scag2014"]={title="Savras",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\nSavras is a god of divination and fortunetelling. Few people worship him, but many pray to him when performing small rituals of foresight. For example, young men and women sometimes attempt to divine the names of their future spouses by saying a rhyming chant that calls upon Savras while gazing in a mirror.\n\nSavras has no currently active temples in Faerûn, and his shrines are few and far between, tucked away in the corners of libraries and scriptoria. Despite this lack of prominence, certain folk pay regular homage to Savras, including investigators, diviners, judges, and others who have a need to uncover the truth. Such individuals can sometimes be identified by the elaborate staffs they carry in homage to Savras. According to legend, Savras was trapped in Azuth's staff for ages. Azuth eventually freed Savras so long as Savras swore fealty, and today the staff is a potent symbol for those who revere Savras. Devout worshipers take great pains to decorate and embellish their staffs, each hoping that Savras might find it a welcoming place to stop for a time."},
  ["creature.scaladar.wdmm2014"]={title="Scaladar",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 315\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / H\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 94 (7d12 + 49)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 20\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 25 | INT 1 | WIS 12 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: fire\n\nImunidades: force, lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLightning Absorption\n\nWhenever the scaladar is subjected to lightning damage, it takes no damage, and its sting deals an extra 11 (2d10) lightning damage until the end of its next turn.\n\nScaladar Link\n\nThe scaladar knows the location of other scaladar within 100 feet of it, and it can sense when any of them take damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scaladar makes three attacks: two with its claws and one with its sting.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h10 (1d12 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 15). The scaladar has two claws, each of which can grapple one target.\n\nSting\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) lightning damage."},
  ["item.scale-mail.phb2014"]={title="Scale Mail",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 144\n\nRaridade: none\n\nThis armor consists of a coat and leggings (and perhaps a separate skirt) of leather covered with overlapping pieces of metal, much like the scales of a fish. The suit includes gauntlets."},
  ["item.scale-mail.xphb2024"]={title="Scale Mail",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 219\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["reward.scaled-toughness.ftd2014"]={title="Scaled Toughness",subtitle="Recompensa - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\nYour skin toughens, making you resistant to certain types of physical harm. You gain resistance to piercing and slashing damage."},
  ["magicitem.scarab-of-protection.dmg2014"]={title="Scarab of Protection",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 199\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nIf you hold this beetle-shaped medallion in your hand for 1 round, an inscription appears on its surface revealing its magical nature. It provides two benefits while it is on your person:\n\n• You have advantage on saving throws against spells.\n\n• The scarab has 12 charges. If you fail a saving throw against a necromancy spell or a harmful effect originating from an undead creature, you can use your reaction to expend 1 charge and turn the failed save into a successful one. The scarab crumbles into powder and is destroyed when its last charge is expended."},
  ["magicitem.scarab-of-protection.xdmg2024"]={title="Scarab of Protection",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 302\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nThis beetle-shaped medallion provides three benefits while it is on your person.\n\nDefense\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to XPHB.\n\nPreservation\n\nThe scarab has 12 charges. If you fail a saving throw against a Necromancy spell or a harmful effect originating from an Undead, you can take a XPHB to expend 1 charge and turn the failed save into a successful one. The scarab crumbles into powder and is destroyed when its last charge is expended.\n\nSpell Resistance\n\nYou have XPHB on saving throws against spells."},
  ["creature.scarecrow.mm2014"]={title="Scarecrow",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 36 (8d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 13 | CON 11 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 13\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the scarecrow remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from an ordinary, inanimate scarecrow.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scarecrow makes two claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (2d4 + 1) slashing damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of the scarecrow's next turn.\n\nTerrifying Glare\n\nThe scarecrow targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see the scarecrow, the target must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw or be magically frightened until the end of the scarecrow's next turn. The frightened target is paralyzed."},
  ["creature.scarecrow.wtthc2014"]={title="Scarecrow",subtitle="Criatura - WttHC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.scarecrow.xmm2024"]={title="Scarecrow",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 269\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 27 (6d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 13 | CON 11 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 13\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, unconscious\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nFearsome Claw\n\nm 3, reach 5 ft. h6 (2d4 + 1) Slashing damage, and the target has the XPHB condition until the end of the scarecrow's next turn.\n\nTerrifying Glare\n\nwis 11, one creature the scarecrow can see within 30 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of the scarecrow's next turn. While XPHB, the target has the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.scarlet-sentinel.nrh-avitw2014"]={title="Scarlet Sentinel",subtitle="Criatura - NRH-AVitW - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 8\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 6 | CON 14 | INT 1 | WIS 6 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe Scarlet Sentinel is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe Scarlet Sentinel has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe Scarlet Sentinel's weapon attacks are magical.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d8 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["magicitem.scarlet-spellbook.aud2014"]={title="Scarlet Spellbook",subtitle="Item Magico - AUD - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nIrregular scraps of red cloth cover this weathered tome. While attuned to this item, you can use it as a Spellbook and an XPHB.\n\nArcane Stamina\n\nWhen you use your Arcane Recovery feature, you also regain XPHB equal to 2d6 plus half your Wizard level (round down).\n\nImproved Spell Recall\n\nWhen you use your Memorize Spell feature, you can replace an additional level 1+ Wizard spell you have prepared for your Spellcasting feature with another level 1+ spell inscribed in this book."},
  ["spell.scatter.xge2024"]={title="Scatter",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 6 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 164\n\nThe air quivers around up to five creatures of your choice that you can see within range. An unwilling creature must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw to resist this spell. You teleport each affected target to an unoccupied space that you can see within 120 feet of you. That space must be on the ground or on a floor."},
  ["vehicle.scavenger.bgdia2014"]={title="Scavenger",subtitle="Veiculo - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\nCrushing Wheels\n\nThe Scavenger can move through the space of any Large or smaller creature. When it does, the creature must succeed on a 12 Dexterity saving throw or take 16 (3d10) bludgeoning damage and be knocked prone. If the creature was already prone, it takes an extra 16 (3d10) bludgeoning damage. This trait can't be used against a particular creature more than once each turn.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe Scavenger's weapon attacks are magical.\n\nProne Deficiency\n\nIf the Scavenger rolls over and falls prone, it can't right itself and is incapacitated until flipped upright."},
  ["feature.scholar.xphb2024.wizard.base.2"]={title="Scholar",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["magicitem.scholar-s-anchoring-bangle.au2014"]={title="Scholar's Anchoring Bangle",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 122\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis heavy magical bracelet inures your mind against potential distractions. While wearing this bracelet, you gain the following benefits.\n\nDeep Knowledge\n\nWhen you take the XPHB action and make an Intelligence check using a skill in which you have proficiency, you can treat a d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.\n\nSingle-Minded Focus\n\nWhen you fail a Constitution saving throw to maintain XPHB, you can take a XPHB to succeed instead. Once you use this property, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["item.scholar-s-pack.phb2014"]={title="Scholar's Pack",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 151\n\nRaridade: none\n\nIncludes:\n\n• a phb\n\n• a phb of lore\n\n• a phb\n\n• an phb\n\n• 10 phb\n\n• a little bag of sand\n\n• a small knife."},
  ["item.scholar-s-pack.xphb2024"]={title="Scholar's Pack",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 228\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA Scholar's Pack contains the following items: XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, 10 flasks of XPHB, 10 sheets of XPHB, and XPHB."},
  ["creature.scholarly-agent.crcotn2014"]={title="Scholarly Agent",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 22 (4d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 16 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nArcane Shock\n\nms,rs 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30 ft., one target. h14 (2d10 + 3) lightning damage. If the target is a creature, it can't take reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nGlyph of Shielding\n\nThe agent adds 2 to its AC against one attack that would hit it. To do so, the agent must be able to see the attacker and have a free hand."},
  ["creature.scholarly-excavator.crcotn2014"]={title="Scholarly Excavator",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 206\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 67 (9d8 + 27)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 14 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus two other languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSiege Expert\n\nThe excavator deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe excavator makes three Thunderous Warhammer attacks.\n\nThunderous Warhammer\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d10 + 2) thunder damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nTelekinetic Toss {@recharge 5}\n\nThe excavator targets one Medium or smaller creature or an object weighing 300 pounds or less that isn't being worn or carried. The target, which must be within 30 feet of the excavator and visible to it, is magically pushed up to 20 feet horizontally in a direction of the excavator's choice. If the target is a creature, it can make a 13 Strength saving throw to resist the effect and is not pushed on a successful save."},
  ["creature.scholarly-mastermind.crcotn2014"]={title="Scholarly Mastermind",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 207\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 82 (15d8 + 15)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 13 | INT 18 | WIS 16 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus three other languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe mastermind makes two Arcane Shock or Dagger of the Poisoned Mind attacks.\n\nArcane Shock\n\nms,rs 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft., one target. h26 (4d10 + 4) lightning damage. If the target is a creature, it can't take reactions until the start of its next turn.\n\nDagger of the Poisoned Mind\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) psychic damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of its next turn."},
  ["subclass.school-of-abjuration.phb2014.wizard.abjuration.0"]={title="School of Abjuration",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.school-of-abjuration.phb2014.wizard.abjuration.2"]={title="School of Abjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 115\n\nThe School of Abjuration emphasizes magic that blocks, banishes, or protects. Detractors of this school say that its tradition is about denial, negation rather than positive assertion. You understand, however, that ending harmful effects, protecting the weak, and banishing evil influences is anything but a philosophical void. It is a proud and respected vocation.\n\nCalled abjurers, members of this school are sought when baleful spirits require exorcism, when important locations must be guarded against magical spying, and when portals to other planes of existence must be closed."},
  ["feature.school-of-abjuration.phb2014.wizard.abjuration.3"]={title="School of Abjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-conjuration.phb2014.wizard.conjuration.0"]={title="School of Conjuration",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.school-of-conjuration.phb2014.wizard.conjuration.2"]={title="School of Conjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nAs a conjurer, you favor spells that produce objects and creatures out of thin air. You can conjure billowing clouds of killing fog or summon creatures from elsewhere to fight on your behalf. As your mastery grows, you learn spells of transportation and can teleport yourself across vast distances, even to other planes of existence, in an instant."},
  ["feature.school-of-conjuration.phb2014.wizard.conjuration.3"]={title="School of Conjuration",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-divination.phb2014.wizard.divination.0"]={title="School of Divination",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.school-of-divination.phb2014.wizard.divination.2"]={title="School of Divination",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 116\n\nThe counsel of a diviner is sought by royalty and commoners alike, for all seek a clearer understanding of the past, present, and future. As a diviner, you strive to part the veils of space, time, and consciousness so that you can see clearly. You work to master spells of discernment, remote viewing, supernatural knowledge, and foresight."},
  ["feature.school-of-divination.phb2014.wizard.divination.3"]={title="School of Divination",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-enchantment.phb2014.wizard.enchantment.0"]={title="School of Enchantment",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.school-of-enchantment.phb2014.wizard.enchantment.2"]={title="School of Enchantment",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\nAs a member of the School of Enchantment, you have honed your ability to magically entrance and beguile other people and monsters. Some enchanters are peacemakers who bewitch the violent to lay down their arms and charm the cruel into showing mercy. Others are tyrants who magically bind the unwilling into their service. Most enchanters fall somewhere in between."},
  ["feature.school-of-enchantment.phb2014.wizard.enchantment.3"]={title="School of Enchantment",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-evocation.phb2014.wizard.evocation.0"]={title="School of Evocation",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.school-of-evocation.phb2014.wizard.evocation.2"]={title="School of Evocation",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 117\n\nYou focus your study on magic that creates powerful elemental effects such as bitter cold, searing flame, rolling thunder, crackling lightning, and burning acid. Some evokers find employment in military forces, serving as artillery to blast enemy armies from afar. Others use their spectacular power to protect the weak, while some seek their own gain as bandits, adventurers, or aspiring tyrants."},
  ["feature.school-of-evocation.phb2014.wizard.evocation.3"]={title="School of Evocation",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-illusion.phb2014.wizard.illusion.0"]={title="School of Illusion",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.school-of-illusion.phb2014.wizard.illusion.2"]={title="School of Illusion",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\nYou focus your studies on magic that dazzles the senses, befuddles the mind, and tricks even the wisest folk. Your magic is subtle, but the illusions crafted by your keen mind make the impossible seem real. Some illusionists—including many gnome wizards—are benign tricksters who use their spells to entertain. Others are more sinister masters of deception, using their illusions to frighten and fool others for their personal gain."},
  ["feature.school-of-illusion.phb2014.wizard.illusion.3"]={title="School of Illusion",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-necromancy.phb2014.wizard.necromancy.0"]={title="School of Necromancy",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.school-of-necromancy.phb2014.wizard.necromancy.2"]={title="School of Necromancy",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 118\n\nThe School of Necromancy explores the cosmic forces of life, death, and undeath. As you focus your studies in this tradition, you learn to manipulate the energy that animates all living things. As you progress, you learn to sap the life force from a creature as your magic destroys its body, transforming that vital energy into magical power you can manipulate.\n\nMost people see necromancers as menacing, or even villainous, due to the close association with death. Not all necromancers are evil, but the forces they manipulate are considered taboo by many societies."},
  ["feature.school-of-necromancy.phb2014.wizard.necromancy.3"]={title="School of Necromancy",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["subclass.school-of-transmutation.phb2014.wizard.transmutation.0"]={title="School of Transmutation",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.school-of-transmutation.phb2014.wizard.transmutation.2"]={title="School of Transmutation",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 119\n\nYou are a student of spells that modify energy and matter. To you, the world is not a fixed thing, but eminently mutable, and you delight in being an agent of change. You wield the raw stuff of creation and learn to alter both physical forms and mental qualities. Your magic gives you the tools to become a smith on reality's forge.\n\nSome transmuters are tinkerers and pranksters, turning people into toads and transforming copper into silver for fun and occasional profit. Others pursue their magical studies with deadly seriousness, seeking the power of the gods to make and destroy worlds."},
  ["feature.school-of-transmutation.phb2014.wizard.transmutation.3"]={title="School of Transmutation",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["item.scimitar.phb2014"]={title="Scimitar",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.scimitar.xphb2024"]={title="Scimitar",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["magicitem.scimitar-of-speed.dmg2014"]={title="Scimitar of Speed",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 199\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, you can make one attack with it as a bonus action on each of your turns."},
  ["magicitem.scimitar-of-speed.xdmg2024"]={title="Scimitar of Speed",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 302\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nYou gain a +2 bonus to attack rolls and damage rolls made with this magic weapon. In addition, you can make one attack with it as a XPHB on each of your turns."},
  ["creature.scion-of-grolantor.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Grolantor",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 165\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 22\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 402 (23d20 + 161)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 27 | DEX 14 | CON 25 | INT 15 | WIS 21 | CHA 18\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, paralyzed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one Great Tree Club attack and two Slam attacks, or it makes three Boulder attacks.\n\nGreat Tree Club\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h30 (4d10 + 8) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 23 Strength saving throw or be pushed horizontally up to 100 feet straight away from the scion and have the prone condition.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h26 (4d8 + 8) force damage.\n\nBoulder\n\nrw 15 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h27 (3d12 + 8) bludgeoning damage.\n\nInhale {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scion inhales a vortex of air in a 120-foot line that is 15 feet wide. Each creature in that area that is Huge or smaller must succeed on a 23 Strength saving throw or be pulled up to 120 feet straight toward the scion and be swallowed. A swallowed creature has the restrained condition, has Cover against attacks and other effects outside the scion, and takes 24 (7d6) force damage at the start of each of the scion's turns.\n\nThe scion's stomach can hold up to two creatures at a time. If the scion takes 60 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, the scion must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, each of which falls in a space within 10 feet of the scion and has the prone condition. If the scion dies, any swallowed creature no longer has the restrained condition and can escape from the corpse using 15 feet of movement, exiting with the prone condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEarth-Shaking Movement\n\nThe scion moves up to its speed and then sends a shock wave through the ground in a 60-foot-radius circle centered on itself. Each creature on the ground in that area that is concentration must succeed on a 23 Constitution saving throw or lose concentration.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nFeed\n\nImmediately after taking damage, if it has at least one creature swallowed, the scion deals 10 (3d6) force damage to each swallowed creature and regains 10 hit points."},
  ["creature.scion-of-memnor.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Memnor",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 167\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 26\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 656 (32d20 + 320)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 18 | CON 30 | INT 24 | WIS 22 | CHA 26\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe scion doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one attack using Cloud Morningstar or Wind Javelin, as well as two Slam attacks.\n\nCloud Morningstar\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h32 (4d10 + 10) force damage plus 22 (4d10) thunder damage.\n\nWind Javelin\n\nrw 18 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h42 (5d12 + 10) thunder damage, and the target must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h28 (4d8 + 10) force damage.\n\nThunderous Vortex {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scion magically creates a vortex of wind in a 60-foot-radius sphere centered on a point it can see within 120 feet of itself. Each creature in the sphere must succeed on a 24 Strength saving throw or be pulled straight toward the sphere's center, ending in an unoccupied space as close as possible to the center. Then a burst of thunder erupts in a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on the same point. Each creature in that area takes 52 (8d12) thunder damage and must succeed on a 24 Constitution saving throw or have the stunned condition until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nFog of Deception\n\nThe scion conjures a magical cloud that fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on a point it can see within 90 feet of itself. Each creature in that area must make a 24 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, a creature has the charmed condition until the end of its next turn. While it has the charmed condition, the creature must use its action to make a melee attack against a creature other than itself of the scion's choice. If no creature is within its reach, the affected creature makes a ranged attack against a creature of the scion's choice, throwing its weapon if necessary. On a successful save, a creature is immune to the scion's Fog of Deception for the next 24 hours."},
  ["creature.scion-of-skoraeus.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Skoraeus",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 23\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 444 (24d20 + 192)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 29 | DEX 20 | CON 26 | INT 19 | WIS 24 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: acid\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one Crystal Club attack and two Slam attacks, then uses Entombing Grasp if available. Alternatively, the scion makes two Runic Boulder attacks.\n\nCrystal Club\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h35 (4d12 + 9) bludgeoning damage. homThe scion can cause the club to flare with bright light, and the target must succeed on a 22 Constitution saving throw or take 18 (4d8) radiant damage and have the blinded condition until the start of the scion's next turn.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 16 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h31 (4d10 + 9) force damage.\n\nRunic Boulder\n\nrw 16 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h27 (4d8 + 9) bludgeoning damage. homThe boulder explodes. The target and each creature within 30 feet of it must make a 22 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 19 (3d12) force damage and has the prone condition. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\nEntombing Grasp {@recharge}\n\nThe scion wreathes its hand in petrifying magic and touches one Huge or smaller creature it can see within 20 feet of itself. The target must succeed on a 24 Dexterity saving throw or take 28 (8d6) force damage and have the grappled condition (escape 19). At the start of the scion's next turn, if the target is still grappled, the target has the petrified condition.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEarth-Shaking Movement\n\nThe scion moves up to its speed and then sends a shock wave through the ground in a 60-foot radius circle centered on itself. Each creature on the ground in that area that is concentration must succeed on a 24 Constitution saving throw or lose concentration."},
  ["creature.scion-of-stronmaus.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Stronmaus",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 171\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 27\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 656 (32d20 + 320)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60, fly: 80, swim: 80\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 20 | CON 30 | INT 26 | WIS 28 | CHA 24\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, fire\n\nImunidades: lightning, thunder\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, prone\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe scion doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one attack using Lightning Sword or Hailstone, as well as two Slam attacks.\n\nLightning Sword\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h36 (4d12 + 10) force damage plus 22 (4d10) lightning damage.\n\nHailstone\n\nrw 18 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h32 (4d10 + 10) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) cold damage, and the target must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h36 (4d12 + 10) force damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nVengeful Storm {@recharge}\n\nThe scion conjures a churning storm cloud in a 30-foot-radius, 10-foot-tall cylinder centered on a point within 120 feet of itself. The cloud's area is Vision and Light. The cloud lasts for 1 minute, until the scion dies, or when the scion uses this bonus action again.\n\nWhen the cloud appears, and as a bonus action on later turns, the scion can move the cloud up to 30 feet and cause one of the following effects in a 30-foot-radius, 120-foot-high cylinder directly below it; the scion can't choose the same effect two rounds in a row:\n\nAcid Rain\n\nThe cloud rains acid. Each creature in the cylinder must succeed on a 25 Constitution saving throw or be covered in acid for 1 minute or until a creature uses its action to remove the acid from itself or another creature. A creature covered in the acid takes 26 (4d12) acid damage at the start of each of its turns.\n\nFreezing Storm\n\nShards of ice pelt down, and freezing wind fills the area. Each creature in the cylinder must succeed on a 25 Dexterity saving throw or take 28 (8d6) cold damage and be hindered by ice formations for 1 minute or until it or another creature within reach of it uses an action to break away the ice. A creature hindered by ice has its speed reduced to 0.\n\nLightning Bolts\n\nBolts of lightning strike down. Each creature in the cylinder must succeed on 25 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) lightning damage and have the stunned condition until the end of its next turn."},
  ["creature.scion-of-surtur.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Surtur",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 173\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 546 (28d20 + 252)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 17 | CON 28 | INT 21 | WIS 24 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: cold, lightning\n\nImunidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one attack using Lava Blade or Lava Ball, as well as two Slam attacks.\n\nLava Blade\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h32 (4d10 + 10) slashing damage plus 18 (4d8) fire damage.\n\nLava Ball\n\nrw 18 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h29 (3d12 + 10) bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) fire damage, and the target must succeed on a 26 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 18 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h28 (4d8 + 10) force damage.\n\nLava Wave {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scion emits a wave of lava from its blade, hands, or mouth in a 90-foot cone. Each creature in that area must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 60 (11d10) fire damage and has the restrained condition from being embedded in hardening rock. A creature can make a 25 Strength (Athletics) check as an action, freeing itself or a creature within reach from the rock on a success. The rock has AC 17 and 40 hit points, and it is immune to fire, poison, and psychic damage. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEarth-Shaking Movement\n\nThe scion moves up to its speed and then sends a shock wave through the ground in a 60-foot-radius circle centered on itself. Each creature on the ground in that area that is concentration must succeed on a 26 Constitution saving throw or lose concentration.\n\nIncendiary Smoke\n\nThe scion causes smoke and white-hot embers to billow from its skin, filling a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on itself that moves with it. While the scion's skin billows smoke, ranged attacks against the scion are made with disadvantage. A creature that moves into the smoke for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must succeed on a 25 Constitution saving throw or take 14 (4d6) fire damage. The scion's skin stops billowing smoke after 1 minute, when the scion dies, or when the scion uses this bonus action to stop the smoke."},
  ["feat.scion-of-the-outer-planes.sato2014"]={title="Scion of the Outer Planes",subtitle="Feat - SatO - 2014",body="Pagina: 12\n\nYour connection to an Outer Plane infuses you with the energy there. Choose a type of plane listed in the Planar Infusion table. Your choice gives you resistance to a damage type and the ability to cast a cantrip, as specified in the table. You can cast this cantrip without material components, and your spellcasting ability for it is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma (choose when you select this feat).\n\nPlane | Damage Resistance | Cantrip\n\nChaotic Outer Plane | Poison | Minor illusion\n\nEvil Outer Plane | Necrotic | Chill touch\n\nGood Outer Plane | Radiant | Sacred flame\n\nLawful Outer Plane | Force | Guidance\n\nThe Outlands | Psychic | Mage hand"},
  ["subclass.scion-of-the-three.frhof2014.rogue.scion-of-the-three.0"]={title="Scion of the Three",subtitle="Subclasse - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 23"},
  ["feature.scion-of-the-three.frhof2014.rogue.scion-of-the-three.3"]={title="Scion of the Three",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\nBecome a Gruesome Agent of Malice\n\nA Scion of the Three draws power from a group of malevolent gods known as the Dead Three: Faerûnian, deity of tyranny; Faerûnian, deity of violence and murder; and Faerûnian, deity of death. While some Rogues of this subclass pledge themselves ardently to those three macabre gods, others find themselves thrust on this path by a curse. Either way, a scion's power manifests as various occult gifts, as well as an uncanny talent for striking and terrifying foes.\n\nScions of the Three are most common in Baldur's Gate, where the Dead Three have long competed for influence over mortal hearts. Underground cults to Faerûnian, Faerûnian, and Faerûnian often count Scions of the Three among their most useful agents. Outside Baldur's Gate, secular thieves' guilds such as the Shadow Thieves of Amn or Xanathar's guild in Waterdeep might cautiously call on a Scion of the Three to undertake an especially violent contract."},
  ["creature.scion-of-thrym.bgg2014"]={title="Scion of Thrym",subtitle="Criatura - BGG - 2014",body="Pagina: 175\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / G\n\nCR: 24\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 499 (27d20 + 216)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 60\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 16 | CON 27 | INT 17 | WIS 20 | CHA 21\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant, Primordial\n\nResistencias: fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: cold\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (6/Day)\n\nIf the scion fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe scion has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nThe scion deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scion makes one Ice Axe and two Slam attacks, or it makes two Glacier Throw attacks.\n\nIce Axe\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h36 (4d12 + 10) force damage plus 18 (4d8) cold damage.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 20 ft., one target. h32 (4d10 + 10) force damage.\n\nGlacier Throw\n\nrw 17 to hit, range 120/480 ft., one target. h36 (4d12 + 10) bludgeoning damage plus 14 (4d6) cold damage, and the target must succeed on a 25 Strength saving throw or have the prone condition.\n\nGlacial Upheaval {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scion digs its hands into the ground at a point it can see within 30 feet of itself and launches a magically conjured mass of ice into the air. Each creature other than the scion in a 30-foot-radius, 100-foot-high cylinder centered on that point must make a 25 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 36 (8d8) bludgeoning damage plus 19 (3d12) cold damage and is pushed vertically to the top of the cylinder, at which point the creature falls. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage and is pushed to the nearest unoccupied space outside the cylinder with no additional effects.\n\nAt the start of the scion's next turn, a mass of ice plummets to the ground on a point the scion can see within 60 feet of the point the scion dug its hands into. Each creature in a 30-foot-radius, 100-foot-high cylinder centered on that point must succeed on a 25 Dexterity saving throw or take 18 (4d8) bludgeoning damage plus 18 (4d8) cold damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEarth-Shaking Movement\n\nThe scion moves up to its speed and sends a shock wave through the ground in a 60-foot-radius circle centered on itself. Each creature on the ground in that area that is concentration must succeed on a 25 Constitution saving throw or lose concentration."},
  ["magicitem.scissors-of-shadow-snipping.wbtw2014"]={title="Scissors of Shadow Snipping",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nAs an action, you make a few snips with these iron shears and cause the shadow of a Humanoid creature you can see within 5 feet of you to detach from its source. If the creature is unwilling to give up its shadow, it can make a 15 Charisma saving throw, retaining its shadow on a success. Whether or not the shadow is snipped, this property of the scissors can't be used again until the next dawn.\n\nThe detached shadow is rooted to the spot where it was snipped until you use a bonus action to cause it to behave in one of the following ways, either of which is possible only if you can see the shadow:\n\n• You control the shadow's movements and can make the shadow move up to 30 feet across a solid or liquid surface, in any direction you choose (including along vertical surfaces), provided it remains within your sight at all times. The shadow is harmless and unable to be harmed, and it is invisible in darkness. It can't speak, and it doesn't require air, sleep, or nourishment.\n\n• You can relinquish control of the shadow, at which point it becomes autonomous and behaves as the DM wishes. It uses the shadow stat block in the Monster Manual, but its creature type is Fey instead of Undead. A creature whose Strength is reduced to 0 by this shadow's Strength Drain attack does not die but falls unconscious instead. The creature regains consciousness and all its Strength after finishing a short or long rest.\n\nA creature whose shadow has detached from it is cursed. If a shadowless creature is subjected to any spell that ends a curse, or if its detached shadow is reduced to 0 hit points, the detached shadow disappears, and the creature regains its normal shadow instantly."},
  ["creature.scorchbringer-guard.ggr2014"]={title="Scorchbringer Guard",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 9 | CHA 10\n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nExplosive Tank\n\nWhen the guard dies, or if it rolls a 1 when checking whether its Scorchbringer action recharges, the tank on its back explodes in a 10-foot radius sphere. Each creature in that area must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. The explosion ignites flammable objects that aren't being worn or carried, and it destroys the scorchbringer.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nLight Hammer\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) bludgeoning damage.\n\nScorchbringer {@recharge 4}\n\nThe guard's scorchbringer spouts a stream of flame in a line that is 30 feet long and 5 feet wide. Each creature in the line must make a 12 Dexterity saving throw, taking 7 (2d6) fire damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["spell.scorching-ray.phb2014"]={title="Scorching Ray",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 273\n\nYou create three rays of fire and hurl them at targets within range. You can hurl them at one target or several.\n\nMake a ranged spell attack for each ray. On a hit, the target takes 2d6 fire damage."},
  ["spell.scorching-ray.xphb2024"]={title="Scorching Ray",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 313\n\nYou hurl three fiery rays. You can hurl them at one target within range or at several. Make a ranged spell attack for each ray. On a hit, the target takes 2d6 Fire damage."},
  ["feature.scornful-rebuke.xge2024.paladin.conquest.15"]={title="Scornful Rebuke",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 37\n\nStarting at 15th level, those who dare to strike you are psychically punished for their audacity. Whenever a creature hits you with an attack, that creature takes psychic damage equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1) if you're not incapacitated."},
  ["creature.scorpion.mm2014"]={title="Scorpion",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 337\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 1 (1d4 - 1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 2 | DEX 11 | CON 8 | INT 1 | WIS 8 | CHA 2\n\nSentidos: blindsight 10 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSting\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h1 piercing damage, and the target must make a 9 Constitution saving throw, taking 4 (1d8) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.scorpion.xmm2024"]={title="Scorpion",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 369\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / T\n\nCR: 0\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 1 (1d4 - 1)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 2 | DEX 11 | CON 8 | INT 1 | WIS 8 | CHA 2\n\nSentidos: Blindsight 10 ft.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSting\n\nm 2, reach 5 ft. h1 Piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) Poison damage."},
  ["magicitem.scorpion-armor.toa2014"]={title="Scorpion Armor",subtitle="Item Magico - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nThis suit of plate armor is fashioned from giant scorpion chitin. While wearing this armor, you gain the following benefits:\n\n• The armor improves your combat readiness, granting you a +5 bonus to initiative as long as you aren't incapacitated.\n\n• The armor doesn't impose disadvantage on your Dexterity (Stealth) checks.\n\n• The armor doesn't impose disadvantage on saving throws made to resist the effects of extreme heat (see chapter 5 of the Dungeon Master's Guide).\n\nCurse\n\nThis armor is cursed. Whenever you don or doff it, you must make a 15 Constitution saving throw, taking 100 (10d10 + 45) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. Only a wish spell can remove the armor's curse."},
  ["item.scorpion-ship.aag2014"]={title="Scorpion Ship",subtitle="Item - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 42\n\nRaridade: none\n\nScorpion ships are archaic metal warships that have never lost their popularity, largely because of their versatility. Articulated legs enable a scorpion ship to land safely on the ground and move across a solid surface at a walking speed of 30 feet. The ship can't float on water, however. A ballista is mounted on the top deck, and a mangonel is perched on the end of the tail. The ship's two claws are relatively inefficient in combat, but a claw that grabs a creature can quickly take it out of action."},
  ["vehicle.scorpion-ship.aag2014"]={title="Scorpion Ship",subtitle="Veiculo - AAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 42"},
  ["magicitem.scourge-of-shadow.coa2014"]={title="Scourge of Shadow",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 275\n\nRaridade: artifact\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: Inestimavel\n\nSaid to be a gift to Glasya from Asmodeus, the Scourge of Shadow is a multi-headed whip constructed from infernal iron. The scourge is nigh-in- destructible, and Glasya carries it with her wherever she goes. When she wields the whip in battle, it shrouds her in an aura of shadow.\n\nThe Scourge of Shadow is a magic whip. You have a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this weapon, and it does 3d4 slashing damage instead of its regular damage. When you hit a good aligned creature with it, that creatures takes an extra 4d4 necrotic damage.\n\nWhenever an unattuned creature attacks with the weapon, it deals 2d4 necrotic damage, ignoring resistances and immunities, to them, but otherwise functions normally.\n\nRandom Properties\n\nThe Scourge of Shadow has the following random properties:\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\n• 1 dmg property\n\n• 2 dmg properties\n\n• 1 dmg property\n\nKeen\n\nThe whip scores a critical on a roll of 18, 19, or 20. When it scores a critical, its damage dice are upgraded to 3d6 instead of 3d4 for the duration of the attack. If attacking a good aligned creature, or attacking with the weapon unattuned, the necrotic damage dice are also increased to a d6 instead of a d4.\n\nFast Reflexes\n\nWhile attuned to the Scourge of Shadow, you gain advantage on initiative rolls, and you add your Charisma and Dexterity modifiers to the roll. You may use either your Strength, Dexterity, or Charisma modifier for the attack and damage rolls (the same modifier must be used for both attack and damage).\n\nVeil of Shadow\n\nYou're protected by a field of shadow that makes you resistant to radiant and necrotic damage. While in Vision and Light or darkness you gain blindsight out to 60 feet and Dexterity (Stealth) checks are made with advantage.\n\nDestroying the Scourge\n\nThough the process is known only to Glasya and Asmodeus, the Scourge of Shadow can be destroyed. It must be taken to the Pit of Fire in Phlegethos. The scourge, along with the body of an archdevil, must be thrown into the Hellfire together. As they hit the flames, a spell of Darkness must be cast at 9th level on the scourge. If each part of the ritual is performed correctly, the whip disintegrates within the Hellfire."},
  ["creature.scout.mm2014"]={title="Scout",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 349\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 16 (3d8 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Hearing and Sight\n\nThe scout has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scout makes two melee attacks or two ranged attacks.\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, ranged 150/600 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["subclass.scout.xge2024.rogue.scout.0"]={title="Scout",subtitle="Subclasse - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["feature.scout.xge2024.rogue.scout.3"]={title="Scout",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 47\n\nYou are skilled in stealth and surviving far from the streets of a city, allowing you to scout ahead of your companions during expeditions. Rogues who embrace this archetype are at home in the wilderness and among barbarians and rangers, and many Scouts serve as the eyes and ears of war bands. Ambusher, spy, bounty hunter—these are just a few of the roles that Scouts assume as they range the world."},
  ["creature.scout.xmm2024"]={title="Scout",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 270\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 16 (3d8 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scout makes two attacks, using Shortsword and Longbow in any combination.\n\nShortsword\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage.\n\nLongbow\n\nr 4, range 150/600 ft. h6 (1d8 + 2) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.scout-captain.xmm2024"]={title="Scout Captain",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 270\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 66 (12d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 14 | WIS 15 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus one other language\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scout makes two attacks, using Shortsword or Longbow in any combination.\n\nShortsword\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage, plus 10 (3d6) Piercing damage if the attack was made with XPHB.\n\nLongbow\n\nr 5, range 150/600 ft. h7 (1d8 + 3) Piercing damage, plus 10 (3d6) Piercing damage if the attack was made with XPHB.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAim\n\nThe scout has XPHB on the next attack roll it makes during the current turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nUncanny Dodge\n\nactTrigger The scout is hit by an attack roll. actResponse The scout halves the damage (round down) it takes from that attack."},
  ["creature.scrag.tftyp2014"]={title="Scrag",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 147\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30"},
  ["creature.scrapper.mismv12014"]={title="Scrapper",subtitle="Criatura - MisMV1 - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 126 (12d10 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 20 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages of its creator but can't speak\n\nResistencias: lightning\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nElectrified Chassis\n\nA creature that hits the scrapper with a melee attack while within 5 feet of it takes 19 (3d12) lightning damage.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scrapper makes two Spike Punch attacks. It can replace one of those with a Wires attack.\n\nSpike Punch\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) bludgeoning damage plus 5 (1d10) piercing damage.\n\nWires\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 20 ft., one Large or smaller creature. hThe target has the grappled condition (escape 16) and must succeed on a 16 Strength saving throw or be pulled into an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the scrapper and take 19 (3d12) lightning damage. The scrapper can have only one creature grappled in this way at a time.\n\nEye Beam {@recharge 5}\n\nThe scrapper shoots a magical beam from its extended eye at one creature it can see within 120 feet of itself. The target must make a 16 Dexterity saving throw, taking 44 (8d10) force damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.screaming-devilkin.mff2014"]={title="Screaming Devilkin",subtitle="Criatura - MFF - 2014",body="Pagina: 19\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / S\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 18 (4d6 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 0, fly: 40\n\nSTR 4 | DEX 16 | CON 13 | INT 5 | WIS 8 | CHA 11\n\nSentidos: darkvision 30 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAgile Flier\n\nOpportunity attacks against the screaming devilkin have disadvantage while it is flying.\n\nCeaseless Screaming\n\nAny creature other than a screaming devilkin that starts its turn within 30 feet of one or more screaming devilkins and can hear it must make a 10\n\nWisdom saving throw. On a failure the creature is incapacitated until the start of its next turn. On a success, the creature suffers no effect.\n\nStunted Legs\n\nThe screaming devilkin has disadvantage on attack rolls and all attack rolls made against it gain advantage while the devilkin isn't flying.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBarbed Tail\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.scribble.crcotn2014"]={title="Scribble",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M"},
  ["background.scribe.xphb2024"]={title="Scribe",subtitle="Background - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 184\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiency:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["magicitem.scribe-s-pen.erlw2014"]={title="Scribe's Pen",subtitle="Item Magico - ERLW - 2014",body="Pagina: 278\n\nRaridade: common\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 100 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 50 PO / 5 dias\n\nYou can use this pen to write on any surface. You decide whether the writing is visible or invisible, but the writing is always visible to a person with the Mark of Scribing.\n\nAny creature with the Mark of Scribing can use an action to touch the invisible writing, making it visible to all.\n\nIf you use the pen to write on a creature that isn't a construct, the writing fades after 7 days."},
